 "wap-command-options": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhKhmIc",
  "title": "wap gets its own command with test options",
  "updated": "2026-11-21T10:28:56Z",
  "key": "wap-command-options",
  "agent": "warp-host-fixer",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-20T17:29:40Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-21T10:28:56Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhFhgWg",
   "title": "wap gets its own command with test options",
   "body": "Original title: wap gets its own command with test options, as warp test had.\n\nUser's todo in AGENTS.md (Build and test): 'wap app with test options as before'. Today tests are bash test/wap/*.sh.\n\nAdded by warp-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312580231\n\nuser 2026-11-20: top priority now: the wap native binary, a `wap` executable as `warp` is (core/native in warp: a driver running the compiler through wasmtime's C API, built via wasm2c + cc), but running wap's compiler. Test options follow later.\n\nbranch: wap-command-options (2026-11-20)\n\nPlan 2026-11-20 (supervisor OK phase 1): native wap as wap/extensions/native/: native.wap (@primitive rules: texts as linear-memory pointers, raise via proc_exit, preload words shadowed), foreign.wap (from \"c\" imports), driver.wap (driver.warp in wap over wasmtime C API: runs wap.wasm, WASI), build.wap (wasm2c + cc). Core hooks asked at warp-interviewer: (a) raise tag only when used ~5, (b) import any module ~10, (c) data_address literal prim ~8, (d) compiler.wap args #args<2 (d5e5bea). Phase 1 = hooks + primitive hello through wasm2c; phase 2 = driver. Blocker found: every wap module is GC (text array i8 + tag), wasm2c refuses 0x5e.\n\nOK 2026-11-20 via warp-interviewer: hooks (a) tag/GC text only when used, (b) foreign import of any module, (c) data_address, (d) compiler.wap #args < 2 — user allowed all four. Phase 1: native hello via wap/extensions/native/build.sh; tests hello raise files texts lists functions modules self native green.\n\nland: wap-command-options 4dc62aa\n\nOK 2026-11-20 via warp-interviewer (phase 2): pointer = a WORD_LAYOUTS row (wap has no type alias form; interviewer: alias first, else the row), written_text takes a Char (\"c\"), data_address gives its address in the result's layout (b1fe929), ø dropped is no code. Phase 2: native wap from wap/extensions/native/driver.wap + c.wap + glue.awk; /Users/me/dev/bin/wap installed. Tests hello raise loops conditions matching functions self native green.\n\nland: wap-command-options 4e1e03b\n\nland: wap-command-options 43e5efd\n\nland: wap-command-options b976cf4\n\nland: wap-command-options 3a512d8\n\nland: wap-command-options 71c4167\n\nland: wap-command-options 806dbe6\n\nparked: build.wap in place of build.sh waits for texts in native programs (a linear-memory text layout in wap/extensions/native); today it would be strcat chains into fixed buffers, and build.sh still bootstraps the first native wap\n\nland: wap-command-options 76996a9",
   "state": "CLOSED",
