   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF2Y9Q",
   "title": "wap's reader: parsing and braceless calls",
   "body": "Original title: wap's reader: parsing and braceless calls (roadmap)\n\nThe wap counterpart of the old compiler's roadmap(s) parsing, parsing-2 … parsing-4, parser-features, parser-features-2 (user 2026-11-20). Open: sub-cards get filled as wap reaches the area; the old roadmap's cards are evidence, not spec, and each comes over only with a wiki page or sample backing it (edge cases don't count).\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312601194\n\nFixed in [0eccf82](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/0eccf8281ee0e842f2c11fe1625fe78de340ddf1): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/lib-field-types'\n\nreader-quadratic (warp-gc-snapshot, 2026-11-21): wap's reader takes quadratic time on large input: constructor-notation dumps of 20 KB read in 132 ms, 40 KB 528 ms, 80 KB 2.6 s, 336 KB 52.8 s (core/parse/reader.wap notation, newline-separated items). Suspects: list += in loops in core/parse/cascade.wap pieces_between and runs_of (a = a + b copies), and each nesting level scanning its tokens again. Details: warp notes/gc_snapshot.md.\n\ndup?: wap-printing (same, 2026-11-23)",
