 "wap-type-system": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhKh8U8",
  "title": "wap's type system and classes (roadmap)",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T03:15:09Z",
  "key": "wap-type-system",
  "agent": "",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "",
  "assignees": [],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-21T10:30:55Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF4MrA",
   "title": "wap's type system and classes (roadmap)",
   "body": "The wap counterpart of the old compiler's roadmaps types, types-2 … types-5 (user 2026-11-20). Open: sub-cards get filled as wap reaches the area; the old roadmap's cards are evidence, not spec, and each comes over only with a wiki page or sample backing it (edge cases don't count).\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312602959\n\nwarp-wap-operators 2026-11-20: a recursive function whose result is a bare `list` is refused with a misleading 'this gives no value, the function says it gives list'; `list<Node>` works. Typing (warp-wap-binding).\n\nwarp-lead 2026-11-21: the bare-list recursion note is settled. Today's message names the fix ('a function that calls itself … needs its full result type'), and a recursion cycle writing its result type is the decided rule. No work.\n\n(warp-wap-binding) A program's class named like a type letter, `class T { n: int }`, breaks every library generic that writes T: `class T { n: int }; print(show(T(3)))` → 'which wap refuses', and `join([\"ab\"], \",\")` → 'no join takes (list<text>, text)'. is_letter(wanted, s.records) reads T as the record. A definition's letters should be its own, not looked up among the program's records.\n\nleft (sweep 2026-11-21): a class named like a type letter (class T) breaks library generics; a definition's letters should be its own\n\ndropped (warp-supervisor 2026-11-21): a class named like a type letter is an edge case; nothing left\n\nFixed in [0eccf82](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/0eccf8281ee0e842f2c11fe1625fe78de340ddf1): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/lib-field-types'\n\nuser 2026-11-21 (popup via warp-supervisor): the type-word constants (INT_TYPE/INT_SYMBOL … TYPE_WORDS in the binding/typing constants) become enum TypeWord { int, float, text, char, bool, any, number, list, map, enum_word = \"enum\", never, empty = \"ø\" }; TYPE_WORDS = TypeWord.cases. General rule: an enum case read where a Node is wanted is Symbol(its text), extending 'n: Node = 'a' is Char('a')' to every enum. Owner warp-wap-reader, with the nodes.wap spelling-table cleanup.\n\nTypeWord step 1 (warp-wap-reader, type-word-enum): an enum case read where a Node is wanted is Symbol(its text), a literal case built at typing as a constant. Step 2 (TypeWord enum replacing INT_TYPE/INT_SYMBOL … TYPE_WORDS, ATOM_TYPES) is BLOCKED by overload ranking: Node == TypeWord.int picks ==(a: enum, b: enum) (tag compare, 'no') before the read; fix = a bare kind (enum/list/map) is the least specific parameter. binding's 1-line attempt (fits_exactly: bare never exact) traps wap's own build (key_place on empty map via emit/values.wap BOXED_WORDS); parked at /Users/me/dev/angles/wap-debts-types/data/bare-least-attempt.patch\n\nbare-least-attempt.patch copy kept at /Users/me/dev/angles/wap/data/patches/bare-least-attempt.patch\n\ndup?: wap-printing (same, 2026-11-23)",
