 "function-record-single": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhKh8qY",
  "title": "Each function described once by one record",
  "updated": "2026-11-20T20:22:55Z",
  "key": "function-record-single",
  "agent": "warp-wap-binding",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-20T16:45:51Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-20T18:03:04Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF4kFg",
   "title": "Each function described once by one record",
   "body": "Original title: Each function should be described once, by one record the declaration stage writes and every later stage reads\n\nPLAN (architecture step 4, warp-wap-binding; code after step 2 lands).\nRecord, written by declare (analyze/declarations.wap) for every definition, header-only ones too (export add(a: int, b: int = 1) as int, host words):\n  class Signature { name: text; definer: Node (carries its DEFINER id, the identity); parameters: list<Node> (name, written type or ø, DEFAULT fact); result: Node? (written result, so the Debt \"a written result type is not declared\" is paid); kind: function | value | case | record field; never_returns: bool; module: text; body: Define? (ø for a header) }\n  Name clash: core/type_notation.wap already has `class Signature { parameters; result }`, a function TYPE. Proposal: that one becomes `FunctionType` (lead's file; ~10 uses), the definition record takes `Signature`. Needs lead's yes.\nWhere it lives: one list on the declared program (fact DECLARATIONS holds Signatures' nodes today as `f: [a, b]`; it becomes the records, indexed by definer id in a NameIndex).\nReaders, each referencing by definer id instead of rebuilding:\n  - binding (names.wap Definition): keeps name/kind/depth for scope, drops its own copy of the shape; DEFINED_AT stays the definer node, whose id finds the Signature.\n  - typing (types.wap Function): Function IS the Signature (function_of, written_types and Function go, ~-40 lines); TypedFunction = Signature + argument types (its `function` field points at the Signature); definition_keyed/typed_from look up by id, not place_key text.\n  - modules.wap: declared_alike (text of name + types) compares Signatures by id/shape, not text.\n  - emitter (Placed, emit/functions.wap function_key): keyed by definer id + instance signature; with warp-wap-emitter, who owns Placed.\n  - the wap section of a module: the Signature list printed back (wasm-module-import resumes on it).\nKeys: place_key \"id name signature\" text (36 uses) and the 18 `key: text` fields become the definer id (text \"file#n\", already unique) plus, for typed instances, the argument types as a list, compared with same_types; no string building.\nOrder: (1) declare writes Signatures beside DECLARES, typing reads them (Function gone); (2) binding and modules read them; (3) keys by id, place_key gone; (4) emitter's Placed with warp-wap-emitter; each a landing with test/wap on wap2 and the census.\nSize: review estimates ~-60 lines net; mechanical across analyze/.\n\nbranch: function-record-single (2026-11-20)\n\nLead OK 2026-11-20: type_notation.wap's Signature becomes FunctionType, as the branch's own first commit with every use (call-sites agent); the definition record takes Signature.\n\nEmitter's needs (warp-wap-emitter 2026-11-20): (1) one key equal on the Define and every call: definer id + an instance's argument types, reachable from a call's DEFINED_AT (today defining_key text); (2) parameter types and result type or none (it makes layouts itself; replaces reading SIGNATURE); (3) never_returns optional. Locals and captures it re-keys to the bare definer id itself; defaults are lowered before emit, so not needed.\n\nUser decision 2026-11-20 (wiki/wasm-representation.md Export names, 81ada66): each overload is exported under its header line, result included: add(a: int, b: int = 1) as int; the plain name is a runtime dispatcher over Kind tags (dispatch.wap's dispatchers, joined across modules by a shared table, refusing ambiguous or result-only overloads without an expected type); the wap section keeps only rules, enums and source bodies, no export declarations. So Signature gets: header(signature) as text, printed with format's spelling (canonical words, defaults as written, result after 'as'); and a reader of an export name back into a Signature (the reader's declaration parse of one header line, then declare's signature_of), so a used .wasm is declared from its export names alone. Header text is canonical, so printing then reading gives the same Signature (a roundtrip test line).\n\nland: declared-result fcf7622820\n\nPhase 1 plan (lead OK 2026-11-20): declarations.wap class Signature {name; key; parameters: list<Node?>; result: Node?; module; shaped} built by one builder from a declaration node (declare's DECLARES, or a lifted Define's head); Module.signatures written by module_declared; Function -> Signature, no definer: TypingState.defines map key -> current Define, define_of(sig, s) refuses loudly when missing; typing seeds definitions from the modules' signatures. Debts: two records (DECLARATIONS + Signatures) until phase 2. Stage table declare row says Module.signatures. Done: f149210af6 FunctionType rename, 9b9910da7b #/! Debts.\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312603302\n\nOK 2026-11-20 via warp-lead: phase 1 approved (watch: move shaped to TypingState if phase 2 finds a second writer)\n\nland: function-record-single f2a1035a2b\n\nPhase 1 landed f2a1035a2b (wap main 6332d23). Phase 2 analysis: DECLARATIONS readers = pipeline (library_around, lowered_module's declared_rewritten, typed_by_rules scope), rules/declared.wap (stage 2 by_name), modules.wap (modules_scope, module_names, clashes, defines_identically), census (preload_scope, declaration_word). They need values and records too, not only functions: Signature gains kind (function | value | record) + the record node for a record, then the readers take Module.signatures and DECLARES/DECLARATIONS go. Worktree /Users/me/dev/angles/wap-function-record-single (branch reused, ff to main).\n\nPhase 2 OK 2026-11-20 via warp-lead: Signature gets kind: DefinitionKind; every DECLARATIONS reader takes Module.signatures; DECLARES/DECLARATIONS go. Conditions: (1) a record's Signature holds its Record node only because readers need its fields today - say so in the field's comment; (2) declared_alike compares parameter types with typing's type comparison (same_types), never text; (3) matcher by_name holds Signatures, its function/predicate holes read kind and result; rules/declared.wap must get simpler, tell warp-wap-reader (its owner). Mark Debts paid on landing: two records; declared_alike's text.\n\nOK 2026-11-20 via warp-interviewer: phase 2 approved under the semi-frozen rule (net −3 core lines); warp-lead approved 6332d23..70b516b; warp-wap-reader yes on rules/. Touched scripts 364 ✓ 0 ✗, census 56/76 files, 1294/1294 functions; self-build 29 s → 18 s\n\nland: function-record-single 44e8bfa\n\nPhases 3 and 4 dropped (warp-lead 2026-11-20): place_key is already the definer id plus the instance signature, and maps need text keys, so a structured key gains nothing; the emitter's Placed already keys that way. Writing the Signature list back into a module's wap section is a feature: only the user can ask for it.\n\nuser 2026-11-20 (to warp-supervisor): mangled export names are wanted after all: build the wiki's 'Export names' (wasm-representation.md): each overload exported under its header line, result with the arrow, add(a: int, b: int = 1) → int; the plain name a runtime dispatcher; a used .wasm declared from its export names. This revives the dropped header-text phase.\n\nExport names (user, 2026-11-20 via warp-supervisor): OK via warp-interviewer, steps 1 and 3(b), under about +15 core lines; landed size +12. The record (Signature: names, defaults) and signature_text, type_given, header_signature live in core/bindings.wap (warp-lead approved as owner); the emitter's header_line is one call to signature_text. type_given kept typing-first: a generic instance exports inc(x: int) → int; two modules writing pick(x: T) still clash. 20 scripts 0 ✗, guardrails green, census green.\n\nland: function-record-single e897ad7\n\nland: function-record-single 6df4e95",
