  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF5-Dw",
   "title": "wap's primitives should name wasm opcodes directly",
   "body": "Original title: wap's primitives should name wasm opcodes directly, from one table\n\nStep 5, emitter: a Prim names an opcodes.wap mnemonic, one host table with WASI types, special names in kernel/primitives.wap; reader changes the preload's prim spellings. Emit files only, may run beside step 1.\n\nbranch: wap-prims-mnemonics (2026-11-20)\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312604644\n\nFixed in [4547064](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/45470647b8937dcdbaadbed36914bcfd69290fb6): feature(minor): prim reads a wasm instruction by its mnemonic, its type and operation glued by a dot\n\nFollow-up (warp-interviewer 2026-11-22, text-helpers-out parked): the text helpers text_equal, text_joined, text_placed and text_written leave core/emit for loops in types/text_bytes.wap once the emitter's own callers are types words placed by typing: record and any comparisons (parts_compared, any_equality_function), the any cast's raise (checked_cast via raised_with), and main's uncaught catch (added only when typing meets a raise, so programs without raise and native ones stay small). About -42 core. Native texts stays at +9 core until then. (warp-wap-operators)",
