 "wap-result-choice": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhKh_ds",
  "title": "wap picks the wrong version of a word when…",
  "updated": "2026-11-20T18:07:12Z",
  "key": "wap-result-choice",
  "agent": "warp-wap-binding",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-20T18:04:29Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-20T18:07:12Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF74CQ",
   "title": "wap picks the wrong version of a word when…",
   "body": "Original title: wap picks the wrong version of a word when two versions differ only in what they give back\n\nhi() as int := 42; hi() as text := \"fourtytwo\"; t = hi() as int; print text(t) compiles and then raises \"int: fourtytwo is no decimal int\". wiki/conversion.md: a word with several results gives the one that is wanted. The wanted type has to take part in ranked (wap/core/analyze/calls.wap). A wrong value: first in line.\nSource: the discussion with the user on 2026-11-18 (warp-architect-review). Acceptance lines: test/wap/test_conversion.sh on branch wap-review (17a72e0ff8).\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312606171\n\nbranch: wap-result-choice (2026-11-20)\n\nAlready fixed on main (checked 2026-11-20 at 44e8bfa): chosen_definition (calls.wap:216) filters by the wanted type when several fit; test_conversion's 'a word with several results gives the one that is wanted' is ✓. Siblings probed, each right: t: int = hi() → int, hi() as text → text, a parameter x: int → int, a written result g() as int → int, text(hi()) → text (the maker T(x) is x as T); x = hi() and a bare hi() are refused naming both readings. No change needed.\n\nFixed in [cdb7039](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/cdb70390798884f386ffdf4c86a1decfc524bfb4): chore: wap, the new warp compiler, copied from pannous/warp at 9df09ce13f",
   "state": "CLOSED",
