 "wap-make-builtins": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhKh_n4",
  "title": "wap cannot turn a value into yes/no with bool(x)",
  "updated": "2026-11-20T18:10:19Z",
  "key": "wap-make-builtins",
  "agent": "",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "",
  "assignees": [],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-20T18:10:16Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF8DtA",
   "title": "wap cannot turn a value into yes/no with bool(x)",
   "body": "Original title: wap cannot turn a value into a yes/no with bool(x) or a fraction into a whole number with int(x)\n\nwiki/conversion.md \"Making\": T(x) and x as T are the same call, Python behaviour for the built-in ones. int(2.7) and 2.7 as int are 2 (today: no int takes (float)); bool(text) reads the word, bool(\"no\") and bool(\"0\") are no; bool of any other value is its test, bool([]) is no (today only bool(b: bool)). `as` becomes a rewrite to the call, no mechanism of its own.\nSource: the discussion with the user on 2026-11-18 (warp-architect-review). Acceptance lines: test/wap/test_conversion.sh on branch wap-review (17a72e0ff8).\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312606334\n\nAlready built on main (checked 2026-11-20 at 44e8bfa), in warp before the split: x as T is the rule $value as $type => $type($value) in preload/sugar/types.wap (warp 5f6b00d760), with no core path; the makers are preload functions in prelude.wap: int(x: float) truncates, bool(t: text) reads the word, bool(c: char), bool(x: T) := truthy(x) (warp fddfc60f99). test_conversion is all ✓, including its three acceptance lines. No change needed.\n\nFixed in [cdb7039](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/cdb70390798884f386ffdf4c86a1decfc524bfb4): chore: wap, the new warp compiler, copied from pannous/warp at 9df09ce13f",
