 "wasm-module-import": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhKh_w0",
  "title": "wap can use a compiled .wasm module as it uses…",
  "updated": "2026-11-22T14:33:00Z",
  "key": "wasm-module-import",
  "agent": "",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "",
  "assignees": [],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-20T20:37:19Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF8PYA",
   "title": "wap can use a compiled .wasm module as it uses…",
   "body": "Original title: wap can use a compiled .wasm module of its own as it uses the source: use \"m.wasm\" gives the same functions and signatures as use \"m.wap\"\n\nUser request 2026-11-19 via warp-supervisor. Owner: warp-wap-emitter. After class steps 3 (Module) and 4 (Function); never ahead of self-build census roots. Plan: (a) emit/ writes each export's wap Signature into a custom section (name: wap); (b) new wap/core/analyze/wasm_modules.wap, beside declarations.wap, reads types, imports, exports, the name section and that custom section into a Module of Functions; translate the structure of ~/dev/script/wasm/test_emcmake/source/wasm_reader.cpp + wasm_reader.h into clean wap (the user allowed copying from C++), only those sections; (c) use \"m.wasm\" gives a Module through it. Outcome test: wap compiles m.wap to m.wasm, a program using m.wasm gives the same result as with m.wap.\n\nFormat decided (user 2026-11-19, wiki/wasm-representation.md): names, exports, imports, class shapes and source positions come by wasm convention (name section incl. type/field names, exports = public, import module = used file, start = top-level statements, sourceMappingURL). Everything wasm erases goes into the custom section `wap` as warp declaration text, a header the normal reader + declare stage read: full signatures (param names, types, optionals, results), defaults, overload sets (export names stay plain), enum cases, class field defaults, the module's rules/operators/aliases, generic or inlinable bodies and folded constants as source, typing facts (never returns), a version stamp (compiler hash, value layout, source hash: stale refused loudly), doc comments in a strippable section. The wasm-specific reading shrinks to finding sections; translate only that part of the C++ reader.\n\nHeader line form (user 2026-11-19): `export add(a: int, b: int = 1) as int`, export + a body-less signature, so it reads as no call or cast; parsed by the normal reader. Ask warp-interviewer with the core cost before building the declaration form (it's a new form in rules/declare).\n\nparked 2026-11-19 (user: wap work only from the self-build census until wap compiles itself). branch wasm-module-import 997846b1d1: slice A done, a module exports its own top-level functions (an overload as name·2…) and writes their header lines (export f(a: int) as int) into a custom section wap (core/emit/header.wap); suite was green before the last main merge, recheck. Left: B read_notation of a .wasm reads its wap section (new analyze/wasm_modules.wap, one line in pipeline.wap), C body-less export declares an imported function (declarations + lowering), D the emitter imports it from the module's path, which the native driver already links; then the outcome test.\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312606477\n\nFrom the archived warp card import-wasm: import test/fixtures/wasm/zlib (zlibVersion, crc32) bound nothing in self-hosted warp; the fixture zlib.wasm was deleted from warp's tree.\n\nLanded: slice A, each function exported under its header line add(a: int, b: int = 1) → int (48849142d3); B+D, use \"m.wasm\" declares each export as a foreign prim of m's path, via wap/extensions/wasm/modules.wap (1f1d8ff). Missing against the 11-20 wiki: the wap custom section (the module's rules, operators and aliases; enum cases and class field defaults; generic or inlinable bodies as source; folded constants; never-returns facts; version stamp; doc comments); the plain-name Kind dispatcher (not approved); the import's module path, resolved from the compiling folder rather than the importer's.\n\nFixed in [d8ff850](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/d8ff850087883052b5cb0a8017da8a5672cfded2): feature(minor): a program uses a compiled wap module as it uses its source, use \"m.wasm\" declaring each function from its export name\n\ndup?: wasm-linker (same, 2026-11-22)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
