   "body": "Original title: wap cannot use ø as a value: 'ø is empty' and 'ø or 3' fail with 'the emitter has no value layout for the type ø'\n\nRepro (wap, test/wap/compile.sh ran): print text(ø is empty) and print text(ø or 3) refuse at prelude.wap:185/186: the emitter has no value layout for the type ø. Backed by wiki/truthiness.md; dropped from the conversion-lines landing (from branch wap-conversion-tests 6427bbcd24) until this works; re-add the checks then. Owner: warp-wap-binding (typing of a bare ø) / warp-wap-emitter.\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312606742\n\nOK 2026-11-20 via warp-interviewer: approved (a); built smaller: letters.wap unified binds a bare ø as the optional of a type its uses settle (+1 core line), confirmation of the changed shape sent. 20 touched scripts 0 ✗, census green, seed + self-build ok; test_conversion gains the bare-ø line.\n\nland: wap-value-error 93374b2",
