   "body": "Original title: wap refuses == of two enum cases that carry fields, like Circle(1) == Circle(2), where old warp compares their fields\n\ndecided 2026-11-18 by warp-wap-interviewer: follow old warp, == compares the tag then the fields; Circle(1) == Circle(2) is no, Circle(1) == Circle(1) yes. Owner warp-wap-emitter, after methods. Plan: an equality helper per enum (tag, then cast and compare each field by its own equality), plus a prelude line.\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312606877\n\nAlready fixed on main, checked 2026-11-20 at 44e8bfa by warp-wap-binding: enum Shape { Circle(r: int), Square }: Circle(1) == Circle(2) is no, Circle(1) == Circle(1) is yes.",
