   "body": "Original title: wap's error messages print a function type badly: list<(int) -> int> shows as list<(Call -> (int) int)>\n\nMoved from warp's board 2026-11-20 (wap-repo-split).\n\nAdded by warp-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=312607029\n\nStill broken at 44e8bfa (warp-wap-binding probe 2026-11-20): xs: list<(int) -> int> = [x => x + 1]; y: int = xs says 'this gives list<(Call -> (int) int)>'. Root: a function type is held as the kernel Call form, and refusals interpolate types raw (\"${given}\", fits.wap:115 and siblings); core/type_notation.wap type_text (used once) has no function or generic arm. Fix shape: type_text writes (params) -> result and name<parts> recursively, and refusals print types through it. Core (semi-frozen): interviewer first.\n\nbranch: wap-error (2026-11-20)\n\nOK 2026-11-20 via warp-interviewer: 1(a)/2(a) at about +12, no article helper; landed size +14 (a shared phrase constant). type_text writes function and generic types; 9 refusals print through it. 16 touched scripts 0 ✗, census green, seed builds.\n\nland: wap-error 7a25bca\n\nrelated: card for messages showing internal forms (wap's messages show the compiler's internal form instead of the code as written): same printer",
