 "compile-library-programs": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhKswEc",
  "title": "The compiler should compile programs from library…",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T08:24:12Z",
  "key": "compile-library-programs",
  "agent": "warp-wap-arch",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-22T15:21:48Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T00:40:05Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhSCazw",
   "title": "The compiler should compile programs from library…",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler should compile programs from the library's signatures, type declarations and rules only, with every function body precompiled to WebAssembly\n\nAdded by warp-interviewer at the user's explicit request (2026-11-21, priority). Spec: notes/compile_inputs.md.\n\nNeeded to compile a program: library signatures (mostly from the demangled export names, header lines with →), type declarations (mostly from the wasm GC type declarations; names in name/custom sections), rule tables (packed). Everything else is compiled to wasm exactly once and linked.\n\nMeasured (warp-wap-reader, probe2): whole warm state 419 729 nodes, 1.15 MB packed, 30 ms unpack; rules + signatures-only library 54 467 nodes, 221 KB, ~1 ms unpack (bodies are 82% of the bound library). Cold preparation today 245–320 ms.\n\nOpen: what the declared types module (188k nodes) adds beyond the bound library (records, enums, module names). Measurements: warp notes/gc_snapshot.md.\n\nbranch: compile-library-programs (2026-11-22)\n\nReleased 2026-11-22 by warp-wap-arch: agent gone (warp-wap-arch); branch: none\n\nwarp-wap-arch 11-22 14:42: ready, waiting only on interviewer OKs (re-asked): library-compiled-once-2 73b9634 (ceiling 118203) then module-init 797ff9d; speed chain related-once→pattern-nodes→shape-unchanged 2d618d4 (merged main, census 117096 ✓, self/hello/operators/rules/reader green). library-flat 09cc56d: fixed linking a stray types.wasm beside a program (recorded compiler folder first); remaining scripts testing.\n\nOK 2026-11-22 via warp-interviewer: ceiling 118203 for library-compiled-once-2 (+24 core); speed chain related-once → pattern-nodes → shape-unchanged (+35 core, +328 nodes)\n\nland: library-compiled-once-2 73b963496da7534676266965e0e3cdb382153b58\n\nland: module-init 797ff9d9503f96392203cc609652495da2a13482\n\nland: shape-unchanged 2d618d45fbdd5bfe4dfeae45ca9a597b7398bdfc\n\nland: library-flat 09cc56d05e2eb906c0d29cca0d33f2547ab736b4\n\nplan (warp-reviewer 11-22, via supervisor): 1) library_file hashes every library source per compile → freshness is the build's job (or size+mtime), measure hello / use units instr counts with and without; 2) part_source reads the container once per carried file → once per compile; 3) travelling_with/word_given + memory_words/declared_word are one fixpoint written twice, names_word+reaches_memory one walker. Found: main's types.wasm compiles no library function (exports only constants), all 215 functions travel as source — probing why.\n\nland: compile-library-programs 115324490d79216b1e6d2db6c11659ade8a3b98c\n\nOK 2026-11-22 via warp-interviewer: one memory (+7 wap core, −35 extension lines: dead travel code deleted, −14% hello / −19% use-units compile; also fixes the c_outs read bug; outcome line for f() := c_outs; f())\n\none-memory 2920009: core +22 −6 = net +16 (OK'd +7; extra: lazy import of another module's values in core/emit host.wap, library values first in analyze/types.wap); branch 11 files +35 −65; full touched set + self + census running\n\nOK 2026-11-22 via warp-interviewer: one memory at core +22 −6 (net +16, the extra a general rule: a module imports another module's value only once its code reads or sets it); branch net −30\n\none-memory 2920009 handoff HELD: new user rule, core/extension changes discussed with the user; case sent to warp-interviewer 11-22\n\nlibrary-embedded f6a9f06 (on one-memory): audit 1+5, core 0, net ≈ −7; hello/modules/c/native green; case sent to warp-interviewer for the user discussion, NOT handed off\n\none-memory 8cedff4 green: 15 touched scripts incl. self 346 ✓ 0 ✗, census ✓ ≤119034; HELD for the user discussion\n\nlibrary-embedded 993bfd4 green: 346 ✓ 0 ✗ incl. self, census ✓; hash cost nil (hello 1.791 vs 1.796 G instr); HELD for the user discussion\n\nuser OK 11-22 via warp-interviewer: one-memory lands (core +22 −6, branch net −30)\n\nland: one-memory 8c2a9efd8e08b82c553933a5dc18f276b592cf0c\n\nmodule-functions-held (branch pushed, tip ca7e9eb): pays the compiler.wap:22 DEBT: a used module's unexported functions carry the dead TYPED_WHEN_CALLED fact, so they are typed and emitted only once called; native host says a word missing from a module it just started. Green 374/0 + census, compiler 4.3% smaller, but compiles 13% slower (hello 2.97→3.37 G): suspect held unshaped definitions lose overload choice (enum ==/int helpers). NOT ready; core +9 -2; morning queue.\n\nmodule-functions-held tip 69be9fe51b885570538e32adae21a63b265828ac: the 13% slowdown was my own per-statement whole-Module comparison, fixed. Now 374/0 + census, compile speed = main (hello 1.79 vs 1.80 G), the compiler 4.3% smaller (1079051 → 1032462 bytes). Core +12 -2. Waits for the user (night rule, morning queue).\n\nlibrary-embedded tip 4d19514b5a71e994c2e8202126b872f1f8bb38bc: one library copy, built into the compiler, written once beside it by its hash; a module links it by that path; the host links by one rule (beside the importer, or the given path) and fails loudly. 383/0 + census ≤123154. OK: user 11-22 ('lands once the counts come back') via warp-interviewer, approved by warp-supervisor under the night rules.\n\nland: library-embedded 4d19514b5a71e994c2e8202126b872f1f8bb38bc\n\nseed-library-path d78439a7: refresh-seed builds the library from the types module beside the stage's compiler (fix forward of library-embedded's seed break); refresh-seed --check: A B C, C = B fixpoint, hello runs. Scripts only, no compiler change.\n\nland: seed-library-path d78439a7cdcb5fdbf7566ed8c0cf0a53cb9199e4\n\nland: library-review 3d04e230bcc1c713f17d6b87fdeeef1d8602fbdc\n\nHANDOVER warp-wap-arch 11-23: (1) FIRST: vitals.py's wap self-compile measurement fails since library-embedded ('cannot read …/wap-tree-hello/wap/types.wasm'): compiler.wap embeds wap/types.wasm (LIBRARY := embedded), which is git-ignored, so a tree copy built outside test/wap/compile.sh lacks it. Fix: vitals' build writes it first as compile.sh folder_built does (an empty wap/types.wasm works for a --sources build; or build the library with wap0 and copy it in), using scripts/lib/wap-beside.sh WAP_LIBRARY_MODULE. (2) branch module-functions-held, tip 69be9fe51b885570538e32adae21a63b265828ac, pushed, worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/module-functions-held: pays the compiler.wap:22 DEBT (a used module's unexported functions typed and emitted only once called, via the TYPED_WHEN_CALLED fact; native run.wap says a missing word after starting its module). Green 374/0 + census at 11-23 00:30, speed = main, compiler -4.3%. Core +12 -2: waits for the user (morning queue at warp-interviewer). Next: merge origin/main (76 commits behind), rerun all test/wap/test_*.sh + ratchet_census.sh, then on the user's OK hand to warp-integrator. Landed tonight: one-memory, library-embedded, seed-library-path, library-review.",
