  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhgj8Fw",
   "title": "native wap build should keep a plain enum case as…",
   "body": "Original title: A native wap build should keep a plain enum case as an int and accept an if that ends a function.\n\nFound by warp-fixer on keyboard-shortcuts-arrows (4e8b9b6dec): the native build boxes them, so wasm2c refuses; editing.wap uses int constants until this works, then switches to an enum.\n\nAdded by warp-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314170820\n\nbranch: native-plain-enum (2026-11-22)\n\nOK 2026-11-22 via warp-interviewer: about 8 wap core lines; in a native build a caseless enum's value is its i32 tag (values_in_memory), GC builds unchanged; then editing.wap's EDIT_* become enum Edit\n\nOK 2026-11-22 via warp-interviewer: native uncaught raise, about 5 wap core lines: under values_in_memory the text and a line end to stderr, then proc_exit(RAISED_STATUS); try/catch stays GC-only; notes/native.md updated in the branch\n\nland: native-plain-enum aa025818f9\n\nfollow-up (warp-reviewer via warp-simplifier 11-22): a native build of `print [1, 2]` fails on main, 'unexpected type form 0x4e': text(list)/show still emits a GC type despite memory lists. Belongs with the native optionals / hook-table work, beside: refuse a case with fields loudly, refuse a native optional of a memory value loudly, writing_function takes a memory text.\n\nuser OK 11-22 (arrow keys); landed on wap main 2d50e83\n\nfollow-up (warp-simplifier 11-22): a match of a text against literal arms never matches natively: core/emit/equality.wap picks by layout and a memory text is I32, so arms compare addresses. Sound fix: a literal arm tests through the == word resolved by typing, no emitter text equality; with the native-memory hook table, core → user discussion.",
