  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhhLfXA",
   "title": "The wap command shows no help",
   "body": "Original title: The wap command shows no help: wap --help, help and -h are run as code instead of listing its commands and options.\n\nUser 11-22 tried the native wap: it behaves quite differently from warp; feature parity not needed, but a help message is. Today: 'wap --help' -> 'nothing defines this name ... help', via a temp file in /var/folders. warp help lists its commands from core/commands' one table; wap should have one command table too (help, version, run, test options, repl, --memory-gb/--seconds), unknown option -> refused with the list.\n\nAdded by warp-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314207926\n\nbranch: wap-help (2026-11-22)\n\nbuilt: branch wap-help fe3451a (native suite 34 ✓); extension change, held for the user's discussion via warp-interviewer before the handoff\n\nuser OK 11-22 via warp-interviewer, with the tweak: rows name their action. Built on wap-help-action 49c7c88 (carries native-plain-enum: a native build holds no function value, so the action is an enum case); lands with native-plain-enum's OK, or fe3451a alone\n\nOK 2026-11-22 via warp-interviewer: user OK, the if-chain version fe3451a lands now; the action-table version (wap-help-action 49c7c88) waits for native-plain-enum\n\nland: wap-help fe3451a\n\nuser OK 11-22 (arrow keys); landed on wap main 2d50e83\n\nwap-version (on top of wap-help, same user ask via warp-supervisor): wap version / console start / help top show wap's version, the native build time, the compiler's commit+build time (wap.build stamp from refresh-seed)\n\nland: wap-version 403450a\n\nland: wap-version ac3f1a4",
