 "circumfix-operators": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhKunIU",
  "title": "Circumfix operators like ‖x‖ for abs are refused",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T13:55:53Z",
  "key": "circumfix-operators",
  "agent": "wap-reader",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T11:44:58Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T13:55:53Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhUJEUQ",
   "title": "Circumfix operators like ‖x‖ for abs are refused",
   "body": "lib/math.warp:1 `circumfix operator ‖ ‖ := abs` (wiki/operator.md:193–200: `‖-5‖+1` is 6; also ⌊x⌋ floor, ⌈x⌉ ceil, ⟦x⟧ round) is refused: \"wap does not lower this form yet\". Blocks 15 lib files that use lib/math.warp.\n\nPlan (approved shape, parked by warp-interviewer 2026-11-21 until native wap):\n- `circumfix operator A B := f` records the pair (operator_table.wap declaration shape, a Language map opener → closer; types/operators.wap the word `circumfix`).\n- Where an operand can start, A … B reads as Call(A, [inside]), the inside its own phrase, nesting counted when A ≠ B (operators.wap).\n- sugar/definitions.wap: `rule (circumfix operator $open $close := $f) => ($open(it) := $f(it))`.\n- A same-glyph pair with another of the glyph inside (‖ … ‖ … ‖) reads two ways: refuse with a fix-it naming brackets.\nAbout 12 core lines. Owner: warp-wap-reader.\n\nbranch: circumfix-operators (2026-11-23)\n\nland: circumfix-operators 34699a4 (pushed; patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/wap-reader/circumfix-operators.patch). Core +~30 code lines: the pair map, the declaration, closing_at in tokens_read, a used file operated first (pipeline), a sign glued after an operand's end splits (fixes x³+1 too), ⟦⟧ glyph range. Careful path pending (test_self + census by integrator). Limit: same-glyph nesting glued ‖‖x‖‖ lexes as one run.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided land 34699a4 at ~30 core (beyond the 11-21 shape's ~12: used files' operators read in the user file; a sign glued after an operand is the operator, x³+1). Known limit ‖‖x‖‖ glued.\n\nFixed in [cbd284f](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/cbd284f01f3f330ebfd45273c6214344e1734d19): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
   "state": "CLOSED",
