   "title": "lib/ini.warp drops every key before the first…",
   "body": "Original title: lib/ini.warp drops every key before the first section when its maps are untyped: parse_ini(\"top = 1\\n[db]\\nhost = x\") loses top. Body: typed again (map<text, any>) on branch ini-typed; the untyped form is a core miscompile of  aliasing a self-referencing map (decision untyped-nested-maps).\n\nAdded by warp-wap-lang with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314219256\n\nthe untyped form miscompiles section = out (a variable aliasing a self-referencing map): top-level writes go to a copy (decision untyped-nested-maps); core cause not fixed here\n\nland: ini-typed 52164e5\n\nFALSE ALARM (warp-wap-lang 2026-11-22): untyped ini keeps top-level keys on main; my probe cut the first output line with tail -4. No data loss, no core cause. ini-typed stays only as the user's ask to write the types; its test line passes either way.\n\nFixed in [4a0b5b9](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/4a0b5b9eb1a8d3697222b5c8dd8423ccae17027b): merge ini-typed: lib/ini.warp types its maps map<text, any> again, so keys before the first section are kept (card lib-ini, user 11-22) (merge ini-typed: keys before the first section are kept (board keeper 11-23: the tip 52164e5 is on main))",
