  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhhf2NQ",
   "title": "library modules do not compile under wap yet",
   "body": "Original title: Most library modules do not compile under wap yet: only 16 of 121 pass use <module>. Body: list and root causes in notes/lib_coverage.md (branch lib-coverage); lib faults fixed in batches, compiler gaps listed with one-line causes (warp-supervisor 2026-11-22).\n\nAdded by warp-wap-lang with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314228030\n\nland: lib-coverage 4447631\n\nland: lib-coverage c3f2332\n\nland: lib-coverage ac5f046\n\nbranch: library-modules-compile (2026-11-23)\n\nbranch library-modules-compile 6148a4d: os.wap, net.wap, color.wap, jpeg.wap, png.wap ported with tests (process-run merged in); next router, wagi, web\n\nland: library-modules-compile 4874b49 (contains host-port-media 0f540ce and process-run fb706c9). Red as wanted: test_jpeg.sh (if as argument, not in: wap-reader), test_color_wanted (list text: wap-binding), test_web_wanted.sh (block after arguments, () -> any handlers, used module's globals beside a C bytes binding: wap-reader, wap-binding, wap-emitter)\n\nland: library-modules-compile 3cbbc64 (supersedes 4874b49)\n\nland: library-modules-compile eb1db97 (supersedes 3cbbc64: + clustering, idna, R, time zones, cron (red: dot-call if argument), float^float, shadowed twins deleted). Parked: english, agent (rewrite rules from a used module); repl, interpret, symbolic, wasm (eval / wasm loading in the running program); powershell (sorting and summing any-valued records); memory (memory primitives not visible outside types)\n\nmarkup parked (wap-lead): needs the data argument mode (block as nodes), at the user; probe kept as its test. Reviewer: sound; follow-up nits after landing: cron Field data instead of the weekday name branch, CRON_MACROS as a map.\n\nwap-reader: if-as-argument fixed in method-if-argument (0db2121, queued). Once it lands: cron red only on its own logic (expected green, move test_cron_wanted lines to test_cron); jpeg still waits on 'x not in xs' (at the user).\n\nland: library-modules-compile af23056 (on f611524: process.wap as its owner's 949a91e, os's map without the typed global)\n\nland: library-modules-compile 6156186 (rebuilt on f3e4a25, without module-global-2; process.wap as 949a91e; os unchanged)\n\nwap-lead: () => \"A\" fits () -> any on main; wap-binding makes a block field mean () -> any. router/web stay in spec shape; recheck test_web_wanted.sh once that lands.\n\nrouter/web on dcc613a: the block after arguments reads now; red only because a block argument is typed by its value when the function has overloads (router's get beside types' map get). Repro sent to wap-binding.\n\nrouter/web on block-overload 82b2a8c4: WAGI line green; web's 7 lines red only on invalid wasm when 'use yaml' (via json) sits beside a C bytes binding (scalar_of(t: text?): any, ref vs i64). 3-line repro sent to wap-emitter. Branch web-routes-green waits for both fixes.\n\nweb: test_web_wanted.sh 8 ✓ on block-overload 82b2a8c4 + foreign-globals-first 2bdb5ac (user OK pending). Once both land: rename it to test_web.sh.\n\nwap-lead: user approved data parameters (markup becomes a library over nodes; data/probe/mk.wap is its test) and extends (feeds, earthquakes, polymarket, wikipedia): port them once wap-reader lands each.",
