 "enum-index-constant-time": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhK6zEU",
  "title": "Converting an enum case to its number builds a…",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T23:56:31Z",
  "key": "enum-index-constant-time",
  "agent": "wap-host-port-gpu",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T22:27:38Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T23:56:30Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhhj2OQ",
   "title": "Converting an enum case to its number builds a…",
   "body": "Original title: Converting an enum case to its number or back builds a list of all cases each time, which makes packing slower\n\nsugar/records.wap rule indexed: int(self) is [cases...].index_of(self) - 1 and Name(index) is [cases...]#(index+1), a fresh list per call. Measured by warp-simplifier (simplify-28, packed.wap Tag enum): warm-state pack 9.64 → 9.89 G instructions (+2.6%), hello compile 2.087 → 2.10 G (+0.7%). Fix belongs in the rule (warp-reviewer): int(self) reads the case's tag (natively a plain enum is its i32 tag), the reverse a lookup in a kept list. Sugar change: discuss with the user via warp-interviewer first. Unblocks simplify-28 (-39 nodes, branch simplify-28 bed4238).\n\nAdded by warp-simplifier with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314231877\n\nAlso from warp-reviewer: a byte that is no case (99 as Tag) now fails as a bare list index out of range; the reverse conversion should raise loudly naming the enum and the number, which packed's old 'no node has the tag N at byte M' did.\n\nparked branch: simplify-28 (reviewer's order comment added), lands once this card does\n\nbranch: enum-index-constant-time (2026-11-23)\n\nbranch enum-index-constant-time 74131157: loud reverse conversion ('9 is no Coin case'), speed neutral, test line in test_enum_page. Measured: kept-global list 3.5x faster conversions but +0.8% warm (every enum types a global) → rejected. Options A (case_tag prim +2 core, sugar after seed refresh), B (repetition counter in templates ~10-20), C (leave) sent to wap-interviewer; recommend A.\n\nland: enum-index-constant-time 4856a374 (handed to wap-integrator; reviewer sound). Card stays open for the speed part: case_tag primitive (option A) with wap-interviewer.\n\nlanded 05761746 (correctness part); card stays open for the speed part",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": {
    "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF4XjQ",
    "title": "wap's architecture changes, in the order the…"
   },
   "subIssuesSummary": {
    "total": 0,
    "completed": 0
   },
   "type": "Issue"
  },
  "left_board": "2026-11-25"
 },
