   "title": "class built by position from a named function…",
   "body": "Original title: A class built by position from a named function holds no working function\n\nclass H { f: (int) -> int }; g(a: int) as int := a + 1; h = H(g); print(h.f(1)) prints nothing; H(g, 1) with a second field gives invalid wasm (values remaining on stack in the adapter). H{f: g} and a lambda H(a => a + 1) work. Found building extensions/native/memory.wap (card native-hooks).\n\nAdded by warp-wap-lang with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314483301\n\nbranch: positional-function-field (2026-11-23)\n\nOK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer: 1 core line, emit/function_values.wap adapting_function\n\nland: fix-positional-function-field d08ee7d (careful: hello, records+functions 94 ✓, test_self ✓, census ✓ except size: main is already 123235 > ceiling 123154, branch +5 = 123240)\n\nFixed in [7cacdfe](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/7cacdfe251f8fb01c76c74646766f3700b1bec69): merge positional-function-field: a named function held by a variable becomes a function value without a closure it never takes (core: one line of emit/function_values.wap; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer; careful path)",
