   "title": "Core decides how a native build keeps values in…",
   "body": "Original title: Core decides how a native build keeps values in the memory, which belongs to the native extension\n\nDEBTs data.wap:46 and places.wap:12. One record (core/emit/memory.wap MemoryLayout) filled by extensions/native/memory.wap: literal words, layouts by type word, text bytes, field bytes, raise code. Branch native-hooks.\n\nAdded by warp-wap-lang with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314494082\n\nuser OK 11-22 via warp-interviewer (full record, native-only choices out of core). Measured: core −5 lines (+48 −52), +31 nodes (91748 → 91779); extension +24 lines, 237 nodes; total size 121285 → 121553 (+268) on its base. Census 1916 of 1916 typed alone, self 85 ✓, hello/native/guardrails/data/dynamic/records 138 ✓ (after the main merge, only the pinned any-char-equality line is red)\n\nland: native-hooks 0311610\n\nremeasured after main merge + in-place calls: core −11 lines (+43 −54), +8 nodes (93175 → 93183); extension +24 lines, 237 nodes; total 122875 → 123120 (+245, over the ceiling 122875: relocated code costs nodes). hello/native/records/guardrails green; owners tree lists both memory.wap\n\nland: native-hooks 4d9e0b4\n\ncorrection: ignore \"land: native-hooks 4d9e0b4\" (wrong hash); the tip is fc5b793\n\nland: native-hooks fc5b793\n\nreview nits (warp-reviewer 11-22, on landed 365233e): (1) core/language.wap and extensions/native/memory.wap say 'core/stage.wap MemoryLayout', the class is in core/emit/memory.wap; (2) built_by is a map keyed by \"list\"/\"record\" texts: two named fields (list_words, record_words) instead, a typo then fails at compile time",
