   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhrqPWw",
   "title": "Two test lines fail only in the cloud full suite…",
   "body": "Original title: Two test lines fail only in the cloud full suite on Linux, green on the Mac\n\nCloud suite b5e9cdb at 3d04e23: (1) test/wap/test_c.sh:26 'libm's C functions come from its own module, use m': got 3.0000000000000004 5, expected 3 5 — glibc's cbrt(27.0) is not exact; the line should use a value exact on every libm (e.g. cbrt(8.0) or a rounded print). (2) test/wap/test_modules.sh:126 and :151 ('a host calls an exported overload by its header line', 'a host calls a word's one function by its plain word'): got empty — called_export runs wasmtime --invoke with 2>/dev/null, so the cloud wasmtime's error is hidden (likely its version or -W flags). On the Mac at 4112c42 both files are green (57 ✓, 0 ✗). Not the library-embedded layout. Added by wap-integrator with todo add.\n\nAdded by wap-integrator with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314854872\n\nbranch: cloud-linux-reds (2026-11-23)\n\nthe Linux warp release ships no wap command; the cloud routine writes a wrapper (exec warp --no-window \"$@\") beside warp. warp is frozen, so the wrapper stays (supervisor 11-23)\n\nland: fix-cloud-linux-reds 9aae6b2 (tests only; c + modules 57 ✓ on Mac)\n\nFixed in [1fe4ea4](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/1fe4ea4c9cfb38a710653a086b07f1c2c9fec55b): merge cloud-linux-reds: use m checked with values every libm gives exactly; a host-export line names a missing wasmtime instead of an empty result (tests only)",
