   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhr4TNA",
   "title": "A program may overload a library word only for a…",
   "body": "Original title: A program may overload a library word only for a type it defines, so missing(x: int?) cannot change what x == ø means\n\nUser decision 2026-11-23 (via wap-interviewer), replaces open_decisions debt 3 (hygienic templates, sugar/conditions.wap:42). Example h2: missing(x: int?): bool := yes; x: int? = 3; print(x == ø) prints yes today. Decided: an overload of a library word (missing, show, text, join, next, index_of, int, print, raise, set, operators) for a type the program does not define is refused at declaration, naming the clash; text(p: Point), next(MyList), ==(Point, Point) stay hooks. Variables never hide a rule's function word: built already (names.wap:42 rule_word_meant), so the DEBT comment's local-variable example is stale. Core estimate ~+8 (interviewer's, reviewer verdict pending). Rejected: rule-file-only binding (breaks text(Point) in string interpolation).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314869795\n\nUser decision 2026-11-23 (second round, after wap-reviewer's visibility alternative): refuse the definition. A program function is refused when a library function of that name is visible in its file (preload plus used modules) and none of its parameter types names a type the program declares (looking inside list<…>, map<…>, optionals, function types; T, any, untyped x are foreign). Methods of program classes and a case's own function belong to their receiver; locals and lambdas are no definitions. Fix-it names the library word, suggests another name or a program type. round(x) := 0, round(x: float) := 0, add(a, b) are refused; function.md drops 'shadows'. Core +12 to +15 (reviewer, with overlap check) / ~+8 (lead, by name). Builder: self-build and lib/ must pass; types patches in flight can refuse helpers.\n\nbranch: own-type-overloads (2026-11-23)\n\nqueued after this card (wap-lead 11-23, from wap-wiki-a): (1) calls.wap part_typed chooses from one flat scope [definitions_named(word)] so an aliased method word sees types source + types.wasm twice → use word_scopes like word_called, 1 line; (2) a declared bare map/list (a: map) read as map<α,β>/list<α> with fresh unknowns in places.wap name_set_typed, ~7 lines\n\nCorrection 2026-11-23 (wap-reviewer): the visibility alternative was withdrawn (a rule writes the call into program code, so a library-file filter misses it). Refusal goes by name, no overlap check: ~+8 core. Generic and other-arity definitions are refused too.\n\nqueued (wap-lead 11-23, traced by wap-emitter): [[1, 2], 3] == [[1, 2], 3] overflows the stack: the ==(any, any) dispatcher's last choice is ==(a: T?, b: T?) at T=any, whose a! == b! re-enters the dispatcher; the boxed list<int> gets no generic choice. Fix in dispatch.wap: a dispatcher's fallback never an overload that dispatches again (any_equal or refuse), lists their own case. Test: check(\"lists holding lists compare item by item\", [[1, 2], 3] == [[1, 2], 3], yes)\n\nqueued, user OK 11-23 via wap-lead: (l) `x -1` with x a variable is the list [x, -1] (~3 analyze lines: a phrase headed by a non-function value is a list); (map decl) `a: map` / `a: list` read as open map<α, β> / list<α> (~7 lines, places.wap name_set_typed). Review wap-reader's analyze part of round-spaced-list when asked.\n\nwap-lead 11-23: the forms (x -1 list, open a: map/list) wait for wap-lead's go, after round-spaced-list lands, x -1 first; the == dispatch loop is a bug fix and goes on\n\nqueue (wap-lead 11-23): own-type-overloads, the == loop, x -1 and open a: map on wap-lead's go, then auto-use (card auto-use, user OK: only the unknown word + what it uses, a module with rewrite rules refused with 'write use <module>', a compiler note per word, auto-usable words not visible for own-type-overloads; pipeline.wap lines reviewed by wap-lead, extensions/warm.wap index by wap-reader)\n\n2026-11-23 interviewer: preload-only scope confirmed (lib/ modules wait for a notion of library module; consistent with auto-use); test renames 5c7309e and test_types_own drops approved as following the decision; size +21 core vs ~+8 told to the user: trim or bring the split back before landing.\n\n2026-11-23 interviewer: trimmed to +14 (10 code, 2 comment, 2 use) at b7d1838, within the user's ~+8 code-line OK; lands once test_self and census are green.\n\nland: own-type-overloads 81457d5 — preload-only scope (lib/ modules wait for a notion of a library module), +14 core, OK interviewer 2026-11-23\n\nUser decision 2026-11-23 (third round, after integrator batch reds): B. Refused: untyped or any parameters, and a definition whose calls a library definition of that name already takes, checked by unification (round(x), round(x: float), missing(x: int?) vs missing(T?), add(a, b), #(list<T>, int), fd_write redeclared). Allowed: a new combination of types (+(int, text) of wiki/operator.md, add(int, int)). ~+2 core on top of +14. test_lists.wap:141 and test_native.sh's hello are rewritten in their own commits (approved).\n\nland: own-type-overloads-b 6fb1b63 — rule (B), user 2026-11-23; +30 core awaiting interviewer size OK\n\n2026-11-23 interviewer after wap-reviewer: 6fb1b63's types_meet (a second unifier, misses subtyping/conformance) goes; the check calls typing's own relation (unified both ways or conforms, throwaway TypingState, or at the start of typing). Target ~+22 core; lands under the user's OK. Price for the user: wap's own source renamed six words to pass the rule (missing→unmatched, opened→case_opened, keys→known_keys, padded→spaced_to, key_place→first_key, write→c_write).\n\n2026-11-23: reworked onto typing's relation (STATIC_CONVERSIONS, unified, conforms) at the start of typing, ~+22 core: within the OK. round(x: int) now refused too (library round(float) takes ints by widening). Census limit carded census-declaration-typing.\n\nFixed in [cbd284f](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/cbd284f01f3f330ebfd45273c6214344e1734d19): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
