   "title": "Library files define syntax with 126 rewrite rules",
   "body": "Original title: Library files define their own syntax with 126 rewrite rules, some naming domain words in rules (storage, session) or repeating each rule twice (increase by / by:)\n\nlib/*.warp: tasks 34, storage 14, signals 11, english 10, web 9, timers 8 rules. storage.warp: 'where $store in [storage, database, local]' = domain vocabulary in rules; english.warp increase/decrease/multiply/divide each twice for 'by' and 'by:'. Per AGENTS a library needing odd syntax is rewritten in plain wap. Survey which rules plain wap replaces today. (warp-reviewer 11-23)\n\nAdded by wap-reviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314884094\n\nbranch: lib-rules-audit (2026-11-23)\n\nland: lib-rules-audit 59d55b48 — notes/lib-rules.md: ~30 rules plain wap today, ~25 copies, ~20 on five mechanisms (data, place, operator modifier, result type, clock literal). Sent to wap-wiki-lib for the port.\n\nstate: branch lib-rules-audit tip 59d55b48 pushed, handed to the integrator (queued after guarded-wap-2), not yet on main. next: once landed, todo done lib-rules-audit <landed commit>.\n\nFixed in [05761746](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/05761746db3f2845333685f33ac6611aa89e70be): merge enum-index-constant-time, lib-rules-audit: a number that is no case of an enum raises naming both (types words case_number/case_of; standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer sound); notes/lib-rules.md audits the library's rewrite rules",
