   "body": "Original title: A definition a rule writes lets a library function of the same name take its parameter's place\n\nBranch template-parameters e56e554 (wap-reader). OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer, relayed by wap-lead (decision a: LAND, core templates.wap +22/−8, stages.wap +2, language.wap +1 field). Added by wap-integrator with todo add, as the record of the OK.\n\nAdded by wap-integrator with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314886083\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided land it (core: templates.wap +22/-8, stages.wap +2, language.wap Rule.parameters), branch e56e554.\n\nFixed in [f217dce](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f217dce3e5432828c87ed917e15175019f2322b9): merge template-parameters: a definition a rule writes binds its parameters as a written one does, so a library function of the same name never takes their place (core/rules; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer; careful path)",
