   "title": "A library may widen the language only for a…",
   "body": "Original title: A library may widen the language only for a mechanism three libraries use, and nothing checks that on landing\n\nuser 11-23. Branch three-uses-rule: AGENTS.md Layers covers sugar/ and library rules, scripts/compiler-growth.sh checks it per landing. (warp-reviewer)\n\nAdded by wap-reviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314894890\n\nland: three-uses-rule dba5f4e (scripts + AGENTS/role notes only, express)\n\nuser 11-23, to warp-reviewer directly: 'We should already have the rule that a library may only add functionality to the core if it is used by at least three different libraries. Make sure that this rule is really there and that we enforce it.' The AGENTS.md wording on the branch is the reviewer's rendering of that; the user saw the summary.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user approved the AGENTS.md wording of dba5f4e (diff shown: Layers three libraries incl. sugar/ and library rules, compiler-growth.sh on express).\n\nFixed in [db3992a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/db3992aedf37ed3b3a7a4c845461b2c9294b5a81): merge three-uses-rule: a library widens the language (core, kernel, sugar/, extensions/, a library rewrite rule) only for a mechanism three different libraries use; scripts/compiler-growth.sh checks it on every landing (user 11-23, wording approved via wap-interviewer)",
