  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhsR_Ag",
   "title": "spaced round group gave its last item instead of…",
   "body": "Original title: A spaced round group (1 2) gave its last item instead of the list\n\nBranch round-spaced-list e48748c (wap-reader), core/rules/lowering.wap +8/-1: (1 2) is a list, only glued 2x multiplies; source keeps Round, format prints (1 2). Card exists only to hold the OK for landing (spec: wiki/list.md).\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided (1 2) is a list (core, this shape). Whether the value also keeps its bracket is open with wap-reviewer; land the list reading now.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314896353\n\n2026-11-23: whether a run-time value keeps its round bracket stays open: the user takes it up with wap-reviewer directly (the user: the universal Node structure should exist in the runtime and be handed around for any value; the question is where a list is forced into the slow Node form instead of the fast struct). Landing the list reading (source keeps Round) is not blocked.\n\nreviewer proposal (user 11-23 wants Nodes at run time): Node is already an ordinary wap enum (wap/nodes.wap), the compiler is a running program full of them. Missing: a literal becoming a Node. Shape: the expected type decides, one rule like int→float: n: Node = (1 2), a Node parameter, code as data → the Node (bracket and separator kept, prints (1 2)); everywhere else, any included, the fast list. Node literal emitted as packed bytes (extensions/packed.wap) + an unpack in the types module. Est. +10..20 core. node(x)/list(n) conversions as types functions.\n\nuser 11-23 correction: a Node shows exactly as it was parsed (its own bracket and separator, [1, 2] stays [1, 2], (1 2) stays (1 2)), so transform + serialize gives the parsed file back, or nearly. So show(Node) is format: ONE printer for the compiler and run time (core/format.wap today), never a second one in types. Gaps to exact: format prints no comments yet (its DEBT; they ride in Meta), and it spells out readings that spacing decided ([a -1] → [a, -1]), which is canonical, not byte-exact.\n\nFixed in [013faf9](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/013faf96b156f5eb15c7092f3c4e413e0e6e5d2a): merge round-spaced-list: values parted by blanks are a list, (1 2) is [1, 2]; a number before a word still measures, 5 m (core/rules/lowering.wap; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer; careful path)",
