   "title": "A quoted key after # on a map read the word of…",
   "body": "Original title: A quoted key after # on a map read the word of that name instead of the key\n\nBranch quoted-key 73f36e2, sugar/data.wap +2 (one rule): {count: 5, b: 2}#\"count\" is 5. spec: wiki/map.md (a key named like a word reads as m#\"count\"; # and [] always read the key, .name calls a word that takes the map).\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: settled by the map.md rule approved today; a bug fix, no user question needed.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314896536\n\nFixed in [1513a66](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/1513a663aab2507296db66499b53dd1472e9bf85): merge quoted-key: a quoted key after # reads that key, {count: 5}#\"count\" is 5, whatever map word shares its name (sugar/data.wap; spec: wiki/map.md; OK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer)",
