  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhsogsA",
   "title": "native build without GC crashes in wasm2c with…",
   "body": "Original title: A native build without GC crashes in wasm2c with 0x4e instead of naming the type it cannot lay out\n\nFound by wap-fixer, costed by wap-emitter. A function ending in if without else returns an optional (GC type); a memory build dies in wasm2c 'unexpected type form (got 0x4e)'. Shape: one check in core/emit/values.wap layout_of: in a memory build a type without memory layout (optionals, any, function values, maps, unlaid records) is refused at the user's line: 'a build keeping values in the memory has no layout for <type> yet'. ~+4 core (+2 in emit/functions.wap only if the refusal lands outside the function).\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided add the check (core, this shape); queued after the forms in flight.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314920323\n\nbranch: memory-layout-refusal (2026-11-23)\n\nLeft: the refusal names the type but not the user's line, because type nodes carry no position (no_layout has the same gap).\n\nland: memory-layout-refusal b1300f6\n\nFixed in [9986a3d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/9986a3df0626281a408f1e337bf6fd0df83762c4): merge loop-capture: a function made in a loop of the program's statements captures the variables it reads as they are then (core; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer, card loop-capture; careful path)\n\nFixed in [48c5078](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/48c5078af9209507042e6e622a0537b8075f799b): merge memory-layout-refusal: a memory build refuses a type it has no layout for, naming it (core +3; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer, card memory-layout-refusal; wap-reviewer: sound; careful path)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
