  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhtIJDw",
   "title": "wap's formatter deletes every comment",
   "body": "Original title: wap's formatter deletes every comment and blank line\n\nDEBT core/format.wap:5. The landing check 'format the files you wrote' is suspended because of it. Shape (wap-reader, slimmed by wap-reviewer): two facts per statement, leading (comment and blank lines above it, a blank run kept as one) and trailing (a same-line comment, which stays on its line, +3 in the reader; also covers end-of-file comments); blocks one item per line, a tab per depth; /* */ printed as # (one per line). Core ~20-24 in format.wap, parse/reader.wap, parse/lexemes.wap. When it lands, the landing check comes back.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build it, trailing comments included (core, this shape).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314950803\n\nbranch: format-keeps-comments (2026-11-23)\n\n2026-11-23: user decided land after the reviewer's cuts (honest size ~36-39 incl. comments). Trimmed tip 7af9a24: +28 net code in core. Test edits (4 flaw-pinning lines, 3 test_reader + test_operators.sh:100 indented blocks) approved. Land.\n\nFixed in [ac74149](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/ac74149eeeb22aff3842add57b0d0dd5f2730b39): merge format-keeps-comments: wap format keeps comments, blank lines and blocks written over lines (core +28 code lines; format keeps comments, user 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer; careful path)",
