 "auto-use": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLF08A",
  "title": "print(primes(30)) fails without use math",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T00:24:41Z",
  "key": "auto-use",
  "agent": "wap-fixer",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T21:30:10Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T00:12:24Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhtL1Pg",
   "title": "print(primes(30)) fails without use math",
   "body": "Original title: print(primes(30)) fails without use math, though use.md promises library words work unimported\n\nspec: wiki/use.md:11 (found by wap-wiki-lib on library-primes.md). Shape (wap-binding, wap-reviewer sound with two limits): an index of lib/'s top-level words → file, built with the warm state (~10 extensions/warm.wap); a name nothing defines brings in only that word (and what it uses inside its module) from the module the index names, one more binding round only then (~6 core/analyze/modules.wap, ~5 core/pipeline.wap); compiler note 'primes from lib/math.wap; write use math'; two modules defining the word refused naming both; a module with rewrite rules is never pulled in silently ('write use storage'); +3 for the limits. Must stay consistent with own-type-overloads: an auto-usable word is not 'visible in scope'. ~14 core + ~10 extension.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build it (core + extension, this shape).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314954688\n\nbranch: auto-use (2026-11-23)\n\nwap-fixer plan, branch auto-use in /Volumes/Worktrees/single-overload-value: (1) warm.wap: an index [word: files] of lib/*.wap and lib/<folder>/*.wap notation, skipping extra/ and host/, built into the warm state; (2) scope.wap's nothing-defines refusal: a word the index names in one rule-free module is marked wanted; (3) one more binding round with those modules used, plus a note 'primes from lib/math.wap; write use math'; two modules defining it, or a module with rules, refused naming them. Estimate 1-1.5 days.\n\nhandover: branch auto-use, tip 1462ea78 (merged origin/main, pushed), worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/single-overload-value. Careful checks were running → data/careful.log in that worktree. test_modules alias red is pre-existing (card module-alias-preload). Next: read careful.log; census was 134397 vs ceiling 134211 → trim or ask integrator for cap raise; write data/auto-use.patch; send line counts (core +26, extensions +15) + field_meant rule to supervisor and wap-binding; reviews by wap-binding and wap-reviewer; hand to wap-integrator, todo landing.\n\nbranch auto-use, tip a2334242 (merge of origin/main). 5ffc664b fixed the compile-speed regression: the standard library's words are read by a language of their own, warm.packed back to 339 kB, hello 2.65G vs main 2.60G; wap-reviewer: sound. Running: hello, compiler-growth, use_page/modules/use_wanted, test_self, census (log: /Volumes/Worktrees/single-overload-value/data/landing3.log). Left: SIZE_NODES raise if the census asks, hand-off to wap-integrator. Idea (reviewer nit): a cold compile could read the standard words on the first missed name instead of up front.\n\nrestart: branch auto-use, tip a2334242 pushed, tree clean. Next: rerun the landing checks on a2334242 (test_hello, compiler-growth, run.sh --wait use_page modules use_wanted, test_self, ratchet_census), raise SIZE_NODES in its own commit if the census asks, then hand the branch and patch to wap-integrator (todo landing).\n\nhanded to wap-integrator: auto-use 0648eaa0 (patch data/auto-use.patch in /Volumes/Worktrees/single-overload-value). Careful checks green except test_modules' module-alias line, red on main too (module-alias-preload). Left for the integrator: land; then remove worktrees single-overload-value, speed-a, speed-b (branches speed-a/speed-b are cowtree throwaways).\n\nland: auto-use 0648eaa0\n\nFixed in [8f8a3cd1](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/8f8a3cd16f0c6c22bfa0a1316a1d97293432e554): merge auto-use: a word only an unused standard module defines brings that module in, with a hint naming its use (core OK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer; wap-reviewer sound; careful checks green, census ceiling 135647)\n\nlanded in 8f8a3cd1. Left, unbuilt: reviewer nit, a cold compile could read the standard words on the first missed name instead of up front. Worktrees single-overload-value, speed-a, speed-b removed; branches speed-a/speed-b and the remote ones are in data/branch-cleanup/delete-landed.sh for the user.\n\nland: fix-auto-use-hint 0285f638 — standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer: sound; patch /Volumes/Worktrees/fix-auto-use-hint/data/fix-auto-use-hint.patch; test_hello green on the merge\n\nFixed in [087a8edd](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/087a8eddd6c85f40c2317a6299acf31a587824f4): merge fix-auto-use-hint: the auto-use hint names the module once (is_prime comes from math: write use math), a library path from lib/ is not doubled (standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer sound)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
