  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T16:21:54Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhtha-Q",
   "title": "Spaced items like multiply as a measure instead…",
   "body": "Original title: Spaced items like (1 x) multiply as a measure instead of forming a list; only glued 2x should multiply\n\nFrom round-spaced-list 013faf9 (wap-reviewer): core/rules/lowering.wap measured() reads exactly two items, a number and a word, as a measure, so (1 x) is 1 * x while (1 x y) is a list.\n\nUser decision 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: implicit multiplication only without a space (2x, 2m; x = 7; 2x == 14). Spaced (1 2 m), (1 x), 5 m are lists. Units get nothing special: the unit library overloads *(number: Number, unit: Unit) and the glued product uses it. The measured() special case leaves core. A warning for a spaced number-word pair is welcome but not required. Wiki pages that write spaced measures (5 m) are rewritten glued (5m) by their page workers.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314974290\n\nbranch: glued-multiplication-only (2026-11-23)\n\nland: glued-multiplication-only cf34474 (reviewer sound, with wap-integrator); wiki unit.md rewritten glued ef124b6 (interviewer OK)\n\nFixed in [f87d921](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f87d9211ddd1b62617ab837b2cc7f958150c0fe4): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
