  "column_since": "2026-11-23T11:55:00Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABht4Dyw",
   "title": "A one-letter text read from a map held as any can…",
   "body": "Original title: A one-letter text read from a map held as any can come back as the bool of an earlier call\n\nRepro: f(m: any): any := m[\"k\"]; print(text(f({k: yes}))); print(text(f({k: \"N\"}))) prints yes twice (expected N). \"NN\" and 7 are right. With wap-emitter (wap-lead 2026-11-23). Met in lib/template.wap (wiki/library-template.md).\n\nAdded by wap-wiki-lib with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314994802\n\nland: any-runtime-bugs 8641e12 (wap-emitter). core/emit/values.wap: a plain value's item array is its type word's own wasm type (one recursion group with the boxes), so map<text, bool> and map<text, char> held as any are told apart. Careful path green but the known any-char-equality red; size ceiling +60 in its own commit.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided land any-runtime-bugs 8641e12 (core emit/values.wap +11/-4, +60 nodes). Repro rerun today: yes, yes (expected yes, N).\n\nFixed in [41334d4](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/41334d4dd2c15e93a0aa97413a55d1b36c4d83ef): merge any-runtime-bugs: a plain value's item array gets its own wasm type, so an any map's one-letter text is no earlier call's bool (core/emit/values.wap; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer, card any-map-value-confused; careful path)",
