 "host-random": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLGcrU",
  "title": "wap has no source of randomness, so random and…",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T17:05:14Z",
  "key": "host-random",
  "agent": "wap-emitter",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T16:32:25Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T17:02:29Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABht4zCQ",
   "title": "wap has no source of randomness, so random and…",
   "body": "Original title: wap has no source of randomness, so random and uuid cannot be written in lib\n\nNothing in wap/ gives entropy; one host word (random_bytes(n) or random_below(n)) makes lib/random.wap and lib/uuid.wap plain wap (wiki/random.md, wiki/library-uuid.md). Told wap-lead 2026-11-23.\n\nAdded by wap-wiki-lib with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314995381\n\ndup?: random-bytes (same, 2026-11-23)\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build it: +1 core/emit/host.wap random_get (as clock_time_get); types ~5 random_bytes(n: int): list<int>; lib plain wap random_below(n) without modulo bias, uuid(), rest of random.md (shape by wap-emitter, probed on wasmtime). User addition: defense in depth, a few lines: random_get's bytes are XORed with a second independent input (clock_time_get nanoseconds, mixed through a hash so each byte depends on all of it), so a host with a weak random_get does not make the output reconstructable. XOR with an independent input never lowers entropy.\n\nUser addition 2026-11-23: also a fast variant: a seeded pseudo-random generator in plain wap (lib, e.g. splitmix64/xoshiro), reproducible from a seed you pass, seeded from random_bytes when none is given. 0 core.\n\nSibling OK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build sleep too: +1 core/emit/host.wap poll_oneoff; types +1 prim, sleep_ms(ms: int) ~6 lines (one monotonic clock subscription over scratch memory); lib sleep(t) for durations; retry backoff stops spinning. Probed 500 ms: warp 0.52 s, native 0.51 s, wasmtime 0.59 s.\n\nbranch: host-random (2026-11-23)\n\nland: host-random 10a4cb1. Left for lib: random_below without modulo bias, uuid(), the shared generator seeded from random_bytes, sleep(t) for durations, lib/functions.wap's spin → sleep_ms\n\nFixed in [9986a3d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/9986a3df0626281a408f1e337bf6fd0df83762c4): merge loop-capture: a function made in a loop of the program's statements captures the variables it reads as they are then (core; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer, card loop-capture; careful path)\n\nFixed in [12558fc](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/12558fcce971daa635035e6d4d154dea2bf8619a): merge host-random: random_bytes and sleep_ms over WASI, answered by the native build too (core +1; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer, card host-random; wap-reviewer: sound; careful path)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": {
    "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF4XjQ",
