   "body": "Original title: An error deep in library code shows its reason only at a types.wasm line, not at the user's own call\n\nFound by wap-wiki-lib in lib/matrix.wap, costed by wap-binding: the refusal chain ends at the user's call without the reason. Shape: the chain's last line, at the user's call, repeats the root reason with where it came from. ~2 core lines in core/errors.wap.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided repeat the root reason (core, this shape).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315002059\n\n2026-11-23: branch root-reason 4a3b372 (wap-binding): the repeat only where the chain starts in a library function ('; first: <root reason with its place>'), program roots already print their own line; ~7 core (errors.wap calling_refused, calls.wap function_typed) against ~2 told: accepted by the interviewer as the same OK (small absolute overrun, no pinned test changed).\n\nFixed in [cbd284f](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/cbd284f01f3f330ebfd45273c6214344e1734d19): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
