   "title": "A library's alias lines are refused",
   "body": "Original title: A library's alias lines (alias ArrayDeque => Deque) are refused\n\nDebt core/parse/operators.wap:33. Blocks lib collections, sorted, ring, disjoint, slugs (wap-fixer). Shape (wap-reader): the operator stage takes a file's alias lines out first and adds their rows to the table words resolve by; rows reach the module and the files that use it (as a module's rules do); format and errors print the canonical word. ~6-8 core in parse/operators.wap, operator_table.wap; binding unchanged. Not the type alias of wiki/alias.md.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build it (core, this shape).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315032311\n\nbranch: alias-lines (2026-11-23)\n\nReleased 2026-11-23 by wap-reader: waits for wap-binding's open a: map form (one form at a time); wap-lead gives the go; nothing built yet\n\nFixed in [bd6646a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/bd6646aa11f2b6e1adc79ca4e4d650f59947d77e): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
