 "lazy-arguments": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLHA4I",
  "title": "Arguments to a word that wants code are evaluated…",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T21:37:12Z",
  "key": "lazy-arguments",
  "agent": "wap-binding",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T15:20:43Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T21:37:12Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhug5aQ",
   "title": "Arguments to a word that wants code are evaluated…",
   "body": "Original title: Arguments to a word that wants code are evaluated at once unless written as a block, and a field typed block cannot be called\n\nspec: wiki/task.md, wiki/async.md, wiki/block.md (wap-wiki-lib; costed by wap-binding).\n(1) Lazy arguments: where every declaration of the word wants code, any argument other than a lambda or a bare name is wrapped as a parameterless function (go f(3), log_debug expensive(), check(c, message: \"…${expensive()}\")); beside an overload taking a value nothing is wrapped (declaration-level gate). ~1-2 core lines in core/rules/lowering.wap (the twice { 4 } rule without its curly-only condition). block.md: '… where code is wanted' gains 'or any expression'.\n(2) A field typed bare block or function is callable: type_notation.wap reads bare block as () -> any, ~1-2 lines; emitter side to be probed. class Button { on_click: block }; Button(on_click: { print \"hi\" }).on_click() prints hi.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build both (core, these shapes).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315032450\n\nbranch: lazy-arguments (2026-11-23)\n\nwap-binding: costed together with named-events as one binding mechanism (written parameter type decides: phrase as written, () -> any deferred), ~18 core lines; waits for the user's OK, nothing built\n\n2026-11-23: built through the general argument-mode mechanism of card named-events (user OK ~18 core there).\n\nland: lazy-arguments 6683927 (sound; part (2), a callable block field, came with block-field 11cca94)\n\nA literal given where code is wanted, `both 3`, is deferred too, as a function giving 3: intended, the general rule (wap-reader asked).\n\nFixed in [66839279](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/668392793c6292a03144bb104c88cd57e57f57ed): feature(minor): any expression given where every declaration wants code runs by the call, go f(3) as go { f(3) } (user OK, card lazy-arguments)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
