   "title": "Front-end bugs: is <type> called the conversion…",
   "body": "Original title: Front-end bugs: is <type> called the conversion, and assigning to ø or a literal was not refused\n\nBranch front-bugs 73fcbc6 (wap-reader). matcher.wap +2: a name that is a type (type word or declared class/record) after is is a type test; layout.wap +2 and a sugar rule: [] as list<text>; lowering.wap: one general 'no place to assign' (a place that is no name, variable, part or item); plus ~2 lines so a typed place's name that a rule rewrites standing alone (ø/nothing, yes, break) is no name: nothing: list<text> = [\"a\"] is refused (the example the user was shown). #{1 2 3} dropped. Test rename bc33e45 approved.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user picked x is <type>, no place to assign, [] as list<text>; dropped #{…}.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315096510\n\nFixed in [dae7b2a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/dae7b2ae79444fa3d2ccddd12b02143f4d7e0841): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
