   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhvypow",
   "title": "A one-character quoted literal is a char, so…",
   "body": "Original title: A one-character quoted literal is a char, so [\"x\", \"n\"] and [\"x\", \"no\"] get different types\n\nParked by the user 2026-11-23. Root (wap-reviewer): atoms.wap:126 'one character is a Char', pinned by wiki/char.md:19; a spelling with two readings by length. Symptoms: f([\"x\", \"n\"]) with overloads f(list<text>)/f(list<int>) refused as list<char>; graphs page prints ['b']. Options: (a) a double-quoted literal is always text, 'x' is a char, ~-2 core plus source fixes; (b) keep the rule, hint from the one candidate matching the literal's kind (refining calls.wap:45), +4 to +6. Rejected: list<char> fits list<text> (hidden copy).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315106584\n\n2026-11-23: wap-reader's branch char-show dd96982 (show a run-time one-character text as 'x', per char.md:19; reds test_lists.wap:126, test_data.wap:57) is held by the interviewer: it extends the length rule the user parked here. Decide together with this card.\n\n2026-11-23 wap-lead: bites again in json/yaml: g(x: any) := x is text; g(\"a\") → no (Footguns.md:180 says a char is a text); to_json([\"a\"]) writes [a]. Red line test_json.wap 'a text of one character written' (wiki-samples 9174f4c).\n\nbranch: one-char-literal (2026-11-23)\n\nwap-binding: call part on branch one-char-literal ce280a1 (+2 net, calls.wap results_written answers for literals, generic takers block a hint), test_char_page green, at wap-reviewer. Run-time part (boxed char passes 'is text', narrowing converts) sent to wap-emitter. char-show dd96982 untouched.\n\nFixed in [bcd5a55](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/bcd5a55bf165638d980871fe4b6904519265367f): Merge commit 'f83d0ff' into HEAD",
