   "body": "Original title: A main-level global x = … cannot be changed by a function of the same file, though variable.md says it can\n\nspec: wiki/variable.md:72; found by wap-wiki-lib (library-functions.md memoize example, red line). Shape (wap-binding): core/analyze/variables.wap ~3: a main-level Set written with global marks its variable declared; in a function of the same file a plain x = … / x += … writes it. Undeclared main-level variables and other files keep today's refusal.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build it (core, this shape).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315110366\n\nFixed in [dae7b2a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/dae7b2ae79444fa3d2ccddd12b02143f4d7e0841): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
