  "column_since": "2026-11-23T14:48:32Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhwWanw",
   "title": "function type written as a result is refused",
   "body": "Original title: A function type written as a function's result, memo(f: (int) -> int): (int) -> int, is refused\n\nFrom wap-lead (wap-wiki-lib, lib/functions.wap memoize). Error: this function's body gives another type than its signature says: (Call -> (int) int). Test: memo(f: (int) -> int): (int) -> int := f; check(\"a function type as a written result\", memo(x => x + 1)(2), 3). Owner wap-reader.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315141940\n\nbranch: function-type-result (2026-11-23)\n\nNot the head's parsing. A one-expression body works: h(n: int): (int) -> int := x => x + n. The written result's type does not flow into a block's last value: h(n: int): (int) -> int := { x => x + n } fails (emit/functions.wap:50), and so does an untyped g = x => x + n then g. Typing the lambda by the wanted result is core/analyze (wap-binding). Typed g: (int) -> int = … works.\n\nReleased 2026-11-23 by wap-reader: not reader: the wanted result type does not reach a block's last value (core/analyze, wap-binding); evidence in the note\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided land it (2 core lines, analyze/function_values.wap).\n\nFixed in [bd6646a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/bd6646aa11f2b6e1adc79ca4e4d650f59947d77e): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
   "state": "CLOSED",
