  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhweaTw",
   "title": "lambda whose body gives no value is refused where…",
   "body": "Original title: A lambda whose body gives no value, like i => print(i), is refused where a function is wanted\n\nOK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer: a λ whose body gives no value (i => print(i), i => xs.add(i)) fits a function type, giving ø and taking the wanted result. ~3-5 core: core/analyze/letters.wap function_value_bound binds it as giving ø (an any holds ø, -> R settles R as any), and its instance is emitted with the wanted result (where a λ's Define takes its result). The raise-only λ stays declined. Shape and cost by wap-binding. Test: each(n: int, item: (int) -> any) := { for i in 0 upto n { item(i) } }; xs: list<int> = []; check(\"a lambda adding to a list fits an any-result parameter\", (each(2, i => xs.add(i)); #xs), 2). Owner wap-binding, queued by wap-lead under the one-form-at-a-time rule.\n\nAdded by wap-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315149786\n\nmerged from the duplicate card 'A callback whose body gives no value (i => print(i)) fits no function parameter' (board keeper 11-23): from wap-wiki-lib (lib each), costed by wap-binding; -> R settles R as any (~1 core/analyze/letters.wap), instance emitted with the wanted result (~2-4 where a λ's Define takes its result), ~3-5 core. Workaround today: i => { xs.add(i); i }. OK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build it; the raise-bodied λ stays declined.\n\nbranch: resultless-lambda (2026-11-23)\n\nland: resultless-lambda 84fb1478. Built already by 78ad2552 (function_value_bound gives a resultless function ø); this branch adds the card's test line to test_functions_calls.wap (green). i => print(i) runs too.\n\nFixed in [980e03b2](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/980e03b21fd86612e8c94a76eec8b7dabb3db64a): merge resultless-lambda: a lambda giving nothing fits a function parameter, pinned by a test line (tests)",
