   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhy91SQ",
   "title": "function made in a loop sees the loop's last value",
   "body": "Original title: A function made in a loop at program level sees the loop's last value ([2, 2] instead of [0, 1])\n\nWrong values (wap-binding probe): for i in 0..3 { fs.add(n => n + i) } gives [2, 2]; Footguns' while … { x=i; f(y):=x+y; x=100; r+=f(0) } gives 300 instead of 6. Inside a function it works. Shape: a function made in a loop captures the variables that loop sets as they are when it is made. ~6 core (scope/variables).\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided fix it, high priority.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315314413\n\nbranch: loop-capture (2026-11-23)\n\nland: loop-capture b8fde93 (handed to wap-integrator). The Footguns while example with a named f(y):=x+y inside the loop is now refused (a named function reading the variables around it: not yet) instead of giving 300; a λ in the loop works\n\nFixed in [9986a3d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/9986a3df0626281a408f1e337bf6fd0df83762c4): merge loop-capture: a function made in a loop of the program's statements captures the variables it reads as they are then (core; OK 2026-11-23 user via wap-interviewer, card loop-capture; careful path)",
