  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhy-H2g",
   "title": "library word named as a value is refused even…",
   "body": "Original title: A library word named as a value (g := floor) is refused even when it has one overload\n\nspec: wiki/lambda.md (function floor), charged.md. Shape (wap-lead): 1 sugar rule for 'function floor'; ~2-3 core in bind: a library word named as a value with no expected type takes its single overload; several are refused naming them. Replaces the old 'bare g := floor refused' note when one overload.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided build it.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315314779\n\nwap-binding: the overload-by-parameter-type gap (hmac(k, m, sha1)) is built on branch shared-parameter-hint (pushed): an argument is typed as the parameter every definition of the call's count shares there; ~5 net core lines in calls.wap, parked to go with this card\n\nwap-binding: user 2026-11-23: shared-parameter-hint stays parked, not landed (hash writes HashAlgorithm.sha1); branch pushed as is\n\nbranch: single-overload-value (2026-11-23)\n\nland: single-overload-value 0b6d4899. One sugar rule (calls.wap: rule function $name: Symbol => $name). The bind part already holds on main: g := floor and f = floor give floor, abs with two overloads is refused. No core lines needed. test_lambda_wanted line 4 is green.\n\nwap-reviewer: sound. Follow-up: the several-overloads refusal's fix-it says `f: (int) -> text = abs` (a made-up type); it should show the overload actually wanted, `abs as (int) -> int`, the general mechanism for picking one.\n\nFixed in [67b5dc13](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/67b5dc1354fbd151e89440181fe4cd67dfaf040a): Merge origin/main: bare-kind-narrows, block-overload (standing OK, wap-reviewer sound), single-overload-value (one sugar rule, spec wiki/lambda.md, user OK on its card, wap-reviewer sound)",
