   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhzcFjA",
   "title": "block written inline as an argument cannot change…",
   "body": "Original title: A block written inline as an argument (twice { c += 1 }) cannot change the variables around it without global\n\nUser decision 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: a block written directly as an argument (twice { c += 1 }, each xs { total += it }) changes the surrounding variables without global, like a loop body; only a block stored with := follows the function rule (global for a variable changed later). Consequence of 'blocks read names like functions' (charged.md §3), which stays for stored blocks. Core cost to be measured (wap-binding); block.md's 'global c' line reverts to 'c = 0'.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315347421\n\nwap-binding cost: today twice { c += 1 } is refused in both places ('this could change the Global/Local c or make a new variable'), no wrong value. (1) At the program's top: ~3 core lines on top of named-events' 18. A block written as the argument is bound so its writes reach the writer's variables, as a loop body's do (variables.wap assigned_variables skips a name the writer has, scope.wap marks the block); those are globals, which a λ already writes. (2) Inside a function: the writer's local must be shared with the λ by reference: a cell per local an inline block writes, made and read through in both functions, ~20-25 core lines, mostly the emitter. Until then it is refused there as today. It does not change the 18's design: the deferred argument stays a λ made where binding sees the call; inline-ness (a block written in the call) is one more fact at that same place.\n\nbranch: inline-block-free (2026-11-23)\n\nWIP branch inline-block-free (/Volumes/Worktrees/analyze-split): lowering marks a block written as a call's argument with fact IN_PLACE (stage.wap); scope.wap binds such an Fn in place at the program's depth (handler_bound, as a Try handler), so its writes reach the program's variables like a loop body's. Inside a function it stays the closure rule (refused) until locals get cells. Probes: twice { c += 1 } → 2, each [1,2,3] { total += it } → 6, bump := {count += 1} stays refused.\n\nlanded-to-integrator dcbbb265. Left: inside a function the block still can't write that function's locals (cells, ~20–25 lines, mostly emitter). Found while pinning a stored block: (1) handlers + [handler] with handlers: list<block> refused, no + takes (list<function>, list<fn λ>), a fits gap; (2) &idle of a nullary function idle := { 0 } is called, not referenced, against wiki/function.md:127.\n\nland: inline-block-free dcbbb265\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: a block passed to a block parameter (whenever x > 5 { n += 1 }, on Key.escape { count += 1 }) writes outer variables directly, like a loop body; this covers the inside-a-function case too (cells for locals, ~20-25 core lines).",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": null,
   "subIssuesSummary": {
    "total": 0,
    "completed": 0
   },
   "type": "Issue"
  },
  "left_board": "2026-11-25"
 },
