   "body": "Original title: The samples are still named .warp, though they are wap programs: rename all of them to .wap and let the ones wap can't run yet show red\n\nUser 2026-11-23 (via wap-interviewer): rename all .warp samples to .wap; what native wap can't handle stays red until it can. A plain git mv of every samples/**/*.warp (the samples repo, /Users/me/dev/angles/samples, shared with warp), plus the path references to renamed files (imports, READMEs). No rewriting to make them pass, no skipping beyond the headless list until --no-window lands. wap's scripts/coverage.sh finds *.wap. warp's scripts (samples.sh, samples-web.sh, sample-assets.sh, bee-full.sh, browser-dry-run.sh) glob *.warp: warp runs .wap fine, so their glob takes both or they lose the samples.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315452448\n\nbranch: samples-wap-extension (2026-11-23)\n\nland: samples-wap-extension e8510009e5 (warp repo; wap side 3b4d6a8 landed on main, samples repo ee5e828 pushed; README names wait for the user's review)",
