  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh1I-9w",
   "title": "wap has none of the C pieces the native host port…",
   "body": "Original title: wap has none of the C pieces the native host port needs: structs by value, u32 and owned text, the driver hook and C header constants\n\nUser 2026-11-23 (via wap-interviewer): copy all of warp's native host (/Users/me/dev/angles/warp/lib/host/native_host*, 3427 lines over SDL3/wgpu/CoreText/AudioToolbox/WKWebView) into wap, so wap has its own native host. Port it straight: copy warp's code and translate, don't redesign. The extension lines the port needs are pre-approved. Every run is headless (--no-window; until it lands, no run of a window, gpu or sound program at all). The port lives in wap's lib/host/native_host/, same file layout as warp's. A form wap can't read yet goes to wap-lead, never a workaround.\nThis card: the extension pieces (extensions/c, extensions/native, types/c.wap): struct by value (bytes<N>), u32/int/owned_text, the driver hook that answers host words from the wap library, and C header constants (SDLK_*, CF_UTF8, ...; the general mechanism if it's under 50 lines, else hand-written constants), plus native_host.warp and platform.warp (66 lines). The other three port cards build on it.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315453428\n\nbranch: host-port-extensions (2026-11-23)\n\nland: host-port-extensions c246e10 (step 1: u32, owned_text, C imports resolved at first call). Next: struct by value as bytes<N>, the driver hook, header constants as enums, native_host.warp + platform.warp.\n\nland: host-port-extensions 685c8f8 (step 2: a C struct of more than 16 bytes by value on ARM64; reviewer sound)\n\nFixed in [2adfc83](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/2adfc83babab7d655d47c2d326573d27aa564354): Merge block-colon: a block-taking rule's word takes what follows its colon as its block (core +12; user OK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer; spec: wiki/for.md)\n\ndup?: host-port-window (same, 2026-11-25)",
