  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh1JU8g",
   "title": "wap's native host has no window, drawing or text…",
   "body": "Original title: wap's native host has no window, drawing or text rendering: port warp's window.warp\n\nUser 2026-11-23 (via wap-interviewer): copy all of warp's native host (/Users/me/dev/angles/warp/lib/host/native_host*, 3427 lines over SDL3/wgpu/CoreText/AudioToolbox/WKWebView) into wap, so wap has its own native host. Port it straight: copy warp's code and translate, don't redesign. The extension lines the port needs are pre-approved. Every run is headless (--no-window; until it lands, no run of a window, gpu or sound program at all). The port lives in wap's lib/host/native_host/, same file layout as warp's. A form wap can't read yet goes to wap-lead, never a workaround.\nThis card: native_host/window.warp (443 lines, SDL3 + CoreText: canvas, paint, text, input, frames).\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315453816\n\n2026-11-23 wap-lead (from wap-emitter/review): bindings write wap's canonical C words: i32 i64 f32 f64 u32 bool handle text texts bytes out length owned_text ø; not warp's int/long/double/string/pointer, never float for a C float (f32). Struct by value: info: bytes<40> (not bytes40), coming in host-port-extensions step 2. Uncallable C functions no longer stop linking (c246e10). Compiler gaps → wap-lead.\n\nbranch: host-port-window (2026-11-23)\n\nc1123d5: window.wap, platform.wap, root native_host.wap, lib/native/SDL3.wap ported (compiles with stand-ins, never run). Typed host words per wap-emitter's hook shape; each part its own uses; window ↔ gpu by use \"gpu.wap\". Red until: windowless()/muted() as wap words (os.warp env reads removed), exit(code) in types (wap-emitter), the bare-return guard bug (wap-binding), int[n] (test_array_wanted), the driver hook, gpu.wap (host-port-gpu), sound/webview (host-port-media). Branch includes the unlanded host-port-extensions merge.\n\nland: host-port-window c1123d5 (express: test_hello ✓, compiler-growth ✓; land after host-port-extensions, which it contains)\n\nland: host-port-window 521ed94 (review fixes: Window instance, key table, raised failures; test_hello ✓, compiler-growth ✓ on abbab9e merge + one platform commit; after wap-reviewer's sound)\n\nFixed in [403723d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/403723ddc0e6d4a1da6a976a0f43a097050b0d55): Merge origin/main: i31-opcodes (exact numbers, user OK via wap-interviewer), list-pattern-rest (user OK ~5-6 via wap-interviewer), host-port-window (port rule: sound), standing-OK small fixes range-end-once, letter-number-equal, dispatcher-place, enum-case-name, resultless-return, unknown-word; struct-words, library-exit, lib-cleanup-2\n\ndup?: host-port-gpu (same, 2026-11-25)\n\ndup?: host-port-media (same, 2026-11-25)\n\ndup?: host-port-extensions (same, 2026-11-25)",
