   "title": "wap's native host has no GPU passes",
   "body": "Original title: wap's native host has no GPU passes: port warp's gpu.warp\n\nUser 2026-11-23 (via wap-interviewer): copy all of warp's native host (/Users/me/dev/angles/warp/lib/host/native_host*, 3427 lines over SDL3/wgpu/CoreText/AudioToolbox/WKWebView) into wap, so wap has its own native host. Port it straight: copy warp's code and translate, don't redesign. The extension lines the port needs are pre-approved. Every run is headless (--no-window; until it lands, no run of a window, gpu or sound program at all). The port lives in wap's lib/host/native_host/, same file layout as warp's. A form wap can't read yet goes to wap-lead, never a workaround.\nThis card: native_host/gpu.warp (2204 lines, wgpu), the bulk.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315454114\n\n2026-11-23 wap-lead (from wap-emitter/review): bindings write wap's canonical C words: i32 i64 f32 f64 u32 bool handle text texts bytes out length owned_text ø; not warp's int/long/double/string/pointer, never float for a C float (f32). Struct by value: info: bytes<40> (not bytes40), coming in host-port-extensions step 2. Uncallable C functions no longer stop linking (c246e10). Compiler gaps → wap-lead.\n\nbranch: host-port-gpu (2026-11-23)\n\ngpu.warp → lib/host/native_host/gpu.wap, translated and typed, compiles behind probe stubs (compile only, nothing run). Based on host-port-extensions: lands after it. Still red, each owned elsewhere: guard { return } before a final assignment refused (wap-binding, 7 functions), memcpy cells<i32> (wap-emitter after the driver hook), GPU lists (warp extensions/gpu_lists, none in wap), system_value from the driver, os's slow (units-chain), names of native_host's other parts (host-port-window). Details: notes/native.md.\n\nland: host-port-gpu d06d451\n\nland: host-port-gpu f4babb7 (window state as window.<field>, host_value)\n\nland: host-port-gpu c8d8b0c (contains host-port-media; after host-port-extensions)\n\nland: host-port-gpu 550b010 (on host-port-window, no media)\n\ndup?: host-port-window (same, 2026-11-25)",
