 "shell-to-wap-scripts": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLNePM",
  "title": "wap's own scripts are still shell scripts:…",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T23:56:27Z",
  "key": "shell-to-wap-scripts",
  "agent": "wap-wiki-lib",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T21:12:05Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T23:56:27Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh1LZAg",
   "title": "wap's own scripts are still shell scripts:…",
   "body": "Original title: wap's own scripts are still shell scripts: rewrite them in wap as soon as wap can run them\n\nUser 2026-11-23 (via wap-interviewer): 'Replace all shell scripts with wap scripts as soon as it works, hopefully very soon.' Today: 32 scripts in scripts/ and test/wap/, 2021 lines. A script moves when wap has what it needs (process start, exit status, files, environment-free options, time caps); start with the smallest and the ones without job-slot or tmux plumbing; the bootstrap ones (test_hello.sh, compile.sh, refresh-seed.sh) go last, since they must run before a wap exists. Each port keeps the script's outcome identical and replaces it in one commit; what wap lacks goes to wap-lead.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315455731\n\nbranch: shell-to-wap-scripts (2026-11-23)\n\nOrder (wap-wiki-lib, 2026-11-23), smallest self-contained first, each port one commit, outcome identical:\n1. test scripts that only run wap on a program and compare its output: test_interpolation, test_warning_wanted, cli, test_apps, test_terminal, test_cli_wanted, test_cli, test_tasks, test_raise, test_files, format_checks, test_records, test_types, test_rules, test_reader, test_operators, test_functions, test_c, test_modules, test_native, test_guarded.\n2. tool scripts over git and files: repeated-code, compiler-growth, coverage, ratchet_census, test_self, test_guardrails.\n3. bootstrap, last: scripts/lib/{wap-host,platform,slots,wap-beside}.sh, guarded, job-slot, test/wap/compile.sh, run.sh, test_hello, refresh-seed.\nBlocker for all of tier 1 onward: wap has no process start. Needed from lib/os.wap (wap-host-port-window ports os): run(argv) giving stdout, stderr and exit status (posix_spawnp + pipes + waitpid over C; texts already crosses as char*[]), a working folder for the child, a time cap (guarded/timeout), later lockf and nice for job slots. Asked wap-lead 2026-11-23.\n\nprocess-run fb706c9 (on 0253cb1) handed to integrator: lib/process.wap run(words, folder:, seconds:) over posix_spawnp; next: tier-1 test script ports\n\nland: shell-to-wap-scripts 1d48115 (after library-modules-compile 0253cb1, supersedes process-run): run.sh runs test/wap/test_<area>.wap scripts; 8 in wap. Left tier 1: files, records, types, rules, reader, operators (format_checks.sh), functions, c, modules, native, guarded; then tier 2/3\n\nqueued from wap-lead (after this card): 1) after uniscript-case lands, regenerate unicode_data.wap at Unicode 17.0 (gen-unicode-tables.py), then delete lib/case_table.warp and case_tables.warp; 2) port lib/reals and hyperreal onto lib/exact.wap, typed, without any\n\nparked: the assert default-parameter fold lands with the next seed refresh (the seed's language lowers the types module and refuses a default there; wap-binding traced it)\n\nFixed in [038e9d9](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/038e9d967facb4641a68d659280ce19e82c033f4): test: test_functions is a wap script, with the shell script's outcomes; scripted.wap's grepped, matches_of and spaced stand for grep, grep -o and tr\n\nreopened: 14 tier-1 scripts landed (dcc613a); left: reader, operators (+format_checks.sh), c, modules, native, guarded; tier 2 tools; tier 3 bootstrap\n\nland: shell-to-wap-scripts-2 8e117d0f (c, reader, operators, modules; format_checks.sh gone). Left tier 1: native (needs run's stdin: wap repl is fed a line), guarded (tests scripts/guarded.sh, goes with it in tier 2)\n\nlanded 2-batch ae6eabb7. land: shell-to-wap-scripts-3 61f2e1e5 (run's input:). test_native → tier 3 (native build + pty). Tier 2 naming question with wap-interviewer (CLAUDE.md names the tools); next: guarded.sh + test_guarded, test_guardrails\n\nland: shell-to-wap-scripts-4 1f775b8e (process start/exited/waited/stop; os, png, jpeg_wanted, web_wanted). Parked: guarded-wap (exit 137 refused by wasmtime, seed lib lacks start: asked wap-lead). Left: test_guardrails, test_native/test_hello (tier 3), tier-2 tools (naming question with interviewer)\n\nguarded-wap 46d21163 complete, parked: waits for the user's 124 (wap-lead recommended) and a seed refresh after shell-to-wap-scripts-4 lands\n\nland: shell-to-wap-scripts-5 b50d967e (test_guardrails in wap; review by wap-emitter). Left: tier-2 tools (naming question at the interviewer), guarded-wap parked (124 + seed refresh), test_native/test_hello with tier 3\n\nguarded-wap rebased onto main after the seed refresh as branch guarded-wap-2 (0e679354; test_guarded 5 ✓); handoff waits only for the user's yes on a runaway's status 124 (wasm exits below 126)\n\nFixed in [c6dcd663](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/c6dcd66360d2dd87c3190599ffe0b37d4bfd8e20): merge shell-to-wap-scripts-5: test_guardrails as a wap script, its 16 rules line for line (tests, notes)",
