   "body": "Original title: wap's types read and write a 64-bit int in memory by one pair of functions instead of three spellings\n\nbranch simplify-38: memory_int/set_memory_int moved from types/c.wap to types/host.wap; clock_nanos and sleep_ms use them (-25)\n\nAdded by wap-simplifier with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315483781\n\nbranch: simplify-38 (2026-11-23)\n\nland: simplify-38 279831f (warp-reviewer OK)\n\nFixed in [2adfc83](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/2adfc83babab7d655d47c2d326573d27aa564354): Merge block-colon: a block-taking rule's word takes what follows its colon as its block (core +12; user OK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer; spec: wiki/for.md)",
