 "host-port-gpu-lists": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLOOJU",
  "title": "wap has no GPU lists, so the ported gpu host…",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T21:11:29Z",
  "key": "host-port-gpu-lists",
  "agent": "wap-host-port-gpu",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T18:31:33Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T21:11:29Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh19xZQ",
   "title": "wap has no GPU lists, so the ported gpu host…",
   "body": "Original title: wap has no GPU lists, so the ported gpu host can't hand a list to the GPU: port warp's extensions/gpu_lists\n\nPart of the native host port (user 2026-11-23: copy warp's code, our own native host; extension lines pre-approved for what the port needs). warp: /Users/me/dev/angles/warp/extensions/gpu_lists (415 lines). Goes to wap/extensions/gpu_lists, by the port rule (notes/agents/worker.md): copy the functionality, not warp's slop. Found by host-port-gpu (red 3).\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315504789\n\nbranch: host-port-gpu-lists (2026-11-23)\n\nSupervisor OK 2026-11-23: built as plain wap in gpu.wap, 0 compiler lines, not as wap/extensions/gpu_lists: typed-width lists hold their cells and cells<T> hands them to C packed; the cell type comes from the shader's array element; f16/bf16 packing as two functions; view_order_into goes with lib/splats.wap's port.\n\nPlain wap, no extension (supervisor agreed): with the user's typed-width lists a list<f32>/list<i32> already holds its cells, and cells<T> hands it to C, so warp's separate GPU list kind (BigInt limbs, staging room, declaration pass, refused list words) has nothing left to do. A storage array's numbers cross as cells of the element its shader declares (f32, i32, u32, f16 two to a word); lib/bits gives f16/bf16 through one IEEE narrowing. view_order_into (splat depth sort) belongs to lib/splats.wap's port. land: host-port-gpu-lists 68db2ff (after host-port-gpu)\n\nland: host-port-gpu-lists bc335f6 (after host-port-gpu; reviewer: sound)\n\nland: host-port-gpu-lists 5ee7d1d (merged origin/main; reviewer sound at bc335f6, merge only since). is list<any> kept: bare is list narrows to an unusable bare list (sent to wap-lead)",
