   "title": "YAML's reader moves its place and rewrites its…",
   "body": "Original title: YAML's reader moves its place and rewrites its rows in place instead of returning the new position\n\nFrom wap-reviewer's lib cleanup review (2026-11-23). lib/yaml.wap: has_row advances r.at as a side effect; sequence_of overwrites r.rows[r.at] to read an item's content as its own row. Wanted: reader functions that return their value and the new position. Also on this card: the delimiter texts (flow_value's ends, SPECIAL_STARTS) are searched with contains on a text; make them lists of chars. Owner: wap-wiki-lib.\n\nAdded by wap-wiki-lib with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315508180\n\nbranch: yaml-reader-values (2026-11-23)\n\nland: yaml-reader-values 0c03435 (reviewer: sound), after lib-cleanup-2\n\nclosed too early by the integrator: 0c03435 is in batch f1e2fe1, testing, not on main yet",
