   "title": "A function can take a braced block verbatim",
   "body": "Original title: A function can take a braced block in another language (a shader, SQL, HTML) as verbatim text\n\nUser OK via wap-lead 2026-11-23: a parameter typed raw takes a braced block verbatim (wiki/dsl.md Raw block). Reader keeps the block as text; the shader library (holes, fragment wrapping) follows in the gpu port.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315514074\n\nbranch: raw-block (2026-11-23)\n\nbranch raw-block tip 9b2bec1: careful path green (self 78, census ceiling 131927, growth OK), reviewer sound, wap-binding sound on shapes.wap line; perf +1% hello. Waiting for user's re-approval at ~41 core (wap-lead → interviewer) before handoff.\n\nUser OK at ~41 core, relayed by wap-lead 2026-11-23 (\"the user approved raw at ~41\"); now ~38. Handed to the integrator: land raw-block a8c2b6d.\n\nFixed in [c595392b](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/c595392be3fec1948df5363a4d5e2a895a3d5433): Merge origin/main: raw-block (raw parameter blocks, user OK ~41 core 2026-11-23, spec wiki/dsl.md; characters.wap split from texts.wap), commaless-map, comprehension-order, field-in-lambda (standing OK, wap-reviewer sound)",
