 "graphics-libraries-port": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLPE0w",
  "title": "The drawing libraries don't load under wap",
  "updated": "2026-11-23T23:05:22Z",
  "key": "graphics-libraries-port",
  "agent": "wap-host-port-gpu",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T21:12:04Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T22:08:31Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh229ig",
   "title": "The drawing libraries don't load under wap",
   "body": "Original title: The drawing libraries (draw, image, color, splats, meshlets, pga_draw, forest, graphics, frames, display) don't load under wap\n\nPart of the user's 'copy all the old warp code' (2026-11-23), split off library-modules-compile (wap-host-port-window keeps the rest of lib/). These libraries sit on the native host port (window, gpu), so the gpu port's worker ports them: straight from warp's lib/, under the port rule in notes/agents/worker.md; compile-only, never run (coverage.sh --runnable skips them anyway). Includes splats' view_order_into (left out of host-port-gpu-lists).\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315560780\n\nbranch: graphics-libraries-port (2026-11-23)\n\nplan (wap-host-port-gpu): first commit renames gpu.wap's host_gpu_* words to the library's names (gpu_render, gpu_show, gpu_picture, gpu_fields, gpu_pass_recorded, …), as media named sound_played; then each lib file a .wap beside its deps, its 'from host' declarations replaced by use \"host/native_host/gpu.wap\" / window.wap; color, frames, display first (no host), then draw, image, shaders, splats (+view_order_into from warp's extensions/gpu_lists), meshlets, forest, pga_draw. Compile-only via a calls harness. Starts once host-port-gpu or host-port-gpu-lists lands.\n\ncolor, jpeg, png already ported by library-modules-compile (4874b49): build image/draw on lib/color.wap's Color and Picture {width, height, pixels: list<Color>}. gpu.wap's own class Picture {width, height, pixels: list<int>} clashes: gpu.wap takes color.wap's Picture (a Color is its argb int) once both landed.\n\nlib/scene.warp (3d) added by wap-lead: ported after gpu.wap, with the others\n\nwhen wap-binding's bare-is narrowing lands (is list → list<any>, is map → map<any, any>): gpu.wap's 10 kind tests become is list / is map (version at host-port-gpu-lists data/probe/gpu_bare_is.wap)\n\nheadless paint parked (user: skip --no-window). When it returns (wap-lead's pick): paint without a window writes ./paint.png, then paint-2.png …, printing 'painted ./paint.png': painting_written(pixels, w, h) := { paintings_written += 1; path = './paint' + (if paintings_written == 1 then '' else '-' + paintings_written) + '.png'; write_bytes(path, png_bytes(Picture(w, h, pixels.map(p => Color(p))))); print('painted ' + path) } in lib/host/native_host/paint.wap\n\nprogress e28b747a: ported draw, image, display, splats, frames, shown_frames, pga (+test_pga_page), pga_draw, scene (+test_scene), gpu_passes. Red: frames on the lambda/library-global emitter crash (fix: foreign-globals-first 2bdb5ac, awaiting OK); pga_draw on aliases leaking across modules (pga's segment vs draw's segment; per-file aliases awaiting the user). In flight: meshlets+forest, shaders (needs function reflection f.params/body/calls/reads, option A with wap-lead → interviewer).\n\nFixed in [ff11149d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/ff11149d9ff00826843a2501bd4e3b685eb2d9d1): refactor: shaders runs a block's leading statements through one word\n\nland: graphics-libraries-port ff11149d (handed to wap-integrator; queued after e568fc51)\n\nland: graphics-libraries-port d8e12da5 (review fixes in). Follow-up when reflection lands: shaders.wap value_width/painted_value as overloads per type (wap-reviewer), reflected f typed function.\n\nbranch graphics-libraries-port tip e4655472 (pushed; merged origin/main, gpu.wap adapted to main's bits.wap: both_bits gone → &, Cell.F16 qualified; splats.wap uses ByteOrder.little). test_hello 0 ✗; area tests pga_page/scene/meshlets/forest were still running at restart. Next: confirm area tests green, refresh patch in ~/Library/Logs/warp/graphics-libraries-port/, hand tip to wap-integrator (note: main's own gpu.wap has the same bits break, fixed by this landing). Reds waiting on others: frames (emitter foreign-globals-first 2bdb5ac), pga_draw (alias scoping, wap-reader), shaders entry words (function reflection option A).",
   "state": "CLOSED",
