 "rule-word-guard": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLPLMA",
  "title": "rule's where takes only one word",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T17:22:42Z",
  "key": "rule-word-guard",
  "agent": "wap-fixer",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T20:39:29Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-23T21:37:17Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh29V3A",
   "title": "rule's where takes only one word",
   "body": "Original title: A rewrite rule's where takes only one word, so it can't say which words a hole may be\n\nwap/core/rules/stages.wap:81 takes a guard only as `where <word>` (last word). lib/storage.warp and lib/markup.warp (warp) use `where $x in [a, b] and $y is unbound`. In wap, `rule ($word $head := $body) where $word in [global, public, const, def] => …` is not guarded at all and rewrites every `<word> f := …`, export included (it turned test_native red in batch-f1e2fe1). Uses: wap/sugar/definitions.wap (global/public/def/const := rules), lib/storage (port), lib/markup (port). Until then definitions.wap keeps four rules.\n\nAdded by wap-wiki with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315567296\n\nAlso: a guard the engine can't read (`where` followed by more than one word) must be refused with a fix-it, not silently dropped so the rule matches everything. stages.wap:81 now drops it whenever the last word is not `where <word>`.\n\nbranch: rule-word-guard (2026-11-23)\n\nplan (supervisor): step 1, standing OK small fix: a where guard the engine can't read (more than one word) is refused loudly with the rule's line, never silently ignored. Step 2, a guard of several words ($x in [a, b] and $y is unbound) is a new form: to wap-interviewer with its core line count and uses definitions.wap, storage, markup; then definitions.wap's four rules become one. Owner review: wap-reader.\n\nstep 1 done: branch rule-word-guard 7d8f773, refusal at stages.wap:82 (+1 line, standing OK small fix); test_hello, compiler-growth, test_rules green. Step 2 (multi-word guard) at wap-interviewer.\n\nland: rule-word-guard 7d8f773 (wap-reader: sound; handed to wap-integrator)\n\nwap-reviewer: sound (sent to integrator). The ports of lib/markup.warp, lib/storage.warp and lib/timers.warp (`where $x in [...]`, `$x is symbol`, `is unbound`) meet the refusal and stay red until step 2: a guard that is an expression over the holes.\n\nFixed in [7d8f773c](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/7d8f773ccdae22c3d7f5423d307fde597e2bc5f6): fix: a rule's where guard of more than one word is refused, never dropped so the rule fires everywhere (standing OK small fix)\n\nwhen this lands: add 'class X is P {…}' as an alias of the claim 'class X: P {…}' (user asked 2026-11-24, see theory-statements-effects).",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
