   "title": "lib/cron.wap compares a field's name to find the…",
   "body": "Original title: lib/cron.wap compares a field's name to find the day of the week, and spells its macros as a list\n\nwap-reviewer's nits on library-modules-compile: the day-of-week case becomes data on Field (no name compare); CRON_MACROS becomes a map. Plus test_cron_wanted's lines that go green once method-if-argument (0db2121) lands move to the page file.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315669230\n\nbranch: cron-field-data (2026-11-23)\n\nland: cron-field-data 6ff5dc5d (hello + cron 15 ✓)\n\nland: cron-field-data bdc51715 (5-7 works; hello + cron 16 ✓; replaces 6ff5dc5d)\n\nFixed in [b3292025](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/b32920258e7cab6e6ad16cc935b4a5faa4f84fcf): merge cron-field-data: cron's day of week reads 0-7, 7 as 0 in the field's data, so 5-7 works; test_cron green (lib, tests)",
