  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh5KmIw",
   "title": "wap's regular expressions are slow:…",
   "body": "Original title: wap's regular expressions are slow: test_guardrails takes 19 s in wap where grep took 3.4 s\n\nlib/regex.wap runs patterns by backtracking over a list of chars per call (program_of compiles the pattern again on every first_match/find_all). test/wap/test_guardrails.wap calls it over every line of wap's source per rule. Seen by wap-emitter's review of shell-to-wap-scripts-5. Likely wins: compile a pattern once and reuse it; a literal-prefix skip; a DFA for patterns without groups.\n\nAdded by wap-wiki-lib with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315706345\n\nbranch: wap-regular (2026-11-23)\n\nland: wap-regular d92266a1 — regex compiles each pattern once and skips starts its first step can't take; test_guardrails 53 s → 30 s. Left as further wins: decode the text once per line rather than per call, and a DFA for patterns without groups.",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
