  "column_since": "2026-11-23T22:55:03Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh5LWvw",
   "title": "list comprehension with three for clauses runs…",
   "body": "Original title: A list comprehension with three or more for clauses runs its first two loops in swapped order.\n\nReported by wap-lead: [[a, b, c] for a in 0 .. 2 for b in 0 .. 2 for c in 0 .. 2] runs b outermost. The cause is in wap/sugar/loops.wap: since 'in' is an operator, the head's $others... sits inside the second clause, so a third clause makes $value... take the first one. Fix: the head ends in one rest. Branch comprehension-order.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315707316\n\nbranch: comprehension-order (2026-11-23)\n\nland: comprehension-order 05fee512; standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer sound; hello, rules, keyword_page, loops green\n\nFixed in [c595392b](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/c595392be3fec1948df5363a4d5e2a895a3d5433): Merge origin/main: raw-block (raw parameter blocks, user OK ~41 core 2026-11-23, spec wiki/dsl.md; characters.wap split from texts.wap), commaless-map, comprehension-order, field-in-lambda (standing OK, wap-reviewer sound)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
