   "title": "wap has no exact π, square roots or hyperreals",
   "body": "Original title: wap has no exact π, square roots or hyperreals: port lib/reals.warp and lib/hyperreal.warp onto lib/exact.wap\n\nPort warp's lib/reals.warp (π, τ, √n kept exact, their sums) and lib/hyperreal.warp onto lib/exact.wap, typed, without any (wap-lead's queue, supervisor 2026-11-23, user's copy-all-of-warp rule: warp's functionality, wap's shape, red rather than ugly). Move the hex.md and numerator/denominator wanted lines if they go green.\n\nAdded by wap-wiki-lib with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315708725\n\nbranch: exact-reals (2026-11-23)\n\nLeft open: whether π (and √ of an int) in types become exact (the interviewer was asked: A = types' π is the Real, B = keep exact_pi). lib/exact_values.warp (the exact x and x as exact rules) stays for card exact-numbers. The wanted lines numerator(6/8) and denominator(-1/3) need exact literals, so exact-numbers too; hex.md's are unrelated.\n\nFixed in [64ee32a8](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/64ee32a8e782625bd7cfa8d211d5df7bb888e186): chore: the int-side overload blocks point at card library-widening (wap-reviewer)",
