 "wap-message-display": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhK6drM",
  "title": "wap's messages show internal form instead of code…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T09:15:16Z",
  "key": "wap-message-display",
  "agent": "",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T07:01:33Z",
  "assignees": [],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T09:15:15Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhhNtLQ",
   "title": "wap's messages show internal form instead of code…",
   "body": "Original title: wap's messages show the compiler's internal form instead of the code as written. Body: every refusal ends with a kernel node like (Call radius x1) or (Set x \"ab\"); the fix is general and in one place: the message printer (errors.wap quoted) shows a node in source spelling, the warp format printer (warp-interviewer 2026-11-22).\n\nAdded by warp-wap-lang with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314209971\n\nexample 11-22: no twice takes (int): twice(b: (Call -> () int)) … define twice(a: int) to take them: (Call twice (Block 4)): the suffix and a function type both print as internal forms\n\nboard keeper 11-23: retyping-warning's slice landed (af432a7 merge retype-message); this card holds the general message printer\n\nExample (wap-reader 2026-11-24): n = 5; for x in n { print x } gives 'no # takes (int): …eight overloads… define #(a: int) to take them: (Call # held·1893)': the for rule's internals (#, held·1893) instead of 'for cannot walk an int'.\n\nbranch: wap-message-display (2026-11-24)\n\nBranch wap-message-display (pushed), +8 net core lines in errors.wap/pipeline.wap: source_of keeps each text the reader read (sources_read: file → text); quoted shows the trimmed line at the code's position, the compiler's form only for code read from no file. Probe: `for x in n { print x }` and `print(Q(\"abcd\").x)` instead of (Call # held·1893) / (Call Q \"abcd\"). Tests collections, matching_lists, functions*, cli_wanted, hello: no new reds (collections and functions_wanted as on main, cli_wanted's 7 wanted CLI features). Waits: user's core OK asked via wap-interviewer (A recommended; B a kernel-form printer ~40+ lines; C leave). Left on the card: the fix-it text itself still names rule internals (define #(a: int) for a for over an int).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: +8 errors.wap/pipeline.wap: refusals quote the source line (option A). Land.\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-enum-index-constant-time: owner session wap-enum-index-constant-time retired (restarted into native-maps 09:11); state: see earlier notes/branch wap-message-display\n\nFixed in [c2d84a75](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/c2d84a7554b997aaa59a7081f7d0516927622c84): merge wap-message-display: a refusal quotes the source line the reader read, the compiler's form only for code read from no file (user OK 2026-11-24, core +8)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": []
   },
   "parent": null,
   "subIssuesSummary": {
    "total": 0,
    "completed": 0
   },
   "type": "Issue"
  },
  "left_board": "2026-11-26"
