  "column_since": "2026-11-24T07:06:54Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhhUOzw",
   "title": "every session, script and role file uses wap",
   "body": "Original title: At the next fleet restart every session, script and role file uses wap names instead of warp.\n\nUser 11-22: 'in the next restart, when we spawn the fleet, we should call everyone wap'. Sessions wap-<role>/wap-<card>; notes/agents/start.sh, ~/dev/bin/urgent-card-watch (SUPERVISOR_TMUX, GATEKEEPER_TMUX, warp-urgent), integrator-watch, todo's <repo>-* agent naming; role files (notes/agents/*.md) move to the wap repo and sessions start in /Users/me/dev/angles/wap. Prepare before the restart, switch at it. Supervisor note: warp notes/agents/supervisor.md.\n\nAdded by warp-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314215904\n\ninterviewer.md and handbook.md name scripts/lib/sync-main.sh, which wap lacks (warp-only); replace with the plain fetch + rebase line or port the script\n\nboard keeper 11-23: the fleet restart named the sessions wap-*, role files are in wap's notes/agents/ and urgent-card-watch tells wap-supervisor; left: warp-gatekeeper and warp-urgent still carry warp names (urgent-card-watch lines 10, 23)\n\nChecked 11-24: left only warp-gatekeeper (live tmux session since 11-22, guards pannous/warp issues; named in ~/dev/bin/urgent-card-watch:10, gatekeeper-start:5,8, gate-ticket, claude-remote.sh comment) and warp-urgent (urgent-card-watch:23, comments). Renaming is the restart-time switch: gatekeeper-start, urgent-card-watch GATEKEEPER_TMUX/URGENT_CLOUD_AGENT and the live session together, and only if the gatekeeper is to guard wap at all (it scans the warp repo). Supervisor's call; nothing changed.\n\nwarp-gatekeeper and warp-urgent are warp's sessions, not wap's (wap-supervisor 11-24): left alone. Done for wap.\n\nFixed in [b77057ee](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/b77057ee2b7813a07f7d90e201670c74520cc025): fix: handbook and interviewer name the real sync command; scripts/lib/sync-main.sh never existed in wap",
   "state": "CLOSED",
