 "op-spelled-once": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhK6544",
  "title": "Each operator's spelling is written twice, in the…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T08:34:20Z",
  "key": "op-spelled-once",
  "agent": "wap-simplifier",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T21:25:06Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T08:31:10Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhhqw3g",
   "title": "Each operator's spelling is written twice, in the…",
   "body": "Original title: Each operator's spelling is written twice, in the Op enum and in the operators table; it should be written once.\n\nFrom warp-simplifier 11-22 (DEBT in wap/nodes.wap, now payable: old warp no longer reads wap source). 63 cases / 216 nodes; code names only Colon x76, None x48, Assign x3, Add x2, Define x2. Options: (a) rename cases after the table rows (little gain); (b) Key.op becomes the text spelling (-216 nodes max, text compares on hot paths: measure first); (c, supervisor) one declaration: each enum case carries its spelling (Op { Colon \":\" … }) and types/operators.wap reads it, so cases stay ints on hot paths. Core change: user discussion first. Low priority.\n\nAdded by warp-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314238862\n\nUser 2026-11-23: OK for the reviewer's slim shape (Op keeps only structural cases : . := = -> None; every other operator rides as its spelling through Other and the table; ~-55 to -60 core) on two conditions: (1) no slowdown, so measure the self-build compile time before and after; (2) users can still define operators, and a user-defined operator is a table row like a built-in one. Check first that no old-warp script still reads nodes.wap.\n\nbranch: op-spelled-once (2026-11-23)\n\nstate (restart): branch op-spelled-once tip 46dc27dc, pushed; merge with main 2026-11-23 done. Shrink -222 nodes (nodes.wap 1769 → 1547). Self-build 19.9 → 19.3 s CPU, wap1 compiling wap/compiler.wap, 3 runs each. wap-reviewer agreed shape (b): Op keeps : . := = -> None Other. The 3 test lines (test_nodes 13 and 19, test_types 82) are in their own commit 9b65f8c3, for the interviewer's morning list. Before the merge, the area tests, test_self and the census were green (test_packed é red is main's, wap-binding has it). Next: data/careful.sh in the worktree (careful checks on the merge; output data/careful.txt), then set SIZE_NODES to the merged total (the provisional 133317 is main's), ask wap-reviewer for sound, hand off to wap-integrator. Also held: simplify-39 (worktree simplify-38, i64.load/store, -2 nodes, awaiting batch/review).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-23 (core): shrink Op to the structural cases (: . := = -> None), every other operator rides as its spelling plus its table row; Op.Add's 2 uses go through the table. Estimate -55 to -60 core lines, no enum-from-list rule. Check first that scripts/wap-census.warp still reads nodes.wap.\n\nsimplifier state: simplify-40 (tip 47ea0fe0, pushed, -223 nodes, reviewer sound) handed to wap-integrator [9a6a90] for landing; worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/simplify-40 to remove after it lands. Next: simplify-41 from the remaining candidates (equality opcode table, items_fitted layout helper, all_cases, parse/ and matching.wap sweep).\n\nreview a504663f (merged with main): sound. nodes.wap -11, nothing in the repo uses a removed Op case any more (PatchOp in json_tools is unrelated), size -222, self-build not slower. Landing waits on the user's grant for the 3 rewritten test lines (9b65f8c3). The user's comment at wap/nodes.wap:23 still cites Op.Add, which is gone; it stays untouched and goes to the user's list.\n\nstate: tip a504663f pushed, merged main a4fdd08a; -222 nodes (135084 → 134862); self-build 19.1 → 18.4 s CPU (6 runs each); careful green (hello, 298/298 area, test_self, census 2196/2196); wap-reviewer sound. Waiting on the user's grant of the 3 test lines 9b65f8c3 and the stale user comment nodes.wap:22 (both on the interviewer's list), then land: op-spelled-once a504663f\n\ntest edits 9b65f8c3 approved by the interviewer (user decision 'Shrink Op'); land: op-spelled-once a504663f, merge message names the decision\n\nFixed in [e5ed7091](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/e5ed7091ef1a1300da4e61ba092a442c3cde3b84): chore: open decisions: Op from the table and templates shaped as their text have the user's core OK (cards op-spelled-once, template-shape)\n\nlanded as fdbb3372 (the 'fixed in' hash was a premature close)\n\nFixed in [271c4f0a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/271c4f0ad392dcd5aa802501cf36c67ee37e8158): test: the size ceiling is the measured 134830, keeping op-spelled-once's shrink",
