   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABht4Rtg",
   "title": "Testing the truth of an any read from a map…",
   "body": "Original title: Testing the truth of an any read from a map, or comparing it with a bool, crashes\n\nRepro: f(m: any): any := m[\"n\"]; v = f({n: \"NN\"}); print(v == no) (and if v, not v) is an out-of-bounds trap; v == ø and v is bool work. Also: is bool on a nested map held as any crashes (a = f({a: {b: \"deep\"}}); is_bool(a)). With wap-emitter. Workaround in lib/template.wap hides()/is_bool.\n\nAdded by wap-wiki-lib with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314994962\n\nbranch: any-truth-crash (2026-11-24)\n\nbranch any-truth-crash c606c0cd: original crash gone on main; remaining: g(m: any) := m[\"ab\"] with two map value types → 'never placed' (re-typed dispatcher result int→any, callers stale). Fix: typing restarts with boxed types known (+12/-5 core). Waiting: wap-reviewer + user OK via wap-interviewer.\n\nland: any-truth-crash e64c0d15 (held for core OK; reviewer sound)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: +12/-5 analyze: typing restarts when a dispatcher's result changes with a new boxed type. Land (e64c0d15).\n\nFixed in [f4198c5e](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f4198c5ef7843ed04b46d17c04b93f5c45d184e5): merge any-truth-crash: merge any-truth-crash: a function reading a map held as any is typed again when maps of another value type reach it later",
