  "column_since": "2026-11-24T07:46:46Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhvmtBg",
   "title": "census leaves typing stage untyped when…",
   "body": "Original title: The census leaves most of the typing stage untyped when a declaration-stage file calls a typing function\n\nSeen in own-type-overloads (B): when wap/core/analyze/modules.wap (declaration stage) called unified() with a TypingState(), test/wap/ratchet_census.sh reported 141 functions untyped (FUNCTIONS_UNTYPED should stay 0), although the compiler built and ran fine. The census tool (scripts/wap-census.warp) seems to type a file's functions only through the stage that uses them, so a call across stages loses them. A tool limit, not a language one: the check now runs at the start of typing (types.wap typed_among), which sidesteps it, but a declaration-time check should be able to use typing's relation. Added by wap-binding with todo add.\n\nAdded by wap-binding with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315095392\n\nbranch: census-declaration-typing (2026-11-24)\n\nwap-binding: not reproduced on main b0ae5087. A function in core/analyze/modules.wap (the declaration stage) calling unified(symbol(\"int\"), symbol(\"int\"), [], TypingState()) leaves the census at 2199 of 2199 functions typed, 0 untyped. So a call across stages does not lose functions in the census. The 141 of 8b1bb063 most likely came from the check running at declaration with an empty TypingState, which knows no records, rather than from the census tool. The check has run in typing (typed_among) since 6fb1b63f.",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": {
    "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhvmgew",
