   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T07:29:05Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhyoucQ",
   "title": "compiler keeps type words in separate lists",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler keeps its type words in several separate lists; one list of type words would shrink it and let unknown type names be refused\n\nType positions meet words from TYPE_WORDS (core/analyze/types.wap), NEVER_RESULT, FUNCTION_VALUE_TYPE fn, EMPTY_TYPE ø, NODE_TYPE, SHAPES (Symbol, List, Key …), kernel form names (Call), Bracket, Separator and type letters. One list (types/ or kernel) read by all of them is a shrink; refusing an unknown type name (`class Person { addresses: numbers }` typo) then rides on it at ~2 lines in core/analyze/scope.wap. Found by wap-reader on class-member-fixes; wap-lead: card as shrink.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315291193\n\nbranch: one-list-of-type-words (2026-11-24)\n\nland: one-list-of-type-words b61dc84e (express: test_hello green, compiler-growth ok, related areas green but node/matching _wanted reds unrelated). Pure shrink: type words in one file. Unknown-type-name refusal asked of wap-interviewer (A: leave it, recommended).\n\nreview b61dc84e: sound. Pure shrink: type words in core/type_notation.wap, no leftover NEVER_RESULT/NEVER_WORD/ENUM_WORD/EMPTY_TYPE_WORD; TYPE_WORDS and ATOM_TYPES only used for membership, so the new order is harmless; conditions.wap keeps the one names_type.",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
