 "native-function-values": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLN3js",
  "title": "native wap's driver can't use function values or…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T18:54:05Z",
  "key": "native-function-values",
  "agent": "wap-fixer",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T17:02:23Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T18:34:57Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh1lieg",
   "title": "native wap's driver can't use function values or…",
   "body": "Original title: The native wap's driver can't use function values or optionals, so it writes loops for contains and -1 for nothing\n\nA native build (wap/extensions/native via wasm2c, values in memory) has no layout for function values or optionals: core/emit/values.wap layout_of refuses them (card memory-layout-refusal gave the refusal). So the driver can't call list.contains(x) (types.wap passes a λ), can't hold list<text> in a class field (commands.wap Usage.words DEBT) and can't return int? (commands.wap option_values returns -1 for no option). Wanted: function values and optionals laid out in memory, then host_words.wap headless_checked uses device_openers().contains(name) and option_values gives int?. Raised by wap-reviewer on wap-headless.\n\nAdded by wap-fixer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315481659\n\nbranch: native-function-values (2026-11-24)\n\nexplored: memory builds refuse fn layouts at core/emit/values.wap memory_kept; options A (lower fn values to memory records + call_indirect, ~60-90 core lines), B (keep refusing), C (drop wasm2c for the driver, remove memory builds) sent to wap-interviewer; waiting for the user's decision\n\nprobed (seed): native build fails on any library λ (print→show uses map), on text? and int?. Shapes to supervisor: A ~50-65 core (fn value = i32 record addr + call_indirect table; T? = addr/0 or boxed record), C drop memory builds (driver as GC wasm under embedded wasmtime: −25 core, −180 lib). Recommend C. Worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/native-function-values, no commits.\n\nparked 2026-11-24: waiting for the user's A/C choice (interviewer, C recommended). No branch commits; probes were field/contains/optional.wap built with wap/extensions/native/build.sh and the seed compiler.\n\n2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: user asked before choosing A/C: how did warp do it, and check 64-bit smart pointers (warp wiki/smart-pointer.md) and i31 with one extra optionality bit. Warp: wasm2c only for primitive files (GC refused), GC programs under the wasmtime-embedding driver = C. Option D (i64 smart pointer in memory builds) sent to wap-supervisor/wap-fixer for measuring.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core +50-65, library +0-10) via wap-interviewer: option A, memory records. In memory builds a function value is an i32 record address + a call_indirect table; T? is the address or 0, a plain T? a boxed record. Native apps stay fully native without wasmtime. C and D (wasp-style i64 smart pointer, measured costlier) were shown and not chosen.\n\nuser's reason 2026-11-24: A because a native memory layout pays off for foreign function calls (C structs, callbacks) and may be reused for GPU buffers. Design consequence: memory records use the C ABI layout (field order, natural alignment, as a C struct), so a record can be handed to a C function or copied into a GPU buffer as is; a function value's record should be able to serve as a C callback (function pointer + context) where the FFI needs one.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: extra budget for automatic conversion between the GC format and the C-layout memory format, so programs never convert by hand: a GC value passed to a C function or a GPU buffer is copied into the C layout, and results come back as GC values. Size to be measured on the branch and reported to the user with the A total (no fixed cap given).\n\nmeasured 2026-11-24 (wap-fixer): items 1-3 core +56 net (+35 code only), wap/ tree +31, within the approved 65. Branch native-function-values. Open: the automatic GC<->C conversion the user budgeted separately, to be reported to the user with its size.\n\nSupervisor audit of steps 1-3: sound after fixes (core net +35 code / +56 with comments). Fix first: enum optional tag 0 reads as ø; zero-field record at address 0; memory_taken unaligned; signature variable passed as its own captures (probe); lists not on field_offset; two repeated branches; tests for the three cases.\n\nNative build fails on main too, not this branch: (1) an enum declared beside a class, e.g. 'enum Color { Red, Green }' + 'class Wide { x: float }', refuses with 'no layout for any: show(any)'; (2) a class of no fields, 'class Flag {}', fails because the class rule writes join([], \", \") and the empty [] stays list<any> natively. Both need an empty list literal / overload typed by its expected type in memory builds.\n\nSupervisor: 8f1760a8 sound (core +62 with comments, within 65). Items 1-3 + C callbacks hand off now; item 4 (converter) on a new branch, counts first.\n\nSupervisor: item 4 converter = option A (0 core: extensions/c/foreign.wap rules + lib/foreign.wap over class-inheritance step 1's declared-record hole), branch native-c-records, waits on class-inheritance step 1.\n\nland: native-function-values ac625671\n\nSupervisor: matching-boxed-test 97b195b0 sound (standing OK small fix, dispatch.wap +1). native-c-records: no 'struct Tm' spelling; try moving foreign.wap catch-alls into stage 2 beside the class rule (0 core) before a stages.wap mechanism.\n\nnative-c-records parked: stage-1 catch-all beats stage-2 class case. Proposed core (~5, stages.wap): within a head a rule waits for the stages of the rules written before it. Asked to the user via interviewer (supervisor rec: yes).\n\nUser OK 2026-11-24 (core, via interviewer): rule order across stages, ~5 core in wap/core/rules/stages.wap: within a head rules tried in written order, each waits for the stage the earlier ones need. Probe existing rules unchanged. Small overrun: interviewer decides; well above 5 back to interviewer. Commit body line: uses: extensions/c/foreign.wap, sugar/types.wap, sugar/records.wap\n\nFixed in [28f389a1](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/28f389a1579514e18ab117119121e6ea044a2f05): merge native-function-values: a native program's records are C structs, its function values live in memory and C calls them back, its optionals an address or 0 (user OK via wap-interviewer, core +62 within 65; wap-supervisor sound)\n\nFixed in [566c8cf4](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/566c8cf4f98a7d2e49ab4849e90868f4910a79c5): test: the size ceiling is the measured 141317",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": {
    "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhF4XjQ",
    "title": "wap's architecture changes, in the order the…"
   },
   "subIssuesSummary": {
    "total": 0,
    "completed": 0
   },
   "type": "Issue"
  },
  "left_board": "2026-11-26"
 },
