 "module-alias-preload": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLOj6w",
  "title": "module's alias sin => sine loses to the preload's…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T08:52:23Z",
  "key": "module-alias-preload",
  "agent": "wap-reader",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-23T19:34:57Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T08:52:23Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh2VORg",
   "title": "module's alias sin => sine loses to the preload's…",
   "body": "Original title: A module's alias sin => sine loses to the preload's sin, so the file using the module gets the math sine\n\ntest/wap/test_modules.sh \"a module's alias reads in the module and the file using it\" (from 0c924c7) never ran until test-modules-exit-last (0b1b4da) moved the exit to the end; it gives 0.1411200080598671 (math sin 3) instead of sine(3) = 6. Likely since lambda-words brought sin into the preload: the preload's word wins over the used module's alias line. Red on main since 0b1b4da. Added by wap-integrator with todo add.\n\nAdded by wap-integrator with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315527084\n\nbranch: module-alias-preload (2026-11-23)\n\nCause: a file's alias line becomes a word alias (operator_table.wap alias_row → word_aliases.add), and a word alias only applies to a name nothing defines (analyze/calls.wap:151), so the preload's sin wins. Two questions are bundled: (1) should an alias a file writes beat a library word? I recommend yes: it's an explicit line, ~3 lines (Alias gets written: yes, and calls.wap/scope.wap apply written aliases even where only the library defines the name). (2) word_aliases is one global list, so a module's alias line also reaches files that never use the module. Scoping it per file is a bigger change. Asked wap-lead.\n\nlib/fast_math.wap (library-port-rest) is alias sin => fast_sin … and waits for this; with it today, `use fast_math` then sin(1.0) is refused: 'sin is defined in types.wasm, which this file does not use'.\n\nbranch module-alias-preload tip bc3c9938 (worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/alias-heads), pushed. Aliases scoped per file (Language.reading/aliases_of); modules, alias_page, reader, operators green (182 ✓). Careful run (self, census, growth) was stopped by the restart: rerun it, raise ceiling in own commit, merge origin/main (raw-block may conflict in pipeline.wap/language.wap; fold onto raw's per-file table), patch, hand off to wap-integrator (user already decided: alias wins, scoped to module and its users).\n\nmain 7436bc9b: test_modules.wap 'a module's alias reads in the module and the file using it' red on main (got sin values, expected 6/4/4); found by integrator while landing module-global-2, red before it\n\nland: module-alias-preload b739f052 — merged origin/main (raw words and alias rows share one helper, handed), careful path green: 301 ✓ (modules alias_page reader operators dsl_page rules self), census green, growth OK, ceiling 134349 measured. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/wap-reader/module-alias-preload.patch. Handed to wap-integrator.\n\nintegrator state at restart: not landed yet; core +13 (language, operator_table, operators, pipeline): next integrator checks for the user's OK on record, then merges b739f052 in /Volumes/Worktrees/wap-land (clean, at 3f261d12) and pushes. Held for morning OK: foreign-globals-first 88f7063c, valueless-argument 3e46a738, is-equal 3b44e172 (notes/open_decisions.md), wap-build e7ebfcb7.\n\ntest_modules line 'a module's alias reads in the module and the file using it' turns red with exact-numbers-literals 82756128 (module functions typed only when called). On main already order-dependent: trig.wap sine(x: int) := x*2 + alias sin => sine, program print(sin(3)) prints 0.1411 (library float sin) alone, 6 once twice_sin(x: int) := sin(x)*2 sits in trig.wap. Reading question with wap-interviewer (A own alias wins / B library wins / C refused).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: core +13: a file's alias beats the library's word in that file and the files using it (sin(3) gives 6). This also answers the order-dependence question: reading A. Land.\n\nland: module-alias-preload 903c3c53 (main merged in, re-handed to the integrator)\n\nFixed in [1b45e592](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/1b45e592bcdd74b56c567e8033f8f71ffbfcd7d9): merge module-alias-preload: a module's alias beats the library's word in the module and the files using it",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
