  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh2aJoA",
   "title": "A C call inside a C callback overwrites the outer…",
   "body": "Original title: A C call made inside a C callback overwrites the outer call's copies of its texts and lists\n\ntypes/c.wap: c_call_started resets c_texts_end, and list_items.wap's handed_at is one FIFO, so a foreign call from a callback during an outer call (wgpu callbacks, qsort's comparator) reuses the outer call's scratch and reads back the wrong list copy. Fix both together: a per-call frame of scratch and copies. Found by wap-reviewer on item-widths.\n\nAdded by wap-emitter with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315532285\n\nbranch: c-callback-overwrite (2026-11-24)\n\nland: c-callback-overwrite 04645f5a — express+normal: test_hello ✓, compiler-growth ✓, c+native 62 ✓ 0 ✗ (test_c was red on main, now green). Census: +113 nodes (main already 135084 > ceiling 135072), the ceiling needs raising for this fix. Also 44df4dfe: run.sh counted a compiler that fails to build as 0 ✓ 0 ✗ (compile.sh exits the per-test shell); now a ✗. Patches: /Volumes/Worktrees/c-callback-overwrite/data/patch/. types/ part (c.wap, list_items.wap) for wap-reader's review.\n\nFixed in [1e945bb5](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/1e945bb5483657032b0241f7fa051236e0c5f7d1): fix: a C call made while another runs (from its C's callback) overwrites none of the outer call's texts, out-pointers or list copies\n\nwap-reader (types/ owner) on f8cf9b73: sound. (1) The outermost reset is right, and the count travelling in CCall restores cleanly. One limit, not blocking: a raise inside a callback skips c_called_back's decrement, so c_callbacks_running stays ≥1 and later outermost calls never reset again. Whether a raise can cross C frames at all is the open question; if it can, run the decrement on every exit. (2) and (3) are fine. Merge note: c-out-of-preload moves wap/types/c.wap to lib/foreign.wap and items_handed/items_returned/handed_at into it. Whoever lands second moves these hunks there.\n\nwap-reader: f8cf9b73 sound (types/). Known limit: a raise inside a callback that crosses C frames skips c_called_back's decrement, so outermost calls stop resetting. Matters only if a raise can cross C frames. Merge: wap-reader's c-out-of-preload moves wap/types/c.wap to lib/foreign.wap; whoever lands second moves the CCall/c_called_back hunks. Duplicate emitter fix reverted (9fdeeba4): nested_c_calls goes green with foreign-globals-first.\n\nreview foreign.wap (4 lines, net 0, tip 8e942d3d): sound. Each C call keeps its CCall in a local and c_call_ended restores it, so nested calls through callbacks are correct. Heads-up: c-out-of-preload (wap-reader) moves wap/types/c.wap to lib/foreign.wap. This branch changes types/c.wap by +56/-19, so whichever lands second has to move these edits over.\n\nland: c-callback-overwrite 8e942d3d, after foreign-globals-first (nested_c_calls red until it lands). Reviews: wap-reader sound (types/), wap-reviewer sound (foreign.wap, standing OK small fix). Patch /Volumes/Worktrees/c-callback-overwrite/data/patch/c-callback-overwrite.patch\n\nintegrator: held at 8e942d3d, both reviews sound; lands right after foreign-globals-first (88f7063c, user OK at 10:00); SIZE_NODES 135151 -> 135341 to remeasure on that merge\n\nintegrator: c-out-of-preload landed (13a0cf0a): types/c.wap is now lib/foreign.wap; move this branch's c.wap hunks there on re-merge\n\nland: c-callback-overwrite 45f83e5e, the hunks moved to lib/foreign.wap after c-out-of-preload; test_c all green, no longer waits on foreign-globals-first\n\nFixed in [7fd0141f](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/7fd0141f18aab455123932415219dd4b99cc6049): merge c-callback-overwrite: a C call inside a C callback leaves the outer call's state and handed lists intact (standing OK small fix; wap-reviewer sound for extensions/c/foreign.wap, wap-reader sound for the library part)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
