  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh2agmQ",
   "title": "memory build's missing layout for any can still…",
   "body": "Original title: A memory build's missing layout for any can still say no place\n\nAfter memory-layout-place, a native build of a program that sends texts through C bindings (a list parameter rule draft whose no-op body was `{}`, an empty map) said only 'a build keeping values in the memory has no layout for any: any'. Some layout path (field, closure or map layout) still passes the type itself as the place. Repro: a library function `f() := {}` reached from extensions/native's driver build.\n\nAdded by wap-emitter with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315532739\n\nbranch: any-layout-missing (2026-11-24)\n\nland: any-layout-missing 7d9261e0 — standing OK small fix (+2, wap-reviewer sound): a memory build refuses a compound type whole at its code; native/guarded/c 65 ✓, hello + growth green\n\nFixed in [5a9e3395](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/5a9e339505cca0c3c70ec87c2f41388ef108cb96): fix: a memory build refuses a compound type it lays out none of whole, at the code that has it, before its parts, which have no place: {} names map<any, any> and its line, not a placeless any\n\nFixed in [4e07458b](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/4e07458b0ee3040fad80900dde0ce8df3c5fb3be): merge any-layout-missing: a memory build refuses a compound type it has no layout for as a whole, at the code using it (standing OK small fix, core +2, wap-reviewer sound)",
