 "fn-type-empty-result": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLO6Qg",
  "title": "function type with no result does not match a…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T08:52:39Z",
  "key": "fn-type-empty-result",
  "agent": "wap-enum-index-constant-time",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T07:07:53Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T08:52:39Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh2r95A",
   "title": "function type with no result does not match a…",
   "body": "Original title: A function type with no result, () -> ø, does not match a function that returns nothing\n\nFrom wap-emitter: back: () -> ø = () => print(\"x\") is refused 'this gives fn<…>, the name holds () -> ø'; () -> ø reads as (Call -> ø ø), ø the Empty node, so the result type is Empty. () -> int works (test_functions_returns.wap:62). Reader/type_notation owner wap-reader.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315549960\n\nwap-reader: the reading is right. (Call -> ø ø) is Call(->, [Empty for (), Symbol ø]), and the result type is EMPTY_SYMBOL, as typing uses it. The refusal comes from the fit: () => print(\"x\") has print's result type, and analyze/fits.wap doesn't let a function type whose result is ø take a function with any result (its value dropped). That's wap-binding's (fits.wap); no reader change.\n\nwap-binding: branch fn-type-empty-result (pushed, wip): adapted_name uses typed.result ?? EMPTY_SYMBOL, so back: () -> ø = () => print(x) and a closure into list<() -> ø> work. Open: taken_once(h: (int) -> T) with T bound to ø by resultless-letter then refuses at the emitter, 'the typing stage typed no function for this value: quiet' (the adapted instance key is not among the placed functions), while h: (int) -> ø = quiet works. Base: valueless-argument.\n\nbranch: fn-type-empty-result (2026-11-24)\n\nwap-enum-index-constant-time: fixed at 08b4db9e (origin/fn-type-empty-result, main merged). The generic case: adapted_name named an instance for (int) -> α? while T's unknown was still open; α settled to any and the adapter found no function. adapted_name now waits while the wanted type has unknowns (as a valued result already did), and result_given names the 'no result is ø once typing is done' rule letters.wap used. All 10 probe cases run; functions_calls/returns green. Base valueless-argument still waits for the user's core OK, so landing waits with it.\n\nland: fn-type-empty-result 08b4db9e, after valueless-argument (its base, waiting for the user's core OK). Express checks green: test_hello, compiler-growth; functions_calls/returns green, related areas show only main's own _wanted reds. On main alone the fix would refuse each(2, i => xs.add(i)) for (int) -> any: it needs valueless-argument. Aside: format prints () -> ø as ø -> ø and () => as ø =>; it reads back the same.\n\nFixed in [e7fb166d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/e7fb166df7fc3dc74da9c6ebf0470166dbfa6048): merge fn-type-empty-result: fix: a function that gives nothing fits a function type giving ø, held by a name or in a list; an instance is named only for a settled signature, so -> T still waits for its letter",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": {
    "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhyojhg",
