   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh25Fww",
   "title": "C cannot call a wap function back: no…",
   "body": "Original title: C cannot call a wap function back: the program exports no c_callback_fired\n\ntest/wap/test_c.sh 'a function that gives nothing is called back through c_callback' (branch valueless-argument c2fad32) fails: 'C called a function back, but the module calling C exports no c_callback_fired'. lib/callbacks.wap defines c_callback_fired, but it is likely never emitted, since library functions are bound only when typing reaches them. The qsort line meets it too, past its set_field_i64 red. Owner: host-port / wap-emitter (not typing). Reported by wap-binding.\n\nAdded by wap-binding with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315562722\n\nFixed in [e20212cf](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/e20212cfb7dfd875bd5b96492fdfe55716c41e33): fix: the module callbacks exports c_callback_fired, the word C calling back reaches, so a program calling c_callback has it",
