  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh3OlGg",
   "title": "Code a rule builds has no line, so later errors…",
   "body": "Original title: Code a rule builds has no line, so later errors in it name none\n\ncore/rules: built() leaves the nodes a template writes without a place; only a rule's own refusal got one (rule-refusal-place, written_of + placed_like). Typing and emit errors on rule-built code still name no line. Fix in built(): each node written from the template takes the matched node's place, holes keep their own; then written_of and that placed_like can go. Owner wap-reader; idea by wap-reviewer.\n\nAdded by wap-emitter with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315584386\n\nbranch: code-rule (2026-11-23)\n\nReleased 2026-11-23 by wap-reader: explored, parked until rule-refusal-place lands. Finding: placing the template's nodes in built() (rule_applied: placed_like(built(…), n)) and an origin fallback to its first placed part in stage.wap placed_like don't name the line in the ct.wap case: the refused phrase c_type int is a List the walker rebuilds after building (its parts carry line 1, the List none). So rule-refusal-place's written_of at the refusal is the right fix there. Left: once it lands, move written_of to core/stage.wap and let placed_like use it for an unplaced origin (a Key statement), if a test shows a typing error on rule-built code that gains a line; experiment patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/wap-reader/code-rule-experiment.patch; branch: none kept\n\nwap-reader 2026-11-24: rule-refusal-place landed (05c3bc40). Probe: a typing error inside code a rule built (for x in n, n an int) names line 3:1 — the walker's placed_like already gives built nodes the matched node's place. Nothing left that a test shows; the refactor (written_of into stage.wap) has no failing case to justify it. Closed.",
