   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh4TwgA",
   "title": "list pattern [first, ..] breaks \"is\" type tests…",
   "body": "Original title: A list pattern [first, ..] in the compiler's own source breaks type tests of shapes, x is Empty, in the compiler built from the seed\n\nRepro (wap-binding, branch is-equal-lines before 9175d8c): in wap/core/analyze/scope.wap write\nnames_case(name: Node, scope: Scope) as bool := match definitions_meant(text(name), scope) { [meant, ..] => meant.kind == DefinitionKind.Case; _ => no }\nThe wap1 built by the seed then refuses every `x is Empty` in the source: \"is: Empty names no type and no test\" (core/parse/lexemes.wap:72, core/stage.wap:42). The block form with meant#1 builds. Either the list pattern miscompiles or the seed lacks the form (list-pattern-rest landed after the seed?).\n\nAdded by wap-binding with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315648293\n\nbranch: list-pattern-seed (2026-11-24)\n\nStale: the seed lacked the form. Both seeds since 5ecbbd00 (built from 79588683, c4b04ade) contain list-pattern-rest (ad7367e3). Checked on origin/main acb55b73: with names_case written as the card's [meant, ..] match, wap1 from seed wap-seed-2026-11-24-881efb6e builds and test_hello is green. No code change; main keeps its .take(1).any form.\n\nFixed in [1cd2981b](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/1cd2981ba6e880b8f1de9b3e837e8621ce30a5d4): chore: wap-seed.lock names wap-seed-2026-11-24-881efb6e, built from c4b04adef7",
