  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh4s4lg",
   "title": "wap build should make a native executable",
   "body": "Original title: wap build should make a program a native executable\n\ncli.md: `wap build app.wap` makes app, by wap/extensions/native/build.sh in wap's folder (as `wap test` runs run.sh). User OK via wap-lead (~5 lines, GC programs refused by build.sh). Branch wap-build, tip e7ebfcb7; test_native 42 ✓.\n\nAdded by wap-emitter with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315674561\n\nbranch: wap-build (2026-11-23)\n\nland: wap-build e7ebfcb7 (patch /Volumes/Worktrees/wap-build/data/wap-build.patch; express: test_hello ✓, compiler-growth ✓; test_native 42 ✓)\n\nnight 2026-11-23 (wap-emitter): fully built and measured, waits for the morning: +12 lines in extensions/native (driver.wap 9: BUILD_RUN, built() with the .wap refusal so a source is never overwritten, script_ran shared with tested; commands.wap 3: Action.Build and its help row), 1 test_native line; test_native 42 ✓, test_hello ✓, growth ✓. Without the .wap refusal it is 9 lines. Tip e7ebfcb7.\n\nState at restart: tip e7ebfcb7 pushed, 12 lines (9 without the .wap refusal); waits for the user's morning OK, then hand off.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (extension) via wap-interviewer: +12 lines in extensions/native WITH the .wap output refusal. Land (tip e7ebfcb7).\n\nFixed in [6b7a3be6](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/6b7a3be6eda44c6c49fda47583c8d1d0e565cb06): merge wap-build: wap build app.wap makes a native executable app; a .wap output name is refused so the source is never overwritten (user OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer)\n\nlanded as bb3f9188 on main (rebased onto the user's note commit; the hash in 'fixed in' predates the rebase)",
