  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh5IISg",
   "title": "A program that uses a library global beside a…",
   "body": "Original title: A program that uses a library global beside a closure or a C binding compiles to invalid wasm\n\nA library global imported lazily renumbers the program's own globals. Fix: core/emit/host.wap imports every library global first (+8 core, wap-reviewer sound, waits on the user's OK via interviewer). Cases: test_modules kept_global, lib/web.wap (use yaml + bytes binding), gpu port put(data: text, size: length) with a closure. Branch foreign-globals-first 47cd298a, patch data/foreign-globals-first.patch.\n\nAdded by wap-emitter with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315703199\n\nbranch: foreign-globals-first (2026-11-23)\n\nState at restart: tip 88f7063c in wap-integrator's batch ccd22407. After it lands: remove worktree, delete branches foreign-globals-first + valueless-argument-emit (local+remote), todo done.\n\nnight 2026-11-24: queued in notes/open_decisions.md for the user's 10:00 OK (core growth waits for the morning); no OK on record yet.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: core +8: library globals numbered before the program's own. Land (tip 88f7063c).\n\nFixed in [53a604ca](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/53a604ca826ee15b030a637299810c22ffc43916): merge foreign-globals-first: every library global is imported before the program's own, so a global imported late no longer renumbers the program's globals (user OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer)\n\nlanded as fd03b599 on main (rebased onto the user's note commit; the hash in 'fixed in' predates the rebase)",
