   "title": "A class written with its brace glued to its name…",
   "body": "Original title: A class written with its brace glued to its name, class Point{x: int}, is not declared.\n\nWiki writes class Point{x:int; y:int} (pattern-matching.md, type.md class Tree{left: Tree?; v:int}); the reader makes Point{…} one glue key, and class/enum/trait/match rule heads write the block apart. Fix in core/rules/matcher.wap: a list whose parts don't fit retries with glued curly blocks spread into head and block. Turns test_type_wanted's 'typed classes nest' line green. Branch glued-block-head.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315714076\n\nbranch: glued-block-head (2026-11-23)\n\ntip 342e6405 (merged with main, ceiling 133497 measured): hello, struct_page, type_page, self, rules, records, matching, pattern_matching_page green, growth OK; struct_wanted fully green and moved. Core +6 in matcher.wap: waits for the user's OK via wap-interviewer, then wap-reviewer. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/wap-reader/glued-block-head.patch\n\ntip e85e5478 (pushed, worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/glued-block-head): wap-reviewer's verdict built — matcher.wap back to main; rule_applied tries all rules on the phrase as written, then once with its end's glued block taken apart (lines.wap apart, beside unglued); forgot_since gone. Core: matcher 0, stages +2, lines +6. Merged origin/main; hello struct_page type_page rules records matching pattern_matching_page self green (type_wanted, matching_wanted red on unrelated forms as on main), growth OK, census green at ceiling 134412 measured. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/wap-reader/glued-block-head.patch. Waits for the user's OK (queued 10:00).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: core +8 (stages +2, lines +6): rule_applied retries with the end's glued block taken apart. Land.\n\nFixed in [1f1f709e](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/1f1f709ed71f591b36b44fac09cd9fd445216082): merge glued-block-head: class Point{x: int} with the brace