  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh5UPRQ",
   "title": "test that a value is a List also holds for calls…",
   "body": "Original title: A test that a value is a List also holds for code like calls and assignments, so sites that mean a written list can take the wrong branch\n\nKernel forms (Call, Set, If …) are lists underneath, so `n is List` holds for every one of them. A site that means a written list should match the bracket, `List(items, Bracket.Square, separator)` (fixed so in core/analyze/calls.wap as_read, branch char-list-constant). Sites still testing `is List`, each to check: wap/core/rules/matcher.wap:124 (`\"List\" => n is List`: a hole typed List matches a Call too), wap/core/rules/patterns.wap:242 (`not (items#1 is List)`), wap/core/parse/operator_table.wap:66 (`head is List`). Found by wap-binding and wap-reviewer.\n\nAdded by wap-binding with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315715983\n\nbranch: is-list-kernel-forms (2026-11-24)\n\nwap-binding: checked all 3 sites on main b0ae5087, and none meets a kernel form. matcher.wap's \"List\" hole type is used by no rule: sugar, types and lib write only Braces, Symbol and Text holes. patterns.wap's grouped_item and operator_table.wap's untyped read rule and declaration source as the reader gives it, before lowering makes kernel forms. A wrong branch cannot happen, and an outcome test cannot show it. Nothing to fix.\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-binding: done: checked, nothing to fix (see note); left: archive; branch: none\n\nNothing to change on main 7e34ec83: no rule uses the List hole type, and grouped_item and untyped read reader output before lowering (wap-binding).",
