 "struct-by-value-everywhere": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLRzik",
  "title": "C struct given by value should cross right on…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T07:34:19Z",
  "key": "struct-by-value-everywhere",
  "agent": "wap-enum-index-constant-time",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T07:31:48Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T07:34:19Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh5tGBA",
   "title": "C struct given by value should cross right on…",
   "body": "Original title: A C struct given by value should cross right on every machine, not only on ARM64\n\nlib/native/foreign.c's native_call_struct has no caller. It passes a struct of 17–128 bytes by value through the C compiler, so it is right on both x86-64 SysV (stack) and AAPCS64 (pointer to copy). types/c.wap c_struct instead hands a pointer to its own copy, which is ARM64's convention only (its DEBT; the on_arm64 check went in seed-on-arm64 because no host but the native wap answered it). Either c_struct's call goes through native_call_struct, which pays the DEBT and needs no architecture question, or native_call_struct goes.\n\nAdded by wap-emitter with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315739689\n\nplan (wap-emitter, night): three hosts answer a C call and none sees a struct: the native wap (extensions/native/host_words.wap host_word_answered → native_call, integers and floats only), warp's host (lib/native/foreign.c), and the wasm2c build (glue.awk's C prototypes). The import must say which argument is a struct of N bytes: the wasm signature cannot (an i32 pointer). Then native_call_struct in each host, or for wasm2c a prototype with a struct type, so C's compiler places it. Spans warp's host: needs warp-side work; not a night card.\n\nbranch: struct-by-value-everywhere (2026-11-24)\n\nland: struct-by-value-everywhere cf4e3023 — the unused native_call_struct goes; the x86-64 struct-by-value gap is native-other-platforms (2), named by c_struct's TODO",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
