 "absolute-links": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLTIUw",
  "title": "A program cannot read or write a file through an…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T14:28:17Z",
  "key": "absolute-links",
  "agent": "wap-fixer",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T13:38:39Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T14:28:16Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh7NTAw",
   "title": "A program cannot read or write a file through an…",
   "body": "Original title: A program cannot read or write a file through an absolute symlink (data/, /tmp, /var) when wasmtime runs it\n\nwasmtime's WASI (cap-std) never follows an absolute symlink, even with / preopened; relative ones work. Fix (supervisor, standing OK small fix): wap/types/host.wap opened_at resolves links with WASI path_readlink when an open is refused; lib/native/wasi.c answers path_readlink; console.wap:17's realpath workaround removed. Test: a read through an absolute link the test makes under its data/. Found by wap-interviewer: a program under data/ (-> /Volumes/Junk/warp/data) said 'cannot read'.\n\nAdded by wap-fixer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315826508\n\nbranch: absolute-links (2026-11-24)\n\nparked: branch absolute-links 3ce2800e. Option B (guest follows links) cannot work under wasmtime: path_readlink itself refuses a link whose target starts at / (WASI errno 63, perm; probe: a 6-line WAT calling path_readlink with --dir /: relative link 0, absolute link 63). The guest never learns the target. Remaining ways: A (make data/ a relative link), or the native host resolving real paths for the guest (a host import, not WASI).\n\nUsers' own absolute links (/tmp, /var, /etc on macOS) stay unreadable for wap programs under wasmtime; option C (a host import giving a real path) covers them if the user wants it. Plan: once data/ is a relative link (A, user with sudo), the branch's test line lands alone, the rest is dropped.\n\nHost-side option (design only, not built): shadow WASI path_open in run.wap / driver.warp (wasmtime C API: wasmtime_linker_allow_shadowing + define_func, keep the original from wasmtime_linker_get); on failure realpath() the guest's path and call the original again. Catch: the real path must sit in guest memory, possibly longer than the guest's buffer, and no host-safe spare space exists in an arbitrary module (wap's scratch past BYTES_AT would do, tying the host to wap's layout). About 40-60 lines per host. Also found: a relative link climbing out of the preopen (../../…/Volumes/Junk/warp/data) fails under warp too; only the installed native wap follows both. The fleet's scripts avoid the link (compile.sh), so only manual checks hit it.\n\nseen by wap-fixer: `cd data/probe; wap ../wap-tests/<wap1>/wap1.wasm - out.wasm` fails 'write: cannot open ../wap-tests/<wap1>/types-<hash>.wasm' — the compiler's types-module cache path climbs out of the preopen '.'; the same compiler by its absolute path works. Same root as this card (a path leaving the preopen): the driver could realpath the compiler path it passes.\n\ncovered by running-type 17b743f9 (on wap's native host: the types module's real_path follows links itself, and the host answers path_readlink with POSIX readlink, so links to absolute paths and .. out of the current folder read; test_files has both checks). A plain wasmtime CLI run still refuses absolute links, which is WASI's own limit. Close this card with running-type's landed commit; branch absolute-links 3ce2800e is dropped then.\n\nFixed in [94f57169](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/94f5716952699f21fb4e1061c8d4eb055aac18f3): chore: open decisions: data link question withdrawn (a relative link does not help either; host-side fix on card absolute-links)\n\nclosed by mistake with 94f57169 (an unrelated chore): reopened; closes with running-type's landed commit\n\nFixed in [f896b0c9](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f896b0c901171fc95daae3810d693123809095b8): merge running-type: run.wap back under 300 lines (pure shrink)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
