   "title": "wap format joins a list or map onto a single line",
   "body": "Original title: wap format joins a list or map written one item per line onto a single line\n\ncore/format.wap written(): a bracket with OWN_LINES prints all its comma items as one row (lib/scene.wap's things table becomes one ~1500-char line). Wanted: each item on its own line, as written.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316120417\n\nbranch: format-keeps-lines (2026-11-24)\n\nbranch format-keeps-lines tip 4865ff67: format.wap +9 (rows_of), stages.wap groupings_written refitted (positions kept); reader+rules green, census 135197. Waits for the user's core OK (asked wap-interviewer).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: +9 format.wap + stages.wap refitted: a bracket's written lines kept. Land (4865ff67).\n\nland: format-keeps-lines b56f99df — handed to wap-integrator with patch\n\nFixed in [d6cbbdca](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/d6cbbdca8b8abc7f7346aa90d377cdcd36f5f233): merge format-keeps-lines: test: the size ceiling is the measured 135197: format keeps a bracket's lines",
