  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiASffA",
   "title": "program that calls no C function still imports…",
   "body": "Original title: A program that calls no C function still imports C's memmove, free, strnlen and memcpy, so it cannot run under wasmtime.\n\ntypes/c.wap moves to lib/foreign.wap (use foreign); pipeline.wap: a module the types module uses is bound to, never prepared again (standing OK small fix, wap-lead). Branch c-out-of-preload (wap-reader). Unblocks export-dispatcher.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316148227\n\nreview d6ae5c3c (pipeline.wap +3): sound, standing OK small fix. Nits: typed_modules and library_code_of both compute used_modules(types.code), which is cached and so cheap, but could be computed once. Check: a used file compiled alone as the program (e.g. a types file the types module uses) is now filtered out of program_modules too; confirm it compiles to the library's copy rather than an empty program, and update the DEBT comment if this pays it off.\n\nbranch: c-out-of-preload (2026-11-24)\n\nreview 30af0f8b (pipeline.wap standard_brought, +2): sound, standing OK. Nit: the DEBT at core/rules/templates.wap:28 says only a definition's name reads DERIVED (analyze/calls.wap ranked). standard_brought now reads it too, so add it to that comment.\n\nland: c-out-of-preload 62c4c41c. standing OK small fix (language.wap: one module per file per compile): d6ae5c3c +3; also 30af0f8b +2 (a word a rule wrote comes in without a hint); both sound per wap-reviewer. Proved against b18b38a0 on a throwaway merge: the types module imports only WASI, and wasmtime --preload of it runs the export (42). called_export lacks that --preload, which is export-dispatcher's to add.\n\nFixed in [13a0cf0a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/13a0cf0ae1241a5e3eb05d52d4beb3c3432522d2): merge c-out-of-preload: C's side (types/c.wap) moves out of the preload into the standard module foreign, so a program calling no C imports no C and runs under wasmtime; a module the types module uses is prepared once per compile (+3), a word a rule wrote is brought in without a hint (+2) (standing OK small fixes, wap-reviewer sound)",
