 "ordering-from-less": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLYPhU",
  "title": "Every ordered library type writes all six…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T09:00:13Z",
  "key": "ordering-from-less",
  "agent": "wap-enum-index-constant-time",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T07:54:11Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T08:01:30Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiAfx-A",
   "title": "Every ordered library type writes all six…",
   "body": "Original title: Every ordered library type writes all six comparison operators by hand; > <= >= could follow from < once, as != follows from ==\n\nwap/types/prelude.wap already has the generic `!=(a: T, b: T) := not(a == b)`. Generic `>(a: T, b: T) := b < a`, `<=` := not(b < a) and `>=` := not(a < b) beside it would let lib/exact.wap, units.wap, semver.wap, time.wap, reals.wap and hyperreal.wap drop their four spelled-out lines each (a shrink). lib/version.wap (library-port-version) defines only compare, == and <, waiting for it. Open: whether a generic operator over T resolves the inner < at the call's type, and its build cost. Found by wap-fixer.\n\nAdded by wap-fixer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316161557\n\nbranch: ordering-from-less (2026-11-24)\n\nland: ordering-from-less 5b3e288a — >, <= and >= once in wap/types/prelude.wap from <, copies gone from 7 files (net -13, 0 core). express path: hello + growth green; areas units exact reals hyperreal uncertain time_patterns texts operators 191 ✓, only red test_units_wanted (wanted, red before). Wiki sentence + test line pending interviewer.\n\nFixed in [a6f299d6](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/a6f299d6ec708ed83c00f99e91b76dc80c7c5fd1): refactor: >, <= and >= are written once in the types module, derived from a type's < as != follows from ==; the copies in exact, units, time, reals, hyperreal, uncertain and texts go\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (wiki) via wap-interviewer: wiki/operator.md sentence as proposed (a type defining < gets >, <=, >=); its test line goes into test/test_operators.wap; land 5b3e288a.",
