  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T14:12:26Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiBcqtA",
   "title": "wap optimize removes the functions, constants and uses a program never reaches",
   "body": "Original title: wap format --fix removes the words and uses a program never calls\n\nUser 2026-11-24 (via wap-interviewer, card exact-numbers note): use the called-or-not detection of module-functions-on-call (2310158e, TYPED_WHEN_CALLED) mainly to remove unused things with the format fix command: functions, constants and use lines nothing calls. Format is wap-reader's; the detection is in core/pipeline.wap. Lead routes it.\n\nAdded by wap-lead with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316222907\n\nbranch: format-remove-unused (2026-11-24)\n\nphase 1 (functions) OK from wap-lead: 'wap format fix <file>', check lists 'file:N: unused: word', fix prints each removed word. Phase 2: use lines (needs a 'module reached' fact, sugar modules are used without calls, ~+5 core). Phase 3: constants (Set is not a Define, needs binding reach). Ask wap-lead before phases 2/3.\n\nbased on 2310158e (exact-numbers-literals: TYPED_WHEN_CALLED written by called_only); lands only after exact-numbers-literals\n\nbranch format-remove-unused tip 926f89b6 on 2310158e: format fix built + test/wap/test_format.wap (3 ✓); +317 nodes; wiki/cli.md line at the interviewer; review: wap-reader\n\nbase changes: wap-lead merges 2310158e with main (pipeline.wap is theirs); format fix gets rebased onto their new tip when they send it\n\ntip 670353db: wap-reader's two must-points fixed (drop by definition place, not line; uncalled moved to compiler.wap, core +2). +306 nodes. At the interviewer: core OK, and exported functions (ABI.md:116). Rebase onto wap-lead's merged base pending.\n\npaused (user order via supervisor): the fleet builds dependent types first; tip 670353db reviewed sound by wap-reader, waits for core OK, exports decision and wap-lead's base\n\nuser 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: these are different commands. wap format = lint; wap fix = lint + apply structural suggestions; wap optimize = (later) stripping unused functions etc. So unused-removal belongs under 'wap optimize', not format fix; park it as optimize's first part, CLI wiki lines to the interviewer.\n\nuser (via interviewer): unused removal is `wap optimize`, not `format fix` (format = lint, fix = lint + structural suggestions). New base from wap-lead: module-functions-on-call a4574fa1. Rework entry point + rebase when the pause lifts.\n\npaused; the worktree is removed, the branch format-remove-unused 670353db is pushed\n\nuser 2026-11-24 (via wap-reader): the removal goes under wap optimize (later), which strips unused functions, constants and uses; not under format or fix. The cli.md lines are with the interviewer. When the pause ends: rename the entry point, widen it to constants and uses, rebase onto module-functions-on-call.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (wiki) via wap-interviewer: cli.md lines approved — wap format <file> prints the canonical form and lists what it would change (lint); wap fix <file> does the same and applies the structural suggestions; wap optimize <file> strips unused functions, constants and uses.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (wiki) via wap-interviewer: wap beautify becomes an alias of wap fix (fix canonical), 0 core.\n\nlib/fix/ is an exact copy of warp's fix CLI; it cannot run in wap (it loads lib/compiler/parsing/lexer.warp, which wap lacks) and nothing refers to it. Kept as the source the coming wap fix command ports from (wap-reader, interviewer agree). Usage swap fix-canonical 13f2fd7e handed to the integrator.\n\ninterviewer 2026-11-24: core parameter typed_modules(..., program: text) in core/pipeline.wap, net 0 lines, no new form, makes the compiler do what the approved cli.md line says: standing OK small fix once wap-supervisor (reviewer) calls it sound; no user question. Phases 2 (uses, ~+5 core) and 3 (constants) come back to the interviewer as their own requests; red in test_optimize_wanted until then.\n\nstanding OK small fix (wap-interviewer): typed_modules gains program: text, net 0 core. optimize <file> on 03d6a5db; constants and uses wanted (test_optimize_wanted). Supervisor review pending, tests running.\n\n03d6a5db diff-audit: core part sound (+1 net). Back: optimize removes functions other files use (library with a print line; rule template helpers) -> spare names mentioned in the folder's other files; print removed after write; tests for comments + used library fn (wap-supervisor).\n\n47d90d93: fixes verified (mentioned_beside spares names the folder's files mention; print after write; tests). Sound (wap-supervisor, core part standing OK small fix). land: format-remove-unused 47d90d93\n\nFixed in [854f740a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/854f740afdc4e2d94402a81359be7b301baf54e2): merge format-remove-unused: wap optimize <file> removes the functions nothing in the folder uses (the cli.md line the user approved; core +1 net, standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound)",
