   "body": "Original title: Version numbers and similar words can follow a word without parentheses or quotes\n\nwap-reader branch phrase-parameters e88162ac; DSL parameter kind word.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316272253\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: a 5th DSL parameter kind word = the next blank-free word, raw (use regex version 1.10.0, version(text: word)); core +4 net over phrase's +52; wiki: dsl.md four→five ways + row | word | the next word, up to a blank, raw text | version 1.10.0 |; use.md:14 phrase→word; function.md:18 'except a word parameter's'.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: alias-line fix A (+6 core operator_table.wap, phrase-parameters 2e80cec5): an alias line's sides are read as written, and format keeps alias lines.\n\nFixed in [4e9b191f](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/4e9b191f5ab490e48c592ae3451f0af9a029c1da): merge phrase-parameters: phrase and word parameters, an alias line read as written (user OK 2026-11-24, core +4 over phrase +52, alias fix A +6; spec wiki/dsl.md)\n\nAfter landing: wap-reader tries `infix operator ’s(owner, field: word)` in the library (p’s name = p.name); a card with the attempt only if plain wap cannot reach the field (interviewer, card unicode-operators).",
