   "title": "Measure how fast wap runs proof kernel work",
   "body": "Original title: Measure how fast wap runs the kind of work a proof kernel does\n\nMilestone K0 (plan 10.5): match over a dozen cases, 10 million small allocations, deep recursion, identity and hash of values, and loops written as functions calling themselves in last place against while loops. Results in data/, nothing kept. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316280103\n\nbranch: theory-measure (2026-11-24)\n\nK0 measured, numbers sent to wap-coc-plan; probes data/k0/. Blockers: enum-equality-doubled (== 2^depth), hash by case name (quadratic maps), self call in last place 15x slower than while and not looped\n\nland: theory-measure 7fa2f376\n\nFixed in [6dff9560](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/6dff95602dd5b27cc7fb4fd2abb9c7409bc3dc7b): merge theory-measure: notes/theory.md's Costs passage, the K0 numbers\n\ndup?: coc-t2-plan (by score, 2026-11-25)",
