  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCUK8w",
   "title": "class is a structure with projections and eta…",
   "body": "Original title: A class is a structure with projections and eta, and two proofs of one proposition are equal\n\nMilestone K4 (plan 6.3, 6.5): projections, eta for structures, unit eta, proof irrelevance. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316283232\n\nbranch: theory-structures (2026-11-24)\n\nwap-coc-plan built projection typing (K4's kernel typing rule) alongside typing; wap-fixer's part: structure eta, proof irrelevance, the equality cache.\n\ncompute.wap (from the K5 review): iota and quotient_step each look the head's declaration up. Fold them into one lookup that matches on the kind (Recursor, Quotient, else ø) when compute.wap is touched for K4; K3's rule that opens a number wants the same place.\n\ntyping part landed 80cdbba7 (wap-coc-plan); eta rules left (wap-fixer)\n\nland: theory-structures 32704679. K4 equality: proof irrelevance, structure eta, unit eta, equality cache (equal.wap, environment.wap). Projection of a constructor computing (compute.wap) is wap-emitter's part.\n\nReview: Supervisor's advisor reads 32704679 (equal.wap +59, environment.wap +6); verdict follows. Idea (wap-fixer): typing and compute caches keep closed terms only; keeping open ones too makes proof irrelevance cheap under binders.\n\nSupervisor review of 32704679: SOUND (advisor). Before landing: notes/theory.md:138 still says results are kept only for closed terms; fix it, and note that read.wap:208 rewrites a hypothesis's type in place, which is safe because only positive answers are kept. Next: (a) type_of keeps open terms too (typing.wap:20), since equal.wap:39-40 retypes both sides and is quadratic under binders, wap-fixer; (b) Projection compute step (compute.wap:36-44) and a recursor on a non-constructor structure value expands it (compute.wap:59-65), wap-emitter on theory-computing; (c) missing test lines: projection of a constructor, proof irrelevance under a binder. unify.wap:24 must pass typed terms (equal now raises on ill-typed).\n\nbranch theory-structures-computing (wap-emitter, built on 32704679): K4's computing — projection step (field_of), recursor on a structure value expands by projections (case_standing, with K), iota and quotient_step one lookup (eliminated), made_by shared. Lands after theory-structures.\n\nland: theory-structures-computing 01db5d1d (after theory-structures 32704679) — theory, theory_quotients_wanted, theory_recursors_wanted 35/35, test_hello green\n\nland: theory-structures cb9bc1ad (replaces 32704679), handed to wap-integrator\n\nred before and after this change: test_theory_logic_wanted 'the axiom is the only door to an unproved statement' (got refused by argument type, expected refused by value type); the test is wrong, fixed on theory-prelude-logic 6de978dd\n\nSupervisor review of cb9bc1ad (open-term type cache): SOUND, ships. Non-blocking: (1) typing.wap:18-19 and theory.md:138-141 should say why it's safe: a kept type is the unfilled form and every elaborator reader fills it (a put-off Problem retried after read.wap:208 can reach proofs_equal with the stale type and give a spurious no). (2) environment.wap:212 comment still says closed terms only. (3) projection_type (typing.wap:81) skips the data-from-proof check under an unfilled level hole; elaborator-only, since declared re-checks.\n\nFixed in [898927fb](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/898927fb529ae623b8bca2044b9c9a1cc16e5f18): chore: the comments say why kept types of open terms are safe with the elaborator's holes",
