   "title": "print of an enum case shows only the case name",
   "body": "Original title: print of an enum case with fields shows only the case name\n\nenum Edit { Keep(item: int), Delete(item: int) }; print Keep(3) prints Keep, print \"${Delete(4)}\" prints Delete, but print [Keep(1)] prints [Keep(1)]. Installed wap and main's wap1. Found by wap-emitter; the kernel's tests print terms.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316284384\n\nbranch: enum-case-print (2026-11-24)\n\nland: enum-case-print e69e1914 (standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer: sound; express path green). Side effect: the enum's ==(a, b: text) goes through text, so Keep(3) == \"Keep\" now gives no; no wiki or test line relies on the old reading.\n\nFixed in [396aa7d6](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/396aa7d6ec519ad92a75b2d00b9f48ed4a6cc897): merge enum-case-print: a case with fields shows as its text, print Keep(3) says Keep(3) (standing OK small fix, 0 net, wap-reviewer sound)",
