   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCVQgw",
   "title": "prelude defines lists, optional values, pairs…",
   "body": "Original title: The prelude defines lists, optional values, pairs, texts and char in the theory\n\nTrack L: text as its code points, a text literal as the library's function of a number, char as text where #it == 1. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316284430\n\nbranch: theory-prelude-data (2026-11-24)\n\nbranch theory-prelude-data (on theory-below, which brings Pair/Unit): part 1 pushed - prelude/data.wap: list (count, joined, mapped, 3 laws), optional (or_else, 2 laws), Pair swapped (law), test_theory_prelude_data 7/0. Left: texts (a texts statement + decoding the literal's number, needs divide/modulo shortcuts from L2), char (needs where/subset in the door, K4).\n\npart 1 handed to wap-integrator: land theory-prelude-data a9b8a1cc (lists, optional, Pair swapped; 7/0). Texts wait for theory-prelude-divide (wap-simplifier: the kernel's divide shortcut exists, its three theorems are unproved; a text literal decodes its number by divide/remainder 256). char waits for subset types in the door. Card stays open.\n\na9b8a1cc audited by wap-supervisor: sound, land it. Fix forward: the test helpers prelude/data/checker/said_of/holds are copied from test_theory_prelude_numbers.wap:7-12, move them into scripted.wap for both files. Add one outcome line for Pair.swap. The refusal of a false law stays: for a checker that is wanted behavior.\n\nfor the texts part (supervisor, on a9b8a1cc sound): move the copied test helpers (prelude/data/checker/said_of/holds, also test_theory_prelude_numbers.wap:7-12) into scripted.wap for both files; add one outcome line for Pair swapped.\n\npart 1 landed (list, optional, Pair): e64bceed\n\npart 2 handed to wap-integrator: land theory-prelude-data 67e6500a. Texts: texts(text_of) binding, a literal = text_of(1 then code points base 0x110000), both readers (explicit, elaborator) read Text and Char literals; prelude data.wap: text (of_points, points, spelled, text_of); checked.wap: char := Subset[1](text, one_point). Tests 5 new lines green. Nothing left on this card once landed: todo done theory-prelude-data <landed commit>. Open questions sent to wap-interviewer: # counts code points (char.md) vs graphemes (Footguns); int(c)/c as int parse a char as decimal text.\n\nsupervisor: advisor review of 67e6500a: sound. Required fix applied by the supervisor in the worktree: environment.wap copied() also carries texts (a literal inside a block's type was refused), plus a test line. Plan stays: the kernel's only literal is the nat; texts encode by code points.\n\nFixed in [67154fad](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/67154fad9ab7a8f1a0a0c2edf0e936f331134d6a): merge theory-prelude-data: texts and chars in the theory, a text literal the number its code points spell (wap-supervisor sound)",
