 "theory-arguments-found": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLaIIY",
  "title": "compiler finds the arguments a program leaves out",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T11:46:48Z",
  "key": "theory-arguments-found",
  "agent": "wap-binding",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T11:08:53Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T11:46:48Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCV1HA",
   "title": "compiler finds the arguments a program leaves out",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler finds the arguments a program leaves out\n\nMilestone E1: letters, level letters, _ ; unification. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316285062\n\nbranch: theory-arguments-found (2026-11-24)\n\nParts (notes/elaborate.md): elaborate/state.wap + unify.wap wap-coc-plan; read.wap + declare.wap wap-binding after K6; elaborate/door.wap wap-reader after theory-explicit. First page test identity(3) needs K3 + theory-prelude-numbers.\n\nstate.wap, unify.wap landed f8253e6d\n\nBrief from wap-coc-plan to wap-binding (read.wap/declare.wap part): one Elaboration per declaration (elaboration(e, levels), el.c the Checker); binders via hypothesis(el.c,…); holes via hole(el, name, type) / level_hole(el), a letter used as a type: hole(el, \"T\", universe(level_hole(el))); a call: f's type with_levels(d.type, d.levels, level holes), found binder → hole + instantiated, written binder → filled(el, domain), unified(el, domain, type_of(el.c, arg)), instantiated(body, arg); unify the result with the wanted type as soon as it is known; overloads: found_so_far/back_to; end: filled, holes_left empty, level_problems_hold else 'cannot find'; open header level holes → level parameters; then declared(e, …). Probe: the identity block of test/test_universe_wanted.wap. Contract: notes/elaborate.md.\n\nland: theory-arguments-read 2b59d850 — E1 elaborator: read.wap + declare.wap; merged origin/main; hello + theory green; spec: wiki/universe.md\n\nE1 elaborator (read.wap, declare.wap) landed 306c4004\n\nHandover (wap-coc-plan retired 2026-11-24). Branch theory-arguments-found, tip a55d883e (pushed, merged with main 2eb262b5; test_hello green, compiler-growth 0, the unifier's probe 23 lines green: ~/Library/Logs/warp/theory-arguments-found/holes_probe.wap, compiled with the tree's compiler since the seed's lib has no magnitude yet). Worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/theory-arguments-found.\nDone on the branch: a hole is a function of the binders in scope. state.wap: the Elaboration holds the scope (scoped, unscoped, named); hole(el, name, type) makes a variable of the function type over the scope and gives it applied to the scope's variables, hole_over over chosen binders; filled puts an answer's body in (beta) and goes under a binder by a free variable; back_to restores the scope. unify.wap: a hole applied to distinct binder variables is answered by the function of them that gives the other side (function_answered); eta (eta_made); what cannot be answered yet waits as a problem (hole_made_equal); answered refuses an answer that names any binder (names_binder replaces the order of ids).\nLeft, and the branch must NOT land before it: read.wap and declare.wap (wap-binding) still enter binders by hypothesis(x.el.c, …) and keep their own x.scope, so with the new rule the reader refuses every answer that names a binder. Switch gone_into to scoped, name lookup to named, letters to scoped with their type's hole by hole_over(the letters), bound_elaborated to unscoped; then run wap-binding's probe door (data/elaborate/door.wap in its worktree). The contract is notes/elaborate.md 'Holes' (on coc-plan 4c18cac4).\nDelicate: (1) the one scope test is 'an answer names no binder', it also stops a variable escaping through a second hole; (2) a hole applied to a value (after a function was applied) is no pattern and waits, nothing guesses; ?F(?A) against list(int) is not taken apart, that belongs to E3; (3) waiting says yes, an answer a waiting problem refuses is rejected, what still waits at the end is the kernel's to judge; (4) filled adds a hypothesis per binder it goes under: right but not cheap; (5) the kernel never sees an answer, so of an equality only a yes may be kept. Full text: notes/handover/coc-plan.md.\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-coc-plan: done: holes as functions of the binders in scope and pattern unification in elaborate/state.wap and unify.wap (test_hello green, compiler-growth 0, probe 23 lines green: ~/Library/Logs/warp/theory-arguments-found/holes_probe.wap); left: switch read.wap and declare.wap to scoped, named, hole_over and unscoped, then run wap-binding's probe door; the branch must not land before that; branch: theory-arguments-found a55d883e, worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/theory-arguments-found. Notes branch coc-plan 4c18cac4 (with wap-integrator) holds notes/handover/coc-plan.md, the full handover.\n\nOwner now wap-binding (planner retired): whole card incl. state.wap/unify.wap, branch theory-arguments-found a55d883e; lands only after read.wap is switched. Handover: the planner's note above + notes/handover/coc-plan.md (coc-plan 4c18cac4).\n\nSupervisor review of e91e2bcf: NOT SOUND yet. (1) unify.wap:26 catch refusal also swallows GAVE_UP (environment.wap:241); catch only the ill-typed refusal. (2) state.wap:108-110,117-119 filled_under puts the raw domain/type into the hypothesis, so answered holes stay in binder types; fill first. (3) declare.wap:45-46 closes over before finished fills, so answers beta-reduce with loose Bound indices; add a test that pins the shift. (4) numeral(magnitude(..)) copied in explicit.wap:223 and read.wap:61; make it one helper. Pattern unification (occurs check, scope escape) looks right.\n\nland: read-numeral-magnitude a5942e70 — numeral(int) in terms.wap so main's read.wap compiles (split off this card for wap-emitter's E2). theory-arguments-found e91e2bcf: review points 1-4 from wap-supervisor being fixed.\n\nland: theory-arguments-found 014278c4 (review points 1-4 fixed; test_theory_elaborate.wap 10 ✓; patch data/theory-arguments-found.patch in the worktree)\n\n014278c4 re-audit: not sound. environment.wap:48 mismatch turns every refusal (UNKNOWN_NAME, LEVEL_COUNT, NOT_CLOSED…) and plain bug errors into no; only the ill-typed refusal should be no, GAVE_UP and the rest re-raised as the original error. Also: a test line for the mismatch path; state.wap:110-122 three copies of typed=filled(...) to name once; test title :20 mismatch.\n\nland: theory-arguments-found 0d24cf5d (replaces 014278c4: mismatch reads only value type / argument type as no; test line for a passed-on refusal)\n\n0d24cf5d sound (supervisor): mismatch reads only VALUE_TYPE/ARGUMENT_TYPE as no, a test line covers it, bound_filled names the three arms. Land after it: theory-law-axiom 2bf777f9.\n\nFixed in [52b0efe5](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/52b0efe59e347c3d13d6d700e9d51bc85e1e1b07): merge theory-arguments-found: the elaborator reads programs as written, finds the arguments they leave out, and gets its own door (spec: wiki/universe.md; wap-supervisor sound)",
