 "enum-equality-doubled": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLaJOU",
  "title": "Comparing two values of a program's own recursive…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T11:48:30Z",
  "key": "enum-equality-doubled",
  "agent": "wap-fixer",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T09:58:42Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T11:48:29Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCW8VQ",
   "title": "Comparing two values of a program's own recursive…",
   "body": "Original title: Comparing two values of a program's own recursive enum with == takes time exponential in their depth\n\nK0 measurement (data/k0/eq2.wap): enum Tree { Leaf; Wrap(inner: Tree) }: == of two 20-deep Wrap chains 9 ms, x4 per 2 levels; a 100-deep App chain never finishes. In the wasm, the shared tag_equal helper (core/emit/equality.wap cases_compared over p.records.items) holds the program's own enum's case blocks twice (tags 95, 96 twice; the types library's Node cases once), so each field is compared twice: 2^depth. Likely p.records lists the program's records twice. Blocks the proof kernel (coc-plan). Found by wap-simplifier.\n\nAdded by wap-simplifier with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316286181\n\nbranch: enum-equality-doubled (2026-11-24)\n\nwap-simplifier's find: the probe is /Users/me/dev/angles/wap/data/k0/eq2.wap and the helper is data/k0/build/helper.wat, which holds the case blocks for tags 95 and 96 twice (lines 266 to 332). cases_compared (wap/core/emit/equality.wap:49) walks p.records.items, which comes from added_records(Records(), statements) at emitter.wap:61, so the Tree Record is probably in the statements twice. The dedupe belongs at the source, not in cases_compared.\n\nbranch enum-equality-doubled 3ae15c8c (fix 22d16d01): added_records keeps one record per declaring place. 200-deep == went from >20 s to 0.33 s; equality_page and enum_page 18/18; hello and growth green. Waiting for wap-reviewer's 'sound', then the integrator. Open: why the emitter's statements hold the record twice (fixed downstream, source not traced).\n\nland: enum-equality-doubled 542fd7d2. Standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer: sound. Typing placed the program's own records twice (once in s.records, once in placed); now once.\n\nFixed in [5876b656](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/5876b65643ccb6e686528885604ffae1e94917f4): merge enum-equality-doubled: a program's own records placed once, so == on a recursive enum runs in linear time (200 deep: >20 s → 0.29 s; standing OK small fix, +1, wap-reviewer sound)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
