 "theory-statements-effects": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLaJxE",
  "title": "Blocks, variables and loops become terms, and…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T18:00:59Z",
  "key": "theory-statements-effects",
  "agent": "wap-emitter",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T13:28:23Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T14:26:27Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCXeKw",
   "title": "Blocks, variables and loops become terms, and…",
   "body": "Original title: Blocks, variables and loops become terms, and effects become types\n\nMilestone E5 (plan 9.5, 9.2). plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316286737\n\nbranch: theory-statements-effects (2026-11-24)\n\nplan sent to wap-supervisor 2026-11-24: statements.wap (blocks/lets/if/exits as Step), loops.wap (for = list.recursor fold; while = opaque looped → Div), effects.wap (Eff/bind/pure, host opaque, effects of, ! Pure). Open: for reaches elaborator by door language without the for rules (rec.)\n\nPlan approved (wap-supervisor): statements.wap/loops.wap/effects.wap under elaborate/, Step(S,R) in prelude effects, while -> opaque looped: Eff(div,S). Decision ⚑A general form: door reads with the pre-lowering stages' rules (by stage/kind, never by rule name) so for/sugar reach the elaborator as phrases.\n\nDoor loads tree rules (E3), so for is rewritten to while before the elaborator. Phase 1 builds on kernel-form names. for: asked interviewer A) For kernel form (rec), B) rule kind, C) wait for E6 measures.\n\nuser 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer (not yet an OK): 'for' takes not only lists but iterators that provide next() (as in warp), and those may be endless; so a for ends only over a finite iterable: we need a dependent type 'finite iterator' (lists are one). The plan (For form or otherwise) must say: for over a Finite iterable is Pure/fold, over any other iterator Div; with the core cost, back to the user.\n\nReworked (user: iterators may be endless): Iterable trait in types/ (next protocol); Finite(T): Iterable + size: nat + law shrinks; for over Finite = fuel-size fold (Pure), else looped Div; found by instance search like Decidable. For kernel form still needed (+1 form, ~10 emit). Sent to interviewer.\n\n9c91764e diff-audit: back. 2^n continuation copies (join point), no If arm in form_elaborated, Set on non-name place silently drops write (refuse), tests for return/if missing (wap-supervisor).\n\nsupervisor review 40c551fb: join point sound, If arm staged for E3 (honest). Fixes: place_binder accepts Key(non-symbol, :, type) → typed s#1: nat = n silently dropped; wanted lines use Equal.refl(nat,6) instead of the siblings' Equal.refl[1]. Then straight to the integrator.\n\na9cb3891: both fixes in, sound; handed to the integrator.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (kernel +1 form For, ~10 core emit) via wap-interviewer: the Finite plan as reworked (Iterable with next(), Finite = Iterable + size + law shrinks, for over Finite = Pure fold, else Div). The user asks to blur the line between class and protocol instead of a separate trait keyword: design how Iterable/Finite are declared as classes that also act as protocols (structural conformance), with its cost, back to the user via the interviewer before declaring them.\n\nuser 2026-11-24: Finite plan approved (For kernel form ~10 emit lines, Iterable/Finite with the shrinks law). Iterable/Finite wait for the class-as-protocol design; the For form is built now.\n\nclass-as-protocol shape sent to interviewer 2026-11-24: member spelling decides kind (field / required word / method=default / law); required word ⇒ no constructor = protocol; structural conformance, declared claim checked; trait = class synonym; core ~+7 (calls.wap +6, Self +1), records.wap 3–4 rules, theory +5; next() returns (item, rest). Fixes Job (protocol_named calls.wap:369).\n\nFixed in [2cf9f22f](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/2cf9f22f53782b868da371d0b8708069a9c1a2f0): merge theory-statements-effects: the elaborator reads statements and effects (E5 phase 1; wap-supervisor sound)\n\nland: theory-statements-for 1d039299 — For kernel form, every for a counted loop; waits for the user's OK on +34 core lines (supervisor relays)\n\nFor 1d039299 (theory-statements-for): counted For(place, count, body), +34 core (+31 with loops.wap). Audit: sound design; fixes: DEBT note → DONE, tests (empty, 5 to 1, break, item write). Supervisor decided (rare edge case, 0 core): writing the loop name changes only that round, for ranges as for lists; Footguns line.\n\nsupervisor: For (branch theory-statements-for, tip 53cf39dd): 3 fixes sound; +34 core/kernel sent to wap-interviewer for the user's OK; land after the OK.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core ~7 + sugar 3-4 rules + theory ~5) via wap-interviewer: class/protocol blurred as wap-supervisor designed: one form class; field = name: type, required word = signature without body, method = body (default body in a protocol); a class with any required word has no constructor (a protocol); conformance structural, ': Proto' a checked claim; laws = required words returning proofs; trait a synonym with got-it note; fixes class Job { act: () -> int } show recursion. next(): (item: T, rest: Self)? (pure, not stateful). This also settles the parked traits question.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (kernel+core +34 net) via wap-interviewer: land the For kernel form as measured (branch theory-statements-for, tip 53cf39dd); no smaller shape required.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (wiki trait.md) via wap-interviewer: the claim is written class dot: Comparable {x:int}. Aliases in the same place, if they don't cost much: class dot extends Comparable {…}, class dot is Comparable {…}, class dot < Comparable {…} (each with a got-it note naming the colon). The trailing form class dot{…} is Comparable is dropped. If an alias needs more than its spelling in the one claim rule, colon only.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: extends / < / : are one act: class B extends A (or B < A, B: A) means B is an A: it gets A's fields and default methods and must define A's required words (checked). With a plain class this is inheritance as now, with a protocol it is the claim. Size measured before landing. 'class dot is Comparable {…}' as a further alias waits for rule-word-guard (rule heads taking a word set).\n\n2026-11-24 interviewer: class-protocol lands at +9 net core (approved ~7). The 2 extra lines are a general fix (template annotations merged, not dropped; format.wap -5), within the estimate's margin, so not a user question.\n\nuser 2026-11-24 (wiki) via wap-interviewer: a function that returns nothing is impure. Such a function counts as effectful even when inference finds no effect: it is never folded, memoized or dropped, and ! Pure on it is refused. Passage for wiki/effects.md and wiki/pure.md plus a test line, assigned through wap-supervisor.",
