  "column_since": "2026-11-24T11:48:34Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCXiRA",
   "title": "calls itself in last place runs 15 times slower",
   "body": "Original title: A function that calls itself in last place runs 15 times slower than the same loop written with while\n\nMeasured in K0 (wap-simplifier, data/k0/ on theory-measure). The kernel's run terms (S2) emit loops this way. Wasm return_call or turning a self-call in last place into a loop.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316286799\n\nbranch: tail-call-slowdown (2026-11-24)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: A — a call in last place (block end, both if branches, every match arm; no fitting after) is emitted as wasm return_call, mutual calls included; ~+12 core (emitter.wap ~10, functions.wap 1, one opcode). Check wasmtime and wasm2c before landing.\n\nbranch tail-call-slowdown d5334207: return_call in last place works on wasmtime (30M deep, functions_calls green). Blocked: wasm2c 1.0.42 writes invalid C for functions with locals ending in return_call (wabt #2884, fixed upstream 2026-10-19, unreleased), so the native wap and test_hello fail. wabt HEAD verified in data/wabt-head; install decision with wap-interviewer.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: install wabt HEAD (pinned commit, Homebrew keg linked over 1.0.42) for wasm2c's return_call fix (wabt #2884); TODO to return to the release at 1.0.43.\n\nland: tail-call-slowdown a679e56c — test_hello, functions_calls, native (wabt-head keg, -std=c23) green; wanted: test_try_wanted (red before), test_overloading_wanted (red, ambiguity)\n\nland: tail-call-slowdown a679e56c (with wap-integrator)\n\nFixed in [f7262831](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f72628311c7013725df6006de64d408a7805c2f6): merge tail-call-slowdown: a call in a function's last place is wasm return_call, mutual calls included, so deep tail recursion runs in constant stack (user OK 2026-11-24, option A, ~+12 core; wasm2c from wabt's main branch, -std=c23)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
