  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T16:11:31Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCYljw",
   "title": "compiler proves what follows by computing, from…",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler proves what follows by computing, from facts in scope and by rewriting with proved laws\n\nMilestone P2: by, chain. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316287839\n\nbranch: theory-simple-provers (2026-11-24)\n\nsupervisor: shape approved (prove/ untrusted; facts, rewriting, by, chain). Rule: automatic rewriting only with oriented laws (lhs bigger, rhs vars ⊆ lhs); permutative laws only via by/chain, once per position; a looping by-law refuses naming it.\n\nby: the wiki's `:= by add_zero, add_commutes` stays red. The operator table can't give a prefix word a precedence looser than the comma, because the comma is no table row: the reader splits a line into Separator.Comma list items before operators are read (core/parse/operators.wap line 53). Missing feature: the comma as a row of the table (a group below assignment), so a word like `by` can bind looser than it. by(a, b) and single-name by are built.\n\nland: theory-simple-provers d6839cff (express+normal: test_hello green, compiler-growth OK, theory_verify one intended red: wiki `by a, b`, the comma no table row; theory_elaborate's 4 choice reds are main's, fixed by dot-word-braceless-call). Steps 1-3 + by; chain waits on the supervisor's reader/table decision.\n\nland: theory-simple-provers b9298ed0 (supervisor audit fixed: laws tried once, refusals name `by`, symmetry test named; theory_verify 18 ✓, the one intended red `by a, b`)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: (1, core +7 layout.wap) an indented line starting with an infix operator continues the line above, ON CONDITION that it does not interfere with blocks (check: an indented block line starting with a prefix-capable glyph like -x, !x, #xs, or a list bullet); if it interferes, use the user's alternative instead: a line ending in an operator continues onto the next (trailing + / ==). (2, 0 core, operator table) a == b == c chains as a == b and b == c, like <.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: a == chain whose operands are booleans (p == q == r) is refused at compile time with a fix-it: write (p == q) == r or p == q and q == r. Expected 2-3 core lines in the chain lowering (standing OK if ≤3 net and sound, else back to the user).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (wiki, 0 core) via wap-interviewer: proof.md 'By a chain of steps' uses the trailing-operator form (a + b + 0 == / a + b by add_zero == / b + a by add_commutes); leading-operator continuation dropped (block-line clash). Footguns.md 284/806 rewrites approved by the interviewer as the direct wording of the user's == chain decisions.\n\nSupervisor: chain-reader-probe 3be5d20f is sound (+2 core, standing OK small fix). Gap: chained_call builds 3-operand chains only, so a == b == c == d and a < b < c < d are not extended; the general n-ary chain is wanted.\n\nland: chain-reader-probe 3be5d20f (equality chains; contains this card's branch via ef393467)\n\nFixed in [e46a9dc0](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/e46a9dc0320f4ad39e293dbc4c2dfc471ca1997c): merge theory-simple-provers: a law stated without a proof is proved by computing, an earlier law or hypothesis, or rewriting both sides; `by a` names the laws (user OK: notes/coc-plan.md provers; wap-supervisor sound)\n\nFixed in [eb4cf9a3](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/eb4cf9a341bb00c2d3517626da9352f7752092cd): test: the size ceiling is the measured 139797",
   "state": "CLOSED",
