  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T02:23:05Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCY1SQ",
   "title": "compiler proves ring identities and linear facts",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler proves ring identities and linear facts about whole numbers\n\nMilestone P3: the laws of wiki/laws.md Proved by wap. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316288095\n\nbranch: theory-arithmetic (2026-11-24)\n\nbranch theory-arithmetic tip c7c6d471: phases 1-2 + int ==, test_hello green, theory tests 62/64 (2 = wanted page spellings), growth OK; awaiting supervisor audit, then handoff\n\nreview c7c6d471 (supervisor): sound after — 1) gate: spec: names the wiki page whose examples it proves (proof.md has no such rule), on the commit that adds apart.wap or its merge; 2) reuse recursor_facts (match.wap:136), binders_counted (match.wap:251), carried() (rewriting.wap:181) and one CARRIED name, not copies in apart.wap; 3) hypothesis rewriters oriented like laws, and reaching REWRITE_LIMIT says so instead of stopping quietly; 4) one comment: termination rests on REWRITE_LIMIT. Kernel re-checks every proof: no soundness risk found.\n\nland: theory-arithmetic 776a8239 (supervisor sound after fixes; handed to wap-integrator)\n\nfollow-on (supervisor): a prover's refusal reason (rewriting 'gave up'/'endless rewriting') never reaches the law's verdict (Tested/Untested); showing it needs verify.wap to carry the reason — verdict wording is wiki (proof.md), so it waits on a wiki line first.\n\nphase 3 shape (supervisor OK, 0 core, ~20 elaborator lines + linear prover): walk proves the loop variable's range once and puts it in scope as a fact; obligations try the provers with facts in scope before 'unproved condition'; general linear prover (linear forms, elimination) from the first commit. wap-binding builds; wap-theory-conditions-lifted reviews statements.wap/obligations.wap.\n\nFixed in [df644b2e](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/df644b2ec6df53355fda5ad493248db9d22098bb): merge theory-arithmetic: provers for whole-number arithmetic (wap-supervisor sound)\n\nland: theory-arithmetic-linear 5e72983e\nPhase 3 (linear arithmetic over the whole numbers) finished, handed to wap-integrator; patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/theory-arithmetic/theory-arithmetic-linear.patch. Normal path: test_hello ✓, compiler-growth ✓, theory tests 206 ✓ / 1 ✗ (test_proof_wanted, red by design), 146 s.\nDone: the loop number's range (1 <= it and it <= count) is the fact; let definitions are facts; differences a - b bounded where b <= a is proved; the prover keeps only bounds linked to the goal; each linear proof is a law of the environment (levels: those its terms name), reused when its statement repeats; the checker grows its hypotheses in place (+= copied: quadratic, the old slowness).\nLeft: loop3 (`i + 1 <= #xs` from `1 <= b - a`) needs a case split on a <= b; review statements/read by wap-theory-conditions-lifted: sound. wap format of the installed wap rewrites the house style (`: T` → `as T`), not applied.\n\nAudit 5e72983e: sound-after-fixes, no unsound lemma. Fixes before landing: (1) linear.wap:90-91/139-140 name the repeated conditions; (2) linear.wap:78 a missing prelude law refuses loudly, never a silent ø; (3) statements.wap:50/175 next_round guards numbers! like walked_elaborated; (4) test_theory_arithmetic gets a negative line (a <= b not Proved). Supervisor decisions: (5) IT_WORD moves out of core/rules into the theory layer; (6) only obligations.wap reaches the provers, through one prove/ entry; statements.wap imports no prove/ file; (7) a prover's lemma refusal stays loud (a prover bug is a bug); a run's lemmas join the environment only when it returns Proved. Fixer: wap-fixer after theory-run-terms. (wap-supervisor)\n\n(5) amended: IT_WORD stays in core (core lowers it); statements.wap just stops importing core/rules/lowering.wap and builds the condition over its own binder. (wap-supervisor)\n\nland: theory-arithmetic-linear fc8fb9b0 — audit of 5e72983e fixed: (1) named conditions of_numbers/made_yes; (2) missing prelude law refused (UNKNOWN_NAME); (3) loop_numbers guards both uses; (4) negative line: unbounded a <= b gives FAILED with a counterexample; (5) statements.wap has no core/rules import, the range is function_of(x, NUMBER, …) (read.wap shares it with it_read); (6) obligations reaches the provers through prove.wap condition_proof; reflexive_case beside equality_checked; statements imports no prove/ file; (7) first_proof withdraws what a prover that found nothing declared (Reach/withdrawn in environment.wap). Also: the base had no_is_not_yes in both logic.wap and numbers.wap (merge of main), fixed (kept in logic). Normal path: hello ✓, 29 theory areas + proof_page 347 ✓ (only _wanted reds), arithmetic 11 ✓, growth ✓. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/theory-arithmetic/theory-arithmetic-linear-audit.patch\n\nRe-audit fc8fb9b0: sound (wap-supervisor). Forward: tested.wap:10 still uses prove/goals.wap directly, so route it through prove.wap (folded into theory-run-terms' fixes). A refusal swallowed by an outer catch may keep a run's lemmas; harmless, since they are kernel-checked.\n\nFixed in [6fafd387](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/6fafd387b0810e35b0e0b5767497610ce55d70fc): merge theory-arithmetic-linear: a loop's index proved in range from its bounds, each linear proof a lemma declared once, the checker growing its hypotheses in place (phase 3; wap-supervisor sound)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
