   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCa00g",
   "title": "reader takes an enum's result type before its…",
   "body": "Original title: The reader takes an enum's result type before its brace and the effect after a function type\n\nPlan 3.11: two shape rules, once the pages are approved. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316289967\n\nbranch: theory-shape-rules (2026-11-24)\n\nNot needed after E2 (wap-reader, 2026-11-24): the elaborator's door reads statements as operated (operated_file), before any shape rule, so a sugar rule could not replace explicit.wap's before_cases. That function is the elaborator reading the written head, not a workaround. A rule that turns the tree into `enum (nat: Type) {…}` would also collide with records.wap's `enum $name { $cases... }`. The effect half (`(text) -> unit ! IO`, read today as `unit! IO`) has no consumer: nothing in wap reads effects yet, so it belongs to the effects milestone of notes/coc-plan.md.\n\nClosed as obsolete: not needed after E2: see the note",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
