 "assign-right-first": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLav2M",
  "title": "indexed assignment xs#i = f() stores into the old…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T12:30:44Z",
  "key": "assign-right-first",
  "agent": "wap-binding",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T10:44:19Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T11:48:43Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiC-hGg",
   "title": "indexed assignment xs#i = f() stores into the old…",
   "body": "Original title: An indexed assignment xs#i = f() stores into the old list when f replaces xs\n\nwap-binding: u.added#at = g() where g does u.added += [x]: the value lands in the old list.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316325731\n\nuser 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: a bug. The right side runs first, then the target is read, as in Python (core/emit: swap two steps; standing OK small fix size).\n\nbranch: assign-right-first (2026-11-24)\n\nland: assign-right-first 2d2953dc — standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer: sound; hello + assignment_page/lists/maps green (the _wanted files were red already)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (wiki) via wap-interviewer: assignment.md sentence approved: \"An item's assignment works out its right side first, then reads the list it changes, as Python does: in xs#1 = grown(), if grown() replaces xs, the new list gets the item.\"\n\nFixed in [35c2e075](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/35c2e075dfdefd2f1664a61e837d7b6b23ffc9e5): merge assign-right-first: in xs#i = f() the right side runs first, then the list is read (the user's rule 2026-11-24; standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer sound)\n\nuser 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: compound assignment stays left first, as written: a += b is a = a + b read left to right, x.lines += [f(x)] loses f's own append; 0 core, one wiki/Footguns.md line. Only plain/item assignment works out its right side first.\n\nUser chose (a): a op= b reads a before b; Footguns line in wiki 1e1ebc9.\n\ncorrection 2026-11-24: the user's 'left first' click was a slip; asked again, the user asked whether the pattern is common enough. It is not (seen once, wap-fixer's theory export, worked around with a local), so it is an edge case: += stays left first (a = a + b), 0 core, one Footguns line.",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": null,
   "subIssuesSummary": {
