  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiDP0EA",
   "title": "still makes a function value although the wiki…",
   "body": "Original title: -> still makes a function value although the wiki keeps it for function types\n\nwiki/closure.md: '=> is the one lambda arrow; -> writes function types'. wap/core/rules/lowering.wap:175 FUNCTION_ARROWS = [\"=>\", \"->\"]; stale test line test/test_functions_calls.wap:66 ('wiki: both arrows denote lambdas'). Blocks types as values: endo := (A: Type) -> A -> A reads as a function. Fix: the one line (standing OK small fix after wap-reviewer) + drop the test line in its own commit; first rewrite any -> lambdas in wap/, lib/, samples/, test/ to =>. Needed before E2's tests. Found by wap-binding, via wap-coc-plan.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316343773\n\nbranch: function-value-wiki (2026-11-24)\n\nbranch function-value-wiki tip a855aef7: FUNCTION_ARROWS = [\"=>\"], all lambdas rewritten; test_hello green, functions_calls 72/0. Standing OK small fix, waiting for wap-reviewer's sound. Seen alongside: use markup fails on main already (a rule template does not treat a lambda's parameter as a local: 'the rule writes $e, which its pattern has no hole for'); a stray -> value gets the generic 'nothing defines this name' instead of a fix-it naming =>.\n\nland: function-value-wiki a855aef7 (wap-reviewer: sound; handed to wap-integrator)\n\nFixed in [279158b6](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/279158b694679be4c1919ba9c50ef262a97998b0): merge function-value-wiki: -> writes only function types, => is the one lambda arrow (wiki/closure.md; standing OK small fix, wap-reviewer sound)",
