   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiDxHXA",
   "title": "prelude's division of natural numbers is licensed…",
   "body": "Original title: The prelude's division of natural numbers is licensed by its theorems\n\nSplit from theory-prelude-numbers (wap-fixer): divide's three theorems (quotient*n + remainder == m; d(m,0) == 0; remainder < divisor) need induction on m with a case split on equals and lemmas equals-sound, zero/successor-multiply, add assoc/comm. Waits for E1/E2 (theory-arguments-found, theory-enums-match-recursion) so the proofs are written with match, not raw recursor terms.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316377552\n\nWhen divide's theorems land, also add an accepted-run line for them to test/wap/test_theory_second.wap (left out of K7 by supervisor decision).\n\nWhen the divide proof lands, add a line to test/wap/test_theory_second.wap: the second checker accepts the export of the prelude with divide bound (the K7 review asked for it; branch theory-second-opinion).\n\nbranch: theory-prelude-divide (2026-11-24)\n\nland: theory-prelude-divide 3ae4ae3c — divide/remainder in prelude/numbers.wap by explicit recursor terms (the kernel door reads the prelude, no match there); 3 shortcut theorems + lemmas, axiom-free; tests: theory_prelude_numbers + theory_second green (25 ✓), test_hello green, compiler-growth OK\n\n3ae4ae3c audited by wap-supervisor: sound, land. Fix forward: rename numbers.wap:75 at_most_successor (too close to at_most_successors) e.g. at_most_step; the test 'division's theorems rest on no axiom' checks only divide_and_remainder, check all three.\n\nFixed in [8e79c8d3](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/8e79c8d3b7f3cbbdfaf058893e0e089d2c91d33a): merge theory-prelude-divide: divide and remainder in the numbers prelude, a shortcut licensed by its three theorems without an axiom",
