  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T12:14:05Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiD-Zbg",
   "title": "Every Unicode symbol can be declared as an…",
   "body": "Original title: Every Unicode symbol can be declared as an operator, and person’s name reads the name field of person\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: (1) almost all of Unicode is allowed as operator symbols: not a list but a simple check of a Unicode range, replacing OTHER_GLYPHS / GLYPH_RANGES in wap/core/parse/atoms.wap (letters stay name characters, quotes stay quotes inside a quote). Today ’ outside a quote: 'a character the reader does not know: ’s name'. (2) the possessive: ’ outside quotes is an operator glyph, a library declares infix operator ’s, so p’s name is p.name (1 library line). If the operator table cannot spell ’s (glyph + letter) as one operator, report to wap-interviewer before adding more core. Wiki: operator.md says any symbol may be an operator; the possessive comes back as a sentence (text to the user first).\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316390695\n\nbranch: unicode-operators (2026-11-24)\n\nMeasured: the use side costs 0 core lines (joined_glyphs joins a glued glyph+word into a declared spelling). The declaration side needs about 3 lines in core/parse/operator_table.wap declaration_words, folding glued tokens before the parameters into one spelling; today `infix operator ⊕s(a,b)` declares nothing. Waiting for the interviewer's OK on (1)A/(2)A.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: (1) A: operator symbol = ASCII punctuation + U+2000–2BFF + ¬±×÷·¹²³, minus the letterlike block U+2100–214F and ∞∅€ (names); about -3 core lines. (2) A: spellings of a glyph glued to a word are declarable (operator_table.wap fold, ~3 core lines; use side already works via joined_glyphs), so a library writes infix operator ’s(owner, field).\n\nland: unicode-operators 74fe711f (patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/wap-reader/unicode-operators-74fe711f.patch). test_hello green, area tests 264 ✓ with only the 2 reds main already has (test_numbers, test_unicode_wanted), operators 69 ✓. wiki/operator.md text awaiting user approval via interviewer.\n\nFixed in [5fbc3629](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/5fbc36293e0a8fe0fc38a83131ef5ebe910241af): merge unicode-operators: every symbol in U+2000–2BFF and ¬±×÷·¹²³ is an operator symbol, letterlike ones and ∞ ∅ € stay letters; a symbol glued to a word declares as one operator (user OK 2026-11-24; spec: wiki/operator.md)\n\nuser 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: operator.md text: shorter wording wanted: say plainly that every Unicode symbol that is not a letter is an operator symbol, no ranges in the wiki (the ranges stay in atoms.wap). The rest (letterlike ∞∅€ as letters, glued spellings ⊕s, ’s outside quotes) unchanged; the ~8 core lines are accepted.",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
