   "body": "Original title: The formatter crashes on the type-theory files and rewrites text interpolation and type annotations into worse code\n\nReported by wap-emitter: `wap1.wasm format` on wap/extensions/theory/*.wap (explicit.wap too) crashes with 'this list has no item at this place'. On a test file it turns \"${x}\" into + text(x) + and ': text' into 'as text', degrading the source. Blocks the landing check 'format the .wap files you wrote'.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316407634\n\nbranch: formatter-crashes (2026-11-24)\n\nland: formatter-crashes 2f326030 (stacks on format-enum-result-colon; patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/wap-reader/formatter-crashes.patch). : text → as text is deliberate per wiki/function.md\n\n7f628cb0 (format.wap, 2 lines) reviewed by wap-supervisor: sound, standing OK small fix. f(x): text -> f(x) as text kept on purpose (canonical word, wiki/function.md).\n\nFixed in [62787a85](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/62787a85e4d62407987f3228ccec01660aa0ce3f): merge formatter-crashes: wap format no longer crashes on an empty block (every theory file formats), and a text with holes beside an operator keeps its quotes (standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound)\n\nFixed in [fcdf78cf](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/fcdf78cf6f0c5d888ccd1e88cb67e6ff32366517): test: the size ceiling is the measured 137695 after the as-narrows revert and the format fixes",
