   "title": "function that calls itself on a field of a field…",
   "body": "Original title: A function that calls itself on a field of a field, like fib, is refused by the elaborator\n\nBranch theory-below. Unit and Pair in the theory prelude; the below helper (brecOn) built per enum from its recursor; recursion.wap finds them through the prelude environment. Decided by wap-supervisor 2026-11-24. Builds on theory-enums-match-recursion.\n\nAdded by wap-emitter with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316411411\n\nbranch: theory-below (2026-11-24)\n\nland: theory-below 913d0c5d (patch /Volumes/Worktrees/theory-below/data/theory-below.patch). products(Pair, Unit) in prelude/logic.wap; each enum's below/course from its recursor; fib elaborates. test_hello + theory, theory_elaborate, theory_logic, nested, numbers, quotients, recursors green; compiler-growth ok (spec: wiki/pattern-matching.md).\n\npost-merge bbb95ac0 (second checker accepts products by binding nothing) reviewed by wap-supervisor: sound. Ignoring a binding trusts less, and the values below arrive as definitions the checker checks itself.\n\nfollow-up theory-below-tidy 7f3a32d2 handed to wap-integrator (supervisor's tidy: course only where made, refusal says why, one Declaration builder, +2 tests); land after theory-below\n\nFixed in [42870deb](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/42870deba619ea1cdc8559222ae92940ec821f6e): merge theory-below-tidy: a type's course used only where the theory made it, a recursion refused without one says why, one major per type and one Declaration builder (wap-supervisor's tidy)",
