   "title": "The second proof checker refuses nested inductive…",
   "body": "Original title: The second proof checker refuses nested inductive types, so they are checked only once\n\nsecond/blocks.wap:95 rejects a field like list(tree). K7 promised nested types are checked twice. Follow-up of theory-second-opinion.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316416517\n\nbranch: second-proof (2026-11-24)\n\nland: second-proof a7d9efe3 (merged origin/main incl. 2405c796; theory_second, theory_nested, hello 27 ✓ 0 ✗; growth 0; patch /Volumes/Worktrees/second-proof/data/second-proof.patch)\n\na7d9efe3 advisor review: not sound yet. Must: sort_of on contained(...) types + added family types (blocks.wap:113-138, nested.wap:63), same check in kernel inductive.wap:63; refusal tests (non-positive nested, ill-typed container arg). Smaller: resting counts written cases. Decision (supervisor): ported unnesting algorithm accepted as independent (no shared code); header says so.\n\nland: second-proof d01f0633 (review fixes: written cases and containers typed, added families' types checked, axioms of container arguments counted, kernel types written cases; 2 refusal tests; theory_second, theory_nested, theory, hello 55 ✓; growth 0)\n\nd01f0633 advisor re-review: second checker sound. Kernel inductive.wap:100 headers_checked accepts a header naming its own block (Vec/Loop example, mutual A,B: A->Type); 1-line refusal + tests, then sound (wap-supervisor, standing OK small fix). Kernel :68 has no door test: elaborator refuses first.\n\ntip ad7c40c8: the kernel's written-case check (inductive.wap after cases) has no door test: the elaborator refuses Box(Loop(Loop)) first, so it is defense only; header check + forged twins tested\n\nland: second-proof ad7c40c8\n\nFixed in [f240fee8](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f240fee8ab8316c03d4f26778159fe086f8f6768): merge second-proof: both theory checkers refuse a block type whose own type holds the block; the second checker types written containers and added families (wap-supervisor sound)",
