   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiEpHEA",
   "title": "generic function over two values refuses float…",
   "body": "Original title: A generic function over two values of one type refuses a float and an int in the numbers test\n\ntest/test_numbers.wap:89 red on main 33054e7e: 'no same_value takes (float, int): same_value(a: T, b: T)'. Seen in the unicode-operators landing and by wap-reader before it (same message), so it is not from that branch. Who broke it is not bisected (supervisor: nobody else bisects).\n\nAdded by wap-integrator with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316430211\n\nbranch: numbers-same-value (2026-11-24)\n\nfix 9d7bb9be, merge 08b3f9b4 (branch numbers-same-value, pushed): a dispatcher's result joins only the definitions it may choose (taking_of + generic); a generic +(list<T>, T) left it unwritten, so held_number(3)+0 was a float. test_hello green; numbers, number_page, calls, functions_calls, call_page 163 ✓ 0 ✗. Core +3 net, standing OK pending wap-reviewer's sound (not running); diff-audit found it sound apart from an edge case. land: numbers-same-value 08b3f9b4\n\nFixed in [84872bcd](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/84872bcd709eb3c855716dfdbae33f89da3e0760): merge numbers-same-value: a dispatcher's written result joins only the definitions it may choose, so held_number(3) + 0 stays an int (standing OK small fix, +3, wap-supervisor sound)",
