  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiEttFw",
   "title": "Running the type-theory front end directly with…",
   "body": "Original title: Running the type-theory front end directly with wap fails: it cannot read the program file\n\nFrom the repo root: `/Users/me/dev/bin/wap wap/extensions/theory/elaborate/door.wap /Users/me/dev/angles/wap/data/try/natural.wap` prints 'cannot read /Users/me/dev/angles/wap/data/try/natural.wap', exit 1 (also with a relative path). From data/try with ../../wap/…/door.wap: 'cannot read ../../wap/extensions/theory/elaborate/door.wap'. The tests pass because they build door.wasm first and run it with folder=tree. Door.md promises `wap …/door.wap program.wap`. Blocks the try line for E1/E2/theorem-law-axiom (seed wap-seed-2026-11-24-f2c4bc85).\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316434391\n\nbranch: running-type (2026-11-24)\n\ninterviewer 2026-11-24: A decided without a user question: a bug fix with one obvious answer, and core is only +1 line (the path_readlink row in core/emit/host.wap), within the standing OK after wap-supervisor's 'sound'; the ~15 lines in types/host.wap and ~8 in lib/native/wasi.c are library/extension. Symlinked folders are common (the user's own data/ is one), so C is no option.\n\n7229d258 (.. half) sound per wap-supervisor (standing OK small fix: +3 WASI rows core, 1 line native). Absolute-link half: option (1) native readlink shim sent to user via interviewer; land both together.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (extension) via wap-interviewer: the native host answers WASI path_readlink itself with POSIX readlink for its preopens '.' and '/' (~10 lines wap/extensions/native + 8-line C shim lib/native, 0 core); other hosts keep refusing loudly. Supersedes the interviewer's guest-side A note above.\n\nland: running-type 072bbec3 (both halves; core unchanged: the WASI calls are foreign words; native host answers path_readlink with POSIX readlink; files+hello 23 ✓ on the merge)\n\n072bbec3 reviewed by wap-supervisor: NOT sound. The readlink shim in main.c doesn't bounds-check guest offsets (memory escape); fault errno for out-of-range, EBADF for other folders, plus a test. Held at the integrator.\n\nland: running-type 17b743f9 (readlink bounds-checked: 21/8/37 refusals, test appended; files+hello 24 ✓; growth 0; patch /Volumes/Worktrees/running-type/data/running-type.patch)\n\n17b743f9 reviewed by wap-supervisor: sound (offsets bounds-checked, EBADF, ENAMETOOLONG). The refusal test stays: sandbox safety is wanted behavior.\n\nFixed in [358f360e](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/358f360ea7a70a0cb6ace3b65598d727979891c8): merge running-type: a program reads a file through a link to an absolute path or through .. out of its folder; the native host answers path_readlink with POSIX readlink, every guest offset checked against the memory (user OK 2026-11-24 for the extension; wap-supervisor sound)\n\nland: running-type 70179d5f (run.wap 299 lines)\n\nFixed in [f896b0c9](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f896b0c901171fc95daae3810d693123809095b8): merge running-type: run.wap back under 300 lines (pure shrink)",
