   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiE-kYQ",
   "title": "wap format drops the colon of an enum's result…",
   "body": "Original title: wap format drops the colon of an enum's result type: enum nat: Type { zero } prints as enum nat {Type {zero}}, which reads differently\n\ncore/format.wap, owner wap-reader. The probe was `wap format` on fd664e77: `enum nat: Type { zero }` → `enum nat {Type {zero}}`, and `enum Equal(a: T): T -> Prop { refl: Equal(a, a) }` → `enum Equal(a: T) {T -> Prop {refl: Equal(a, a)}}`. `x: on k { a }` keeps its colon. The read tree is Key(nat, Colon, [Type, {zero}]) (explicit.wap before_cases).\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316450790\n\nbranch: format-enum-result-colon (2026-11-24)\n\ncac9170c reviewed by wap-supervisor: sound once a phrase led by a block word after the colon (for n in xs: if c {…}) still opens the block; test line for it. standing OK small fix.\n\nland: format-enum-result-colon 0d2155fa (handed to wap-integrator, patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/wap-reader/format-enum-result-colon.patch)\n\nFixed in [fcdf78cf](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/fcdf78cf6f0c5d888ccd1e88cb67e6ff32366517): test: the size ceiling is the measured 137695 after the as-narrows revert and the format fixes\n\nFixed in [4a676ab9](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/4a676ab9c13a09354919c34bfe11977eb86e28a7): merge format-enum-result-colon: a colon before a phrase ending in its own block types what precedes it, so enum nat: Type { zero } keeps its result type; a leading block word still opens a block (standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound)",
