   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiFD4vA",
   "title": "elaborator does not load the prelude, so a…",
   "body": "Original title: The elaborator does not load the prelude, so a program can't use nat, lists or the proved laws\n\nnotes/elaborate.md:32 says elaborate/door.wap loads wap/extensions/theory/prelude/; today only the kernel door (check.wap) reads it, so prelude proofs are written as explicit recursor terms (theory-prelude-divide). Once loaded, prelude proofs may use match. Shares door.wap with running-type (wap-fixer): rebase on it.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316456166\n\nbranch: elaborator-load (2026-11-24)\n\ninterviewer 2026-11-24: A decided without a user question (rare in real programs, extension only, 0 core, no test edits): a program's own declaration hides the prelude's for its later names, like a local name hides an outer one; consistent with the console's 'newest definition wins' (previous-line). ~10 lines in elaborate/declare.wap + read.wap.\n\nland: elaborator-load 2c394b21, handed to wap-integrator\n\n2c394b21 reviewed (diff-audit + wap-supervisor): shadowing sound. Back to worker: refuse missing --tree (no cwd fallback, door.wap:41); drop 'rules' claim (door.wap:2,22, read.wap:44); one TREE_OPTION (door.wap:23 + scripted.wap:92, shared with theory-traits-conditions); check.wap:15 ignores --tree; outcome test for hiding + missing tree.\n\nc16d77e0: fixes verified (options.wap door_arguments, loud NO_TREE, tests). Sound (wap-supervisor). land: elaborator-load c16d77e0",
