  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiFVoew",
   "title": "Main is red: theory door no longer compiles",
   "body": "Original title: Main is red: the theory door no longer compiles, so the second checker's and nested tests fail\n\nwap/extensions/theory/explicit.wap:238:33 `Number(value) => numeral(value as int)` refuses: 'this gives number, the name holds int'. test_theory_second and test_theory_nested red. Suspects (newest first): 84872bcd numbers-same-value (dispatcher result joins only choosable definitions), 67c56ece as-narrows. Reported by wap-fixer. Owner bisects; nobody else.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316474356\n\nbranch: red-theory (2026-11-24)\n\ncause as-narrows 67c56ece: path_key ignored a Set subject. Fix 6c6d6f43 (+1 core: Set(place, value) => path_key(place)) reviewed by wap-supervisor: sound, standing OK small fix.\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-simplifier: done: main reverted as-narrows (2405c796); the +1 path_key Set fix that lets as-narrows re-land is on branch red-theory 6c6d6f43, handed to wap-binding; left: nothing\n\nland: red-theory-reland 299974d9 (as-narrows again + path_key Set fix), handed to wap-integrator\n\nalso: a number literal of 2^63 or more crashes check.wap: explicit.wap:238 'numeral(value as int)' traps in int(x: float), wasm backtrace instead of a refusal. E.g. int.of_nat(18446744073709551616) in a door program (met by wap-reader on prelude-collections-rationals).\n\nFixed in [93cce38e](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/93cce38e87a791b7521df59c3c2617b767b2a416): fix: a condition finds the name it gives a value, so (given = value) is int reads given as an int in the then-arm and a number's as int is an int again\n\nFixed in [4952680e](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/4952680e332387ce735755aef43b0a8de9be85df): merge origin/main: the format fixes; the size ceiling is the measured 137921",
