  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiFze_A",
   "title": "nested block under nested container leaves helper…",
   "body": "Original title: A block nested under a container that is itself nested leaves the hidden helper type's name in its recursor's type\n\nIn wap/extensions/theory/second/nested.wap, `contained` turns an added family back into its container only one level deep. When the container is itself nested (e.g. a Rose inside a list inside another container), the recursor type still holds `Rose#1(...)`. Found by the advisor review of second-proof a7d9efe3; wap-supervisor asked for this card. Check whether the kernel's recursor shows the same.\n\nAdded by wap-fixer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316506042\n\nbranch: nested-twice-recursor (2026-11-24)\n\nland: nested-twice-recursor 60078695. The kernel shows no such leak: its at_container reads declarations already.\n\nsupervisor: 60078695 sound (advisor): added_for takes declared family/case types; plain block still fully checked (positivity, universes); independence intact; outcome test computes through Tree/Rose/list. Land.\n\nFixed in [711b2855](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/711b2855b6fcf61d591c5ed5e10f3a1892936737): merge nested-twice-recursor: the second checker reads a nested block's container cases from their declarations, so a block nested twice is accepted and its recursor computes (wap-supervisor sound)",
