   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiF6w1g",
   "title": "x ?? raise \"…\" is refused as a list instead of…",
   "body": "Original title: x ?? raise \"…\" is refused as a list instead of giving x's type\n\nFrom wap-simplifier: `t: text = given ?? raise \"none\"` (given: text?) → 'this gives list<any>, the name holds text'; `?? return` works. raise in value position should type as never, like return. Owner: wap-reader (core/analyze types) after its current card; a core fix ≤3 lines lands under the standing OK.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316512981\n\nbranch: nullish-raise-refusal (2026-11-24)\n\nsupervisor: 3a82315d sound (standing OK small fix): called_after_infix generalised from rule-leading words to any word, holes excluded; matches Footguns 'as an operand the call stays inside it'.\n\nstanding OK small fix; supervisor: sound; careful path green on a81fbb94 (hello, areas, test_self, census)\n\nland: nullish-raise-refusal a81fbb94\n\nFixed in [14f329a0](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/14f329a0c7e4fbdbd75897a6e3ffa26131b60087): merge nullish-raise-refusal: a braceless call after an infix operator is its right side, `x ?? raise \"none\"`, `1 + count xs` (wiki/Footguns.md; standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound)",
