  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiGskJg",
   "title": "definition like big := xs where it > 1 becomes a…",
   "body": "Original title: A definition like big := xs where it > 1 becomes a function instead of the filtered list\n\nFound by wap-simplifier. `big := xs where it > 1` is read as a function (implicit-it) instead of the filtered list. User via interviewer 2026-11-24: bug fix under the standing OK if ≤3 net core lines with the supervisor's sound. Related: implicit-it (242af35).\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316563625\n\nbranch: where-it-definition (2026-11-24)\n\nsupervisor: names-it-arguments a1a0d5de (wap-simplifier) sound, standing OK small fix: names_it stops at Fn, so it belongs to the innermost function.\n\nland: names-it-arguments a1a0d5de (supervisor: sound, standing OK small fix)\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-simplifier: done elsewhere: wap-simplifier's a1a0d5de is the same fix; nothing left; no branch\n\nFixed in [0fd0689c](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/0fd0689c5ddb196e656cfc5364e07e066a0fc334): merge names-it-arguments: an it inside a function value is that function's own, so `big := xs where it > 1` is a value (standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound)",
