  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiHjO7A",
   "title": "if b then bool.no else bool.yes loses its else…",
   "body": "Original title: if b then bool.no else bool.yes loses its else branch since the braceless-call fix\n\nMain red: 3a82315d (called_after_infix: not is_hole_word) makes the word after the infix '.' a braceless call, so 'bool.no else bool.yes' swallows else. Red: 4 choice lines in test/wap/test_theory_elaborate.wap. Fix (reader, standing OK ≤3): a word glued to the infix before it (access group) stays an operand. Reported by wap-binding.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316619768\n\nbranch: dot-word-braceless-call (2026-11-24)\n\nland: dot-word-braceless-call 744d6d3d (standing OK small fix, 1 net code line; test_theory_elaborate choice lines green, call/errors/operators unchanged)\n\nsupervisor: 744d6d3d sound (standing OK small fix, 1 line); pinned by test_theory_elaborate's choice lines; sent to integrator.\n\nAlso red from the same nullish change: test/wap/test_rules.wap comprehensions (y for x …). Side issue: test/test_rules.wap and test/wap/test_rules.wap share the log data/wap-tests/test_rules.wap.txt in run.sh, so one hides the other.\n\nland: dot-word-braceless-call 57868c71 (also fixes the comprehension regression of test/wap/test_rules.wap; test_rules, theory_elaborate, errors green)\n\nSupervisor: 57868c71 is sound. Standing OK small fix: glued_before and leads_block, +2 conditions.\n\nFixed in [77d48b41](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/77d48b414a0147042c9886805e2348e8465146f4): merge dot-word-braceless-call: a dotted word or comprehension before else is a value, not a braceless call, so `bool.no else …` reads again (standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound)",
