   "title": "test/test_matching.wap no longer compiles: value…",
   "body": "Original title: test/test_matching.wap no longer compiles: a value any holds is tested ... not this type (Prim boxed_test x1)\n\nRed on main with no card, reported by wap-reader: test/test_matching.wap fails to compile with 'a value any holds is tested for references and plain values, not this type: (Prim boxed_test x1)', on main compilers before match-inside.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316626945\n\nbranch: matching-boxed-test (2026-11-24)\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-reader: done: nothing; left: test/test_matching.wap fails to compile on main: 'a value any holds is tested for references and plain values, not this type: (Prim boxed_test x1)' (core/analyze/conditions.wap:133 boxed_tested); branch: none\n\nFixed in [87f43a68](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/87f43a6889c84baf338e4d44fe89980f816a759b): merge matching-boxed-test: a word taking a shape of Node exports no dispatcher, so kind(d: Duo) beside kind(n: Node) compiles again (standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound)",
