 "wap1-build-race": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLfmYc",
  "title": "Two test runs building the same compiler leave it…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T16:11:11Z",
  "key": "wap1-build-race",
  "agent": "wap-fixer",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T15:11:22Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T16:11:11Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiH5y7Q",
   "title": "Two test runs building the same compiler leave it…",
   "body": "Original title: Two test runs building the same compiler at once leave it broken for every later test\n\nReported by wap-emitter. test/wap/compile.sh folder_built writes each run's types.wasm into the tree's shared wap/types.wasm (library_module) and compiles wap1 against whatever is there, so two concurrent builds of one wap1-<hash> leave a wap1.wasm naming the other run's types module: 'wap: no module …/bin/wap-seed/types-<n>.wasm, as script.wasm names it'. Fix: build against the building folder's own types.wasm, copy into the tree after the mv. Also: two builds of the same source give types modules differing at byte ~53790 (building path embedded?): builds must be byte-identical.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316643719\n\nbranch: wap1-build-race (2026-11-24)\n\nfinding: a compiled module names the absolute paths of the source files it was compiled from (types/types.wap#97 in type names, file:line:col in messages), so builds in different folders differ. compile.sh now builds in the folder on relative paths (byte-identical wherever it runs). scripts/refresh-seed.sh still builds on absolute scratch paths and writes wap/types.wasm and wap/warm.packed into the tree directly: same fix applies there.\n\nland: wap1-build-race 9f3c9662\n\nland: wap1-build-race 9f3c9662 (patch: /Volumes/Worktrees/wap1-build-race/data/wap1-build-race.patch)\n\nFixed in [6b5fbd4d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/6b5fbd4dffe1293ab00289eeca8a20f8aadc6e7c): merge wap1-build-race: each compiler is built in its own folder from a copy of the source, so concurrent builds stay byte-identical (wap-supervisor sound)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": null,
   "subIssuesSummary": {
    "total": 0,
    "completed": 0
   },
   "type": "Issue"
  },
  "left_board": "2026-11-26"
 },
 "class-protocol": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLfxgk",
  "title": "A class with a signature without body is a…",
  "updated": "2026-11-24T18:33:35Z",
  "key": "class-protocol",
  "agent": "wap-binding",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T16:39:52Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T18:13:53Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiIEzOA",
   "title": "A class with a signature without body is a…",
   "body": "Original title: A class with a signature without body is a protocol: no constructor, structural conformance, laws as required words\n\nTopic dependent-types. User decision 2026-11-24 (via wap-interviewer): class and protocol are one form; required word = signature with no body; any required word ⇒ no constructor; conformance structural, ': Proto' a checked claim; law = required word returning a proof; trait a synonym; next(): (item: T, rest: Self)? pure. Cost ~7 core (calls.wap +6, Self +1), 3-4 sugar rules, ~5 theory. Fixes the Job bug (protocol_named at calls.wap:369). Planned owner: wap-binding after theory-operators.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316655113\n\nbranch: class-protocol (2026-11-24)\n\nJob bug reproduced (data/probe/job3.wap): `class Job { work: () -> int }; work(n: int) := n; run(j: Job) := 1; print(run(5))` prints 1 instead of refusing: protocol_named reads any all-function-field Record as a protocol, so 5 'conforms' via the free work(int). Plan: required word = body-less signature member written by the class/trait rule as a field typed with Self first (`area: (Self) -> any`); protocol_named keys on such fields; any required word drops the constructor. Paused for theory-sums audit fixes.\n\nland: class-protocol 6483c28c\n\nSupervisor audit 6483c28c: unsound. Crash at calls.wap:424 on an untyped parameter; a class with a data field accepted as a protocol; patterns.wap:98 changes lib/storage.warp's head reading; core keys on 'Self' by name; claim_checked special-cased in core. +16 net core against ~7 approved: shrink, then whatever is still over goes to the user.\n\nSupervisor re-audit 04f88e08: unsound. Core protocol test over-matches any record with a function field taking itself (plain classes change); the storage head reading is unverified; a misnamed test line. +14 net core. Next: core reads a sugar-written protocol fact; then the count goes to the user.\n\nSupervisor audit ce9a04b2: sound after fixes (default bodies dropped; crash on non-function @protocol field; meta fact merge in templates; META_RECORD copy). Decided by supervisor: PROTOCOL_ANNOTATION in core is the mechanism's own word; claim_checked scope accepted; patterns.wap $x: [$k] read as key, test_rules line is its spec. Net core +12 code / +19 with comments, goes to the user against ~7.\n\nSupervisor: 12b1d8fd sound. +9 net core code (approved ~7) asked to the user via interviewer, recommended land.\n\nInterviewer cleared +9 core; integrator told to land 12b1d8fd.\n\nland: class-protocol 9cee6655 — waits on the user's OK for +9 core (wap-supervisor sound)\n\n2026-11-24 interviewer: no explicit user yes for +9. User approved ~7; +9 decided by the interviewer under the user's standing rule (small matters within an estimate's margin are not user questions): the 2 extra lines are a general template-annotation fix that shrinks format.wap by 5. The user was told after the decision and has not objected. Land 9cee6655.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: land at +9 net core. Standing: the interviewer decides overruns of a few lines within an estimate's margin and logs them on the card.\n\nFixed in [159a9e67](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/159a9e678eb1a4594f91ee5387c3c296f3d91cc8): merge class-protocol: class and protocol are one form, a required word is a signature without a body, `: Proto` a checked claim (user decision 2026-11-24, +9 core cleared via wap-interviewer; wap-supervisor sound)\n\nFixed in [8e94959a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/8e94959a5d87d48226d1894010f70a5d5b534162): merge class-protocol at its tip 9cee6655 (user OK 2026-11-24 explicit, +9 core)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
