  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T17:13:55Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiIcuNg",
   "title": "type X = T with a condition, and the plan's char…",
   "body": "Original title: A type can be named for another type with a condition, type X = T, and the plan's char, vector and dot lines are still open\n\nRest of theory-subtypes (E4), released by wap-simplifier: the approved type sugar `type X(…) = T`; the plan lines char/vector/dot. The int(c) refusal is with wap-interviewer (it clashes with int(\"7\")). Follow-up: read.wap case_given's declaration(…)! should refuse, not trap.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316680202\n\nFrom wap-binding (theory-sums): convert (Subset to parent) fits Unit.unit at an open level against a wanted Sum and then refuses later with 'cannot find: the p of convert'. A conversion is accepted while a level hole is open.\n\nbranch: theory-subtypes-rest (2026-11-24)\n\nland: theory-subtypes-rest bd0128b9. Done: type X(…) = T sugar (spec: wiki/subtype.md, user OK); char lines (c, \"ab\" refused, shout(c) free), vector and index lines green through the door; a bool where a Prop is wanted is that it is yes (prelude/conversions.wap); yes/no read; case_given refuses; convert fits only when decided now (the open-level bug from theory-sums). Left red in test_theory_subtypes_wanted.wap: top-level c: char = \"a\" (the door reads only definitions at top level), initial's name#1 (text indexing with an index type: needs P3's arithmetic from #it > 0), dot (no .* and n not found from a list's length). Seen: show prints a list as list.item chains and a text literal as text_of(<number>), not [5, 6] and \"ab\"; in the main compiler test_alias_wanted now stops at 'type Bytes = list of byte' with an internal 'binding analysis reads only kernel forms' message (red before too, at line 4).\n\nSupervisor audit bd0128b9: sound after 5 fixes (sent). Global type-sugar output reaches scope.wap with an unlowered body; positional TRUTHS copies; the open_level test lacks a conversion; put_off compares counts; file.wap:48 merge with theory-sums becomes [operators, conversions, any].\n\nSupervisor sound adf66a55 + the scope.wap form_bound arm (2 core lines, standing OK small fix): a type with parts written as a value is refused in user words instead of the internal catch-all (x := list<byte>, print(list<byte>), type Bytes = list of byte).\n\nland: theory-subtypes-rest 7ee8c293 (supersedes bd0128b9: audit fixes and the scope.wap refusal). A type as a value in the main compiler (type Bytes = list of byte, x := list<byte>) is the work of test/test_alias_wanted.wap, now refused by name.\n\nFixed in [2ea47109](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/2ea47109c3784eae8e7742518b098c3f7b4b2a86): merge theory-subtypes-rest: the rest of E4, `type X(…) = T`, conditions in wap's operators, a type written as a value refused by name (wap-supervisor sound; scope.wap standing OK small fix)\n\nFixed in [02bcb700](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/02bcb700a1206e969b72e0fab8d79feea71843b3): test: the size ceiling is the measured 139896",
