   "title": "landing check 'wap/compiler.wap format' fails for…",
   "body": "Original title: The landing check 'wap/compiler.wap format' fails for every file, so no one can format wap code\n\nwarp --no-window wap/compiler.wap format <file> gives: No module, library or package named folder (warp looks for folder.warp). /Users/me/dev/bin/wap format <file> reads format as time's format. AGENTS.md Done asks for this check. Reported by wap-binding 2026-11-24.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316720523\n\nbranch: format-broken (2026-11-24)\n\nland: format-broken f44cc1da\n\nSupervisor sound f44cc1da: 7 lines in extensions/native, a command row and its driver line, following verify's pattern, plain wap, no new form. Bent rule: extension changes normally go to the user first. This one lands without that, because it only restores the landing check AGENTS.md Done already requires.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer: land (7 extension lines, 0 core)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (extension, 7 lines, 0 core) via wap-interviewer: land it. Also user OK: AGENTS.md line 246 becomes `wap format <file>` once that works on the installed binary (the interviewer edits it then).\n\nFixed in [a6abf88d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/a6abf88d00d275a51d88ee41d3ccf1443020e7e5): merge format-broken: `wap format <file.wap>` in the native wap runs the compiler module's format (user OK 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer; wap-supervisor sound)",
