   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T19:43:40Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiKXffw",
   "title": "A class that extends another class does not get…",
   "body": "Original title: A class that extends another class does not get its fields yet\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core ~15-25, spec: wiki/class.md) via wap-interviewer: option 1, a stage-2 declaration rule can read a declared class's members (core/rules/declared.wap): class $name extends $base {…} => class $name { $base's members…, $members… }. General mechanism, later used by a protocol's default fields and 'with the fields of Y' records. extends, < and : are one act (B is an A: A's fields and default methods, A's required words checked). The claim half already works on class-protocol (77fa9b7a). Measure on the branch; well above 25 core lines comes back to the user. Red lines: test_class_wanted extends / <. Measured by wap-binding.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316808370\n\noverlap 2026-11-24: native-function-values item 4 (wap-fixer, GC<->C converter) wants a compile-time 'fields of T'. Same need as this card's rule reading a declared class's members: one mechanism, shared; wap-fixer and wap-binding agree who writes it.\n\nplan (wap-binding): (1) a declaration hole $b: class, matched by a name declared as a Record (core/rules/matcher.wap hole_declaration), binds the Record declaration itself (Signature.record); (2) a declaration rule's output is shaped again by the stage-1 rules (core/rules/declared.wap), since the class sugar is stage 1 and its output (Record, constructor, methods) must come out; (3) sugar: rule class $name extends $base: class { $members... } => inherited $name $base [$members...]; rule inherited $name Record($b, [$fields...], $cases) [$members...] => class $name: $b { $fields..., $members... }; < and extends rewrite to the same; the claim (class-protocol) checks A's required words. Open: A's methods on a B and B fitting A-typed places need a conversion B->A at the call (test_class_wanted's conversion line), measured separately. Branch from class-protocol once it lands; est. core 6-10 lines.\n\nbranch: class-inheritance (2026-11-24)\n\nland: class-inheritance 8a6341a9 (after class-protocol 9cee6655). Step 1 is fields via extends / <. Left: B fitting A-typed places, A's methods on B, cross-module signatures after stage 2.\n\nSupervisor audit 8a6341a9: sound after fixes. ':' must be the same act (merge claim + inherit heads); base with cases refused; defaults inherited; redefined field replace-or-refuse; records#1 ambiguity refused; class hole READ_WITH; order-showing test. Net core +14 with comments (~+7 code).\n\nSupervisor audit 1d607f10: unsound — redeclare rule misses defaults/non-first fields (silent duplicate): replace by a general duplicate-field refusal; protocol by shape misreads plain classes: use @protocol fact; probe READ_WITH on name; run rules/records/sugar areas for stages.wap:296. Defaults inheritance → follow-up card.\n\nbranch class-inheritance tip d667c817 (merged origin/main 578bbee7); supervisor's 1-6 addressed, awaiting re-review; core net +25\n\nSupervisor re-audit d667c817: sound after small fixes — specificity comment (why @protocol rule wins), same_field helper for 4 copies, declared.wap paths one shape, wiki sentence for duplicate-field refusal via interviewer. Core net 25 (budget top).\n\ninterviewer 2026-11-24: class.md:46 approved: a class names each field once; B redeclaring a field of A is refused with a fix-it (rare; within the approved 25 core).\n\ninterviewer 2026-11-24: wiki/class.md:46 'a class names each field once' approved (wiki de268fb); the refusal names both fields and says rename or drop one. Core net +26 after the supervisor's same_name dedupe (one over 25, the helper line)\n\nSupervisor: 7b5cd1bd sound. Core +26 (1 over, same_name dedupe helper) → interviewer margin call.\n\nland: class-inheritance 7b5cd1bd\n\nFixed in [519b3c8d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/519b3c8d44d3cb8716dda7d5b36aa5db3eec3bd8): merge class-inheritance: `class B extends A {…}` and `class B < A {…}` take A's fields, then B's own, chains included (user OK option 1, 15–25 core; wap-supervisor sound)\n\nFixed in [eef509ad](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/eef509ad8e18ccd86fa93a20595c90c91b2ff5b7): test: the size ceiling is the measured 142094",
