  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-24T19:24:35Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiK7dBQ",
   "title": "A comma list after a definition should belong to…",
   "body": "Original title: A comma list after a definition should belong to its value: x := a, b means x := (a, b)\n\nUser decision 2026-11-24 (via wap-interviewer): a trailing comma list belongs to the definition's last part. Makes `a = 1, 2, 3` (wiki/multi-value.md), `theorem … by a, b` and `T ! IO, FFI` read as the wiki writes them. Core reader/shape-rule change, estimated 5-10 lines: measure; well above 10 goes back to the interviewer. Red today: test_theory_verify `by a, b`. Found by wap-theory-conditions-lifted.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316845473\n\nbranch: definition-comma-list (2026-11-24)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer, standing: small overrun. Approved 5-10, measured 13 code lines in core/parse/operators.wap (definition_row); accepted if the audit is sound, no form added.\n\nSupervisor audit 9eefed27: sound after fixes — per-definition grouping (bare items join the preceding definition; drop the any(defines) exemption), x := a+b, c is (a+b, c), += follows the same rule, rows_of name clash with format.wap:139, missing outcome lines, wiki line via interviewer. Interviewer accepted 13 (≤~15).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: 20 core code lines in core/parse/operators.wap plus 1 in the by reader, with general grouping (each definition opens a group). Interviewer: the multi-line enum line 'Warning = \"warn\", Hint' reading as a list is the rule itself (rare, no such line in the repo): no special case. Wiki 2f2dca9: drop the a = 1, b = 2, 3 example from the page (edge case); keep: x := 1, 2, 3 is a list too, the comma binds tighter than a definition.\n\nland: definition-comma-list 1bb200e0 (+ wiki 05854f3); user OK 20 core lines 2026-11-24\n\nSupervisor re-audit 1bb200e0: unsound — regroups x, y = 1, 2 and enum { Error, Warning = \"warn\", Hint } (test_enum_page:14, test_variants:37, wiki/enum.md). Fix: group only rows whose first item is a definition. Missing lines: x := a+b, c; T ! IO, FFI; by a, b; wiki line.\n\nSupervisor: 4d1289cd sound (grouping only when the row is led by a definition).\n\nland: definition-comma-list 4d1289cd (+ wiki 05854f3); supervisor sound\n\nFixed in [663e5439](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/663e543928e679fbeb620c62ce1a7735de4d2245): merge definition-comma-list: the comma binds tighter than a definition, `x := 1, 2, 3` a list, each definition of a row opening a group, `by a, b` and `T ! IO, FFI` taking the row (user OK 20 core 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer; wap-supervisor sound)\n\nFixed in [accf68f4](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/accf68f41c963288c6e08881d069f231a59eab09): test: the size ceiling is the measured 141668",
   "state": "CLOSED",
