  "column_since": "2026-11-24T22:11:51Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiLEALQ",
   "title": "A record handed to a C function crosses as the…",
   "body": "Original title: A record handed to a C function crosses as the struct C reads\n\nSupervisor-approved option A (0 core): extensions/c/foreign.wap rules for a class parameter on class-inheritance's declared-record hole ($b: class binds the Record), lib/foreign.wap c_record_offsets/c_record_bytes (4f35a36b). Memory build: record_address beside items_address (types/memory_lists.wap vs list_items.wap) to skip the copy; follow-up if it costs a rule. Test: mktime on a struct tm class. Blocked on class-inheritance step 1. branch: native-c-records (wap-fixer)\n\nAdded by wap-fixer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316853580\n\nbranch: native-c-records (2026-11-24)\n\nparked at 24eeb244: rules + lib helpers; blocked on 'a head's rules run at its latest stage' (core, to user via supervisor); probe data/probe/tm.wap\n\nSupervisor audit 7094d93f: unsound — written-order raise regresses data.wap key# (test_data:100), moves non-competing rules; trial within stage is specificity. Proposed: a rule waits for the stages of the MORE SPECIFIC rules of its head (probe first). Measure core vs class-inheritance tip. field_found dup.\n\nInterviewer accepted 2026-11-24 (within user's approval, ~5 core): a rule waits for the stages of the more specific rules of its head; most specific wins across stages; written order plays no part. notes/rules.md states it so; load-order question dropped.\n\nreview 709a6779: unsound. core net +10 mechanism (+16 branch) vs ~5 approved; typed rules: weight/general from unlowered pattern, matcher from lowered (stages.wap:107-126); waits_for computed twice + empty by_head keys (125-126); stale written-order comment c/foreign.wap:58; test_rules.wap:85 header cites notes not wiki/decision; uses: trailer names 2 files with no use; C-only move claim unproven (dump moved rules). Supervisor.\n\nuser OK (via interviewer) ~10 core for stage order + wiki/rule.md 'Which rule applies' (describe hello). Remaining review fixes 2-6 still required. Supervisor.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: stage order at ~10 core (approved ~5): the most specific rule of a head wins across stages, a general rule waits for the more specific ones. New wiki/rule.md passage approved, with describe hello in place of describe int.\n\nstage order by specificity: user OK 2026-11-24 (core, ~10 core lines) via wap-interviewer; wiki/rule.md 'Which rule applies' approved and on wiki master ddd075f; commit carries spec: wiki/rule.md\n\nuser 2026-11-24 (core/extension) via wap-interviewer: typed C, drop the mechanism. i32, i64, u32, f32, f64, handle … become real, distinct wap types (int32 and float32 exist); a from-lib declaration is an ordinary typed function; the crossing is chosen by overloads (c_passed(x: Tm) …) at typing; one catch-all overload keeps the list of types that cross; out, length and bytes<N> stay as rules. The stage-order mechanism (17 core, group_kept included) and the wiki/rule.md passage are withdrawn (the earlier ~10 OK is superseded).\n\nuser chose typed C (via interviewer): stage-order b4bcaac6 + wiki/rule.md passage withdrawn, must not land; integrator told; wap-fixer builds typed C on a fresh branch (~−22 lines). Supervisor.\n\nwap-fixer: typed-C estimate wrong (no class-generic overload, ~1400 lib spellings); 0-core alt (+12 ext: catch-alls enumerate spellings) sent to interviewer for user re-decision; probing on branch typed-c. Supervisor watch: the enumeration must be a library enum/list, not one rule per name.\n\nuser 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer (supersedes typed C now): the cheap fix. Explicit C spellings replace the catch-alls beside the class case in extensions/c/foreign.wap (0 core, ~+12 extension); an unknown C type gets the plain 'nothing defines' error. Typed C (real C types, crossing by overloads) waits for compile-time fields of T: card it.\n\nuser: cheap fix now: enumerated C spellings, 0 core, ~+12 ext (branch typed-c); typed C carded later as c-type-names. Supervisor.\n\ninterviewer 2026-11-24: typed-c's 1-line core fix in wap/core/rules/stages.wap (stage 2 opens a one-phrase round group as stage 1 does) is a standing OK small fix once wap-reviewer says sound.\n\nreview bea2d5bc (supervisor): sound after fixes — 1) restore a loud refusal listing the supported C types for an unknown one (foreign.wap:75 catch-all gone); 2) lib/foreign.wap: c_record_started repeats items_handed (210-212), c_field_next repeats c_record_offsets' placement — one name each; aligned/struct_bytes copy of core places.wap accepted (lib cannot call core; c-type-names fields of T removes it); 3) stages.wap:184 Round-only: make it hold for one-phrase Curly/Square too or say why not, and probe a phrase rewriting to a ; sequence inside ( ) (group_kept drops the bracket?); 4) 13 c_given_back lines accepted, missing named-list where noted on c-type-names; pre-existing: list<Tm> argument packs references (note on c-type-names).\n\nreview 2edabdea (supervisor): sound — core net +1 (Round+Curly open as stage 1, Square keeps items; ; sequence probed), lib copies named once, plain unknown-type error per the user's decision; standing OK small fix. Lands once native/rules/records are green.\n\nland: typed-c 7731393e (supersedes native-c-records b4bcaac6, kept as reference). standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound. Red: only test_native's record line, from the lib/foreign.wap relative-path bug (wap-binding).\n\nland: typed-c 18bac7db, native 59 passed, 0 failed (record line built natively via native_ran)",
