  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhsF6uw",
   "title": "class and enum rules write each type's show, text…",
   "body": "Original title: The class and enum rules write each type's show, text and number functions as generated code, where one library function over any record would do\n\nsugar/records.wap: class/enum rules emit show, text, ==(enum, text), int/index per type, through a private helper language (member_as, member_of, member_named, shown_case, spelled_case, case_valued). Library policy (how a value shows, enum == text) lives in a rewrite. Missing mechanism: a record's fields and cases readable by a types function (reflection), then show/text/int are plain generic functions in wap/types. Related: enum-index-constant-time. (warp-reviewer, architecture survey 11-23)\n\nAdded by wap-reviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314883534\n\nbranch: derived-words-library (2026-11-25)\n\nplan sent to wap-supervisor: part A (enum show/text/==/int/index as types functions over prims case_name, case_number, case_at; spelled names from the Record) after T1's prim table lands; part B (records) needs a compile-time loop over a type's fields, a missing mechanism; no code yet, branch derived-words-library at origin/main\n\nparked (supervisor): part A's prims case_name/case_number/case_at depend on the module's enum tags, so they come with T1b (emitter-layout-decisions), not T1's table; part B carded as record-fields-loop\n\nReleased 2026-11-25 by wap-theory-reads-types: parked: plan in the notes; part A waits for T1b, part B is card record-fields-loop; branch derived-words-library has no commits\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (core) via wap-interviewer: part A lands as built on branch derived-words-a: core emit +4, kernel 0, sugar/prelude -4 (net +4); one library show for plain enums, case->number constant time, number->case stays a search\n\nland: derived-words-a 0847c1e2 (part A, user OK 2026-11-25: emit +4, kernel 0; hello green, growth ok, enum/variant areas 73 ✓ + the 3 known wanted reds; patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/derived-words-library/derived-words-a.patch; wap format skipped: whole-file drift, carded format-spelling-drift)\n\npart A landed 73de761c (show by case name, case number by tag); later parts open\n\nFixed in [040bcce2](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/040bcce2882b0087d729929f5e0f5c5fff5b96a7): merge derived-words-a: a plain enum counts its cases by tag and shows them by name through the library, one show for plain enums (user 2026-11-25, core emit +4)",
