   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhwYwSg",
   "title": "A one-character text built at run time shows with…",
   "body": "Original title: A one-character text built at run time shows with double quotes, though char.md says it is a character\n\nchar.md:19: a one-character text is a character, ['a' \"bc\"]. Literals show so; texts built at run time don't (lib/xml.wap ['1','2']). Test from wap-lead: check(\"a one-character text built at run time shows as a character\", \"${[\"ab\".slice(0, 1), \"bc\"]}\", \"['a', \\\"bc\\\"]\"). Owner wap-reader (types).\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315144261\n\nbranch: char-show (2026-11-23)\n\nbranch char-show dd96982: show(t: text) gives '…' for one character (1 line). Held: test_lists.wap:126 and test_data.wap:57 pin \"a\" for one-char texts; asked wap-interviewer (A: char.md holds, tests change; B: page reworded, branch dropped).\n\nReleased 2026-11-23 by wap-reader: parked with one-char-literal (user decision pending); branch char-show dd96982 pushed, held unlanded\n\nobsolete: the user decided B, char.md reworded (wiki a6c83b0: texts print in double quotes whatever their length); main shows [\"a\", \"bc\"] for a run-time one-character text, as the page says. Branch char-show dd96982 dropped unlanded (for the supervisor's cleanup).\n\nFixed in [665da486](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/665da486287be000b5d9610bc89c7eedeb82a7ec): merge glue-any-module: a native executable links a C function from any module name, a library's path included (glue.awk reads wasm2c's whole alphabet through native_function; standing OK small fix, wap-supervisor sound); the GPU window's surface on Wayland and X11 (lib)",
