 "wap-host-bridge": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLMkrY",
  "title": "host words under wap cannot run",
  "updated": "2026-11-25T15:02:06Z",
  "key": "wap-host-bridge",
  "agent": "",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-24T08:19:07Z",
  "assignees": [],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T15:02:05Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh0MSiw",
   "title": "host words under wap cannot run",
   "body": "Original title: About 50 samples that use host words (sound, midi, gpu, images, webview, clipboard, drawing) cannot run under wap, because the host answers them in warp's value layout\n\nFrom wap-lead and wap-emitter's FFI costing: the ~50 'C type does not cross' samples are from-host words returning warp Node values (warp notes/native_host.md), not C gaps.\nOptions: (a) warp's driver answers a wap module's host imports in wap's value layout (warp side); (b) native_host ported to a wap library (lib/, with whatever extensions/native needs).\nSupervisor lean: (b): the focus is wap only (user 2026-11-22), and a library comes before compiler or host code. Needs costing first: lines in lib/ and extensions/native, plus what warp's side would cost for (a). The build waits for the user's extension OK.\nSeparate small C gaps: c_type int (~1 line), owned_text (~4 lines), freeing about 1 sample.\ndraw.warp:91 fails on && inside WGSL shader text: that is the shader text being read as wap, not a reason to write 'and'.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315396790\n\nCosted by wap-emitter. (a) about 3 wap + 100-200 warp lines, frees all ~50 samples. (b) about 3400 library + 50-80 extension lines, ≥2 sessions, plus a decision on C header constants. host-random and sleep need nothing (WASI). Sent to the user via wap-interviewer: (a) now, (b) later recommended.\n\nAlso blocks wiki/graphics.md entirely: use draw stops at c_type node (test_graphics_wanted red, from wap-wiki).\n\nUser decision 2026-11-23 (via wap-interviewer): C. A now: warp's driver converts wap values for the 31 host words (~3 wap + 100-200 warp lines). B later: the wap-library port of the native host. Every run of these samples is headless (warp --no-window): the user's no-window order.\n\nbranch: wap-host-bridge (2026-11-23)\n\nShape (wap-emitter): wap programs run on wap's own native driver, so the bridge is wap-side, with 0 warp lines. A from-host word's node args and results cross through the module's memory as kind+bytes (types/c.wap + extensions/c rules, ~20 lines). extensions/native links warp's native_host.wasm and its warp_runtime/warp/<m> imports lazily (~15), builds $Node values with native_host's new_* exports, calls host_<word> and reads the result back with item_count/int_item_at/shown_at (~35). ~70 lines in all. Every run headless.\n\nSuperseded 2026-11-23 by the user: no bridge into warp; warp's native host is ported to wap (host-port-extensions, -window, -gpu, -media).\n\nReleased 2026-11-23 by wap-emitter: superseded by the native host port (host-port-*); WIP on branch wap-host-bridge\n\nReleased 2026-11-23 by its agent: superseded by the user's decision to port warp's native host to wap (card host-port-extensions); WIP on branch wap-host-bridge 7f… : lazy C import resolution (host_words.wap, worth keeping for the port) and a memory crossing of host nodes (not needed now)\n\nRestarted on main as branch wap-host-bridge-main (old 386f2c18 superseded: its lazy C import is on main, its node crossing is not needed). Survey of the 57 host-library samples (native wap, tree compiler): every failure is in lib, none in core. (1) none of lib/host/native_host/*.wap compiles: run_option/windowless/muted undefined (the driver's run options; mine: --no-window, --muted told to programs like library_folder), gpu.wap memcpy source: cells<i32> (warp's crossing; wap: list<int32>). (2) the front libraries are still .warp: sound (19 samples), draw (18; its shader {…} WGSL read as wap: a shader(wgsl: raw) definition makes it raw, raw words carry across use), keys 5, image 4, shown_frames 2, pga_draw, graphics/math-in-shader samples. Order: run options, native_host compiles, then shown_frames+keys+shader, image, draw, sound.\n\nstep 1 done: 86f4082a on wap-host-bridge-main (wap --no-window/--muted told to programs; os run_option, windowless, muted; test_native green). Blocked next: native_host modules use c and os together, refused by 'both define' on identical from-'c' lines (hygiene's fresh c_value·N): wap-binding fixes it on branch identical-fresh.\n\nbranch wap-host-bridge-main tip fb27be13: run options told to programs (os windowless/muted/run_option); platform, sound, gpu, window compile under wap; webview stops at 'argument is function' (test_reflection_wanted.wap:30 is the to-do); C import signature clash asked at wap-interviewer (A refusal / B import per signature)\n\nbranch wap-host-bridge-main tip a5dfa03a: native_host modules compile (webview red on 'is function'); keys.wap + shown_frames.wap ported (frame event wires key presses); one-line analyze fix (no-value lambda fits (any)->any field) awaiting wap-reviewer. Next: shader word, image/draw/sound fronts.\n\ndraw.wap (CPU canvas, color's Picture; gpu.wap's Picture unified) at 4fa64a5b on wap-host-bridge-main; test_graphics green. Left: the GPU shape path and pixel_scale (draw.warp), image, sound fronts\n\nPaused (user order: dependent types first). Branch wap-host-bridge-main at d3d34262 (pushed), worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/emit-reds. Done: run options, native_host modules (webview red on `is function`), shown_frames + keys, draw.wap (CPU canvas), image.wap (image.warp removed; checked by probe: BMP/PNG/JPEG read by signature, flip/mirror/crop/tint/gray/blur, .bmp and .png saves). Known: a program calling any image() overload is red until jpeg.wap's `x not in xs` reads (test_jpeg_wanted). No image test: no wiki page shows image. Left: sound.warp port, draw's GPU shape path and pixel_scale, then landing checks + handoff.\n\nLanding blocked: on wap-host-bridge-land (4fa64a5b + origin/main, pushed) test_graphics is red in run.sh: the harness runs test programs without --no-window (run.sh lines 39-40), so show() takes the window path, and the tree-built native wap aborts with 'no C function wgpuCreateInstance … (wgpu_native)' instead of falling back to the PNG. Fix: (1) the native wap links wgpu_native, or picture_shown fails soft when it is missing (extensions/native, mine); (2) run.sh passes --no-window, once a seed refresh carries that option (the installed wap refuses it today). Rest green: test_hello, compiler-growth, native, events, os.\n\nSupervisor 2026-11-24: no soft failure. A native wap without wgpu refuses show() with a loud error naming what is missing (today's abort already names wgpu_native; keep it loud, give it the show() context), never a quiet skip to the PNG. So the fixes are: (1) the tree-built native wap links wgpu_native so show() opens its window; (2) run.sh passes --no-window after a seed refresh. Parked under the dependent-types pause.\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-emitter: done: run options, native_host modules, shown_frames+keys, draw.wap CPU canvas, image.wap; left: sound.warp port, draw's GPU shape path and pixel_scale, native wap linking wgpu_native, run.sh --no-window after a seed refresh; branch: wap-host-bridge-main d3d34262 (parked under the dependent-types pause)\n\nChecked 2026-11-25 (wap-annotation-attachment-fix): not done, not duplicated. host-port-extensions/-window/-gpu/-media are archived Done, but this card's own work, branch wap-host-bridge-main (tip d3d34262, 2026-11-24), never landed: 10 commits main has in no form (git cherry), +455 -157 lines: lib/draw.wap, image.wap, keys.wap, shown_frames.wap in plain wap (draw.warp, image.warp still warp on main), os run options (--no-window/--muted told to programs), native_host compile fixes, callbacks for webview, and core lines (analyze/modules.wap 6, rules/templates.wap 2, stage.wap 2, each claimed as a standing-OK small fix, to be reviewed). It conflicts with main now (in: test/wap/test_native.sh wap/extensions/native/driver.wap wap/extensions/native/main.c ). Left: merge main into wap-host-bridge-main and land it, which turns test_graphics_wanted's draw line green; then sound (19 samples, lib/sound.warp), webview's 'argument is function' (test_reflection_wanted.wap:30), and the C import signature clash question at wap-interviewer (A refusal / B one import per signature). Old branch wap-host-bridge (386f2c18) is superseded and can go.\n\nland: wap-host-bridge-main d80bbe05 — main merged (4b0e2a80), core/kernel/sugar identical to main so no core lines; run.sh runs tests with --no-window (91c5c700); handed to wap-integrator\n\nFixed in [bafe8bf5](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/bafe8bf5dfcd721d210c93fbee4fc8b9690b698d): merge wap-host-bridge-main: the host bridge's library words and the native wap's window bridge, whole",
   "state": "CLOSED",
