  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T18:35:55Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh08JQA",
   "title": "Running a program with wap can open a window or…",
   "body": "Original title: Running a program with wap can open a window or play sound, and wap has no option to run without them, so tests and sample runs can pop up windows\n\nUser (2026-11-23, urgent): no test or sample run may show a window. Found: the hourly coverage cron (scripts/coverage.sh) ran samples/graphics/raylib_circle, sdl_red_square and raylib_mouse_circle (60 s) through the installed wap and they opened windows; wap-wiki-lib's sample census did the same (its --no-window was refused: wap has no such option).\nStopgap: coverage-headless (f310333) skips samples by folder (graphics, gpu, sound), by imported module (raylib, SDL, draw, …) or by use of window.; wap-wiki-lib's census skips the same.\nWanted: wap --no-window (the warp spelling) in extensions/native: window, audio and input host and C calls run hidden or refuse loudly, so every harness passes it and the skip list goes. Extension change: needs the user's OK with its line count.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315441670\n\nbranch: wap-headless (2026-11-23)\n\nmeasured: windows/sound only come from C imports (raylib/SDL2/SDL3/glfw headers), linked in host_words.wap c_function_defined. Plan: --no-window option; linking refuses InitWindow, InitAudioDevice, SDL_CreateWindow(+AndRenderer), SDL_OpenAudioDevice, glfwCreateWindow loudly (warp's headless_checked); coverage.sh passes it, skip list goes. ~+15-20 lines in extensions/native: shape sent to wap-interviewer for the user's OK; build after it.\n\nuser OK via wap-interviewer: +15-20 in extensions/native, build as described\n\nland: wap-headless 9660c92 (feature 0521158; +18 net in extensions/native; test_native 41 ✓, test_hello ✓). Next: wap-headless-harness after the seed refresh (flag in coverage.sh and compile.sh, SHOWING_* gone).\n\nwap-headless-harness 3fd53fe ready (hello+native 50 ✓ through the changed harness); lands after the seed refresh\n\nfollow-up after landing (wap-lead): optioned() keeps the options it took for the host word run_options (wap-emitter's host-port-extensions hook); types/system.wap run_option(name): text? reads them (for window.wap windowless())\n\nrun_options contract with wap-emitter: run_options(): text from host, options as written one per line, \"\" for none\n\nparked by the user, skip lists suffice (2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: \"just skip them\"; the extension OK withdrawn). Branch wap-headless tip c2e8974 (e373d46 + TODO comments): --no-window by the options table, a link-time refusal of window/sound C imports, +33 in extensions/native, test_native 41 ✓. Branch wap-headless-harness 3fd53fe on top: the flag in compile.sh and coverage.sh, SHOWING_* dropped. The flag may come with the native host port (run_options contract agreed with wap-emitter).\n\nReleased 2026-11-23 by wap-fixer: done: nothing landed; parked by the user (skip lists suffice); left: --no-window with the host port; branch: wap-headless c2e8974, wap-headless-harness 3fd53fe\n\nwap-native: branch wap-headless-main b02a3cfc = wap-headless-harness 3fd53fe merged with today's main (conflicts in coverage.sh, run.wap resolved). Asked wap-interviewer whether the user re-approves --no-window (parked 2026-11-23); nothing lands without it.\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-native: done: wap-headless-harness merged with main as branch wap-headless-main b02a3cfc (hello ✓, test_native 44 ✓); left: user re-approval of --no-window asked via wap-interviewer (parked 2026-11-23, OK withdrawn); nothing lands without it, then a seed refresh before harnesses pass the flag; branch: wap-headless-main b02a3cfc\n\ntaken by wap-annotation-attachment-fix: wap-headless-main merged with main (32534eb9) — main's --no-window (run options, draw headless) joined with this branch's device-opener refusal, moved from link time to the opener's first call so window.wap programs run headless; run.sh's own --no-window dropped (compile.sh's wap carries it); extensions/native +22 vs main (user OK 2026-11-23 was ~15-20)\n\nland: wap-headless-main dc5e2aa4 (handed to wap-integrator; extensions +26 −4, overrun told to wap-interviewer)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 standing: small overrun (wap-interviewer): extensions/native +26 -4 (~+22 net) vs ~15-20 approved 2026-11-23; 0 core; refusal now at the first window/sound C call under --no-window; tip dc5e2aa4\n\nFixed in [70664a68](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/70664a68491972af6eac71448ce2fdeae7f6ccec): merge wap-headless-main: no test, coverage or sample run shows a window or opens a sound device; under --no-window a C call that opens one stops the run at its first call (user OK 2026-11-23; overrun accepted by wap-interviewer)",
