 "c-device-openers-in-bindings": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLNqGM",
  "title": "C functions that open a window or sound device…",
  "updated": "2026-11-25T19:29:18Z",
  "key": "c-device-openers-in-bindings",
  "agent": "wap-annotation-attachment-fix",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-25T17:56:38Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T18:51:20Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh1XTZw",
   "title": "C functions that open a window or sound device…",
   "body": "Original title: The C functions that open a window or a sound device are named in the native wap's driver instead of by the libraries that bind them\n\nwap/extensions/native/host_words.wap DEVICE_OPENERS lists raylib's, SDL's and GLFW's window and sound openers (InitWindow, SDL_CreateWindow, SDL_OpenAudioDeviceStream …) for --no-window's refusal. The names belong to the binding libraries (lib/native/raylib.warp, SDL2.warp, SDL3.warp): a mark on the C declaration, carried in the module's warp.c_functions line (wap/extensions/c/functions.wap has three fields left empty), read by the driver, which then knows no library's names. Needs a declaration mark (a compiler extension, the user's OK). Raised by wap-reviewer on wap-headless.\n\nAdded by wap-fixer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315467875\n\ndesign sent to wap-interviewer: an effect mark on the foreign line, `… from 'raylib' ! Device`, carried in a c_functions field, the driver's DEVICE_OPENERS gone (ext +3 −2, core 0); waits for the user's answer and for wap-headless-main to land\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (extensions+wiki) via wap-interviewer: A, the binding libraries mark openers '! Device'; Device joins effects.md (opens a window or sound device); extensions +3 -2, core 0\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (via wap-interviewer): A, the openers marked `! Device` in the binding libraries, Device in wiki/effects.md (\"opens a window or sound device\"); ext +3 −2, core 0; starts after wap-headless-main lands\n\nbranch: c-device-openers-in-bindings (2026-11-25)\n\nbranch c-device-openers-in-bindings 7ed tip a053a44e pushed, on wap-headless-main + library-port-native (both unlanded): openers marked ! Device in raylib/SDL2/SDL3; the mark rides on the import name (foreign.wap c_import_name), host_words reads it into a DEVICE_SLOT, DEVICE_OPENERS gone, glue drops marks; test_native line spelled with ! Device; wiki effects.md 216f585. native+c+graphics 89 ✓. Extension cost +9 −3 (approved +3 −2): the line reads 'raylib'! Device, so one rule regroups the mark with the library. Waits: both bases landing, then merge main and hand off.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (extensions+test) via wap-interviewer: a053a44e lands, extensions +9 -3 (net +6 vs +1 approved), core 0; test_native --no-window line marks InitWindow '! Device' (own commit)\n\nuser 2026-11-25: '@Device' annotation instead of '! Device' if it's easier on the parser (drops the grouping rule); worker measures and picks the smaller\n\ndecided 2026-11-25 (wap-interviewer, from the user's '@Device if easier'): @Device at equal cost (~4 rule lines, core 0); honest meaning, only native reads it; one line in c.md, nothing in effects.md; test_native follows\n\nmatcher: annotation holes (`@$mark`) would let foreign.wap carry any mark into the import; today @Device is matched literally\n\n@Device tried: an extension rule's annotation pattern is ignored (rule (@Device $name(…): $result from $library) after the plain rules never fires; first, it takes every foreign line, c.wap's calloc then 'does not lower'); in a program's own rules it holds. Attempt: /Volumes/Worktrees/c-device-openers/data/attempts/at-device.patch. Tip stays 800d7f8b with ! Device; recommended landing it (A), awaiting supervisor/interviewer.\n\ndecided 2026-11-25 (wap-interviewer): land '! Device' at 800d7f8b (user OK'd a053a44e; @Device was 'if easier', it isn't: the C extension ignores an annotation in a rule pattern, core/rules bug, own card; switch to @Device after)\n\nland: c-device-openers-in-bindings 7cb06f04 (merged main 9ac28a7a; growth, hello, native c graphics 89 ✓), ! Device kept; @Device after card extension-rule-annotations\n\nFixed in [310d3158](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/310d315824c7deecedc264d987d67f0e64fd3fd9): merge c-device-openers-in-bindings: a C function that opens a window or a sound device is marked so on its foreign line, `InitWindow(…): void from 'raylib' ! Device`; the native wap's own list of such names goes (user OK 2026-11-25, extensions net +6, 0 core)\n\nswitch to @Device covered by the user's preference (wap-interviewer 2026-11-25): extension-rule-annotations 43766281, core +1 standing OK small fix (supervisor: sound), +122 nodes",
   "state": "CLOSED",
