 "format-else-if": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLYtno",
  "title": "format breaks else-if chain over lines",
  "updated": "2026-11-25T23:00:00Z",
  "key": "format-else-if",
  "agent": "wap-annotation-attachment-fix",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-25T22:10:57Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T23:00:00Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiA-dng",
   "title": "format breaks else-if chain over lines",
   "body": "Original title: wap format breaks an else-if chain written over lines: the formatted code no longer compiles\n\nFound running format over lib/template.wap (fd03b599).\n```\nif x == 1 { print 1 }\nelse if x == 2 { print 2 }\nelse { print 3 }\n```\nformats as `if x == 1 {print 1}` / `else (if x == 2 {print 2})` / `else {print 3}`, which refuses: \"nothing defines this name: else\". On one line, `if a then 1 else if b then 2 else 3` becomes `… else (if b then 2 else 3)`: the meaning is right but the brackets are needless.\nOther needless rewrites from the same run, all in core/format.wap:\n- `x ?? return v` → `x ?? (return v)`: a prefix call as the last operand needs no brackets.\n- `t[a - 1 + #open:]` → `t[(a - 1 + #open): ø]`: an open-ended slice gains brackets and ø.\n- a one-line block `{ return x }` → `{return x}`: the house style is spaced 1491:1 in wap/ and lib/, while test_reader pins `{a b, c d}` for data braces. Which spacing a code block gets is a question for warp-interviewer.\nCorrect (the canonical word or the minimum brackets): `): T :=` → `) as T :=`, `0 upto n` → `0 .. n`, `(a and b) or c` → `a and b or c`, `print #\"x\"` → `print (#\"x\")` (spacing decided it), `'a'` → `\"a\"`.\n\nAdded by wap-lib-rules-audit with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316192378\n\nbranch: format-else-if (2026-11-25)\n\nbuilt: branch format-else-if 92001b00 (+7 core: stages.wap groupings_written groups as the walk does, lines.wap continued shared); native 64 ✓, rules, conditions, hello, growth green; asked user via wap-interviewer 2026-11-25\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (core) via wap-interviewer: +7 core (stages.wap +6, lines.wap +1), format groups as the rules' walk does; branch format-else-if 92001b00\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (+7 core) via wap-interviewer; land: format-else-if 92001b00 (handed to wap-integrator)\n\nFixed in [4a4885d5](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/4a4885d5771cce1240be9dd5a8d88e20cbffa071): merge format-else-if: wap format groups as the rules read, a phrase a rule fits whole as written and a continued line part of the phrase before, so an else-if chain over lines stays as written and compiles (user OK 2026-11-25 via wap-interviewer)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
