 "theory-run-terms": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLaL5g",
  "title": "Programs run from erased terms",
  "updated": "2026-11-25T05:30:05Z",
  "key": "theory-run-terms",
  "agent": "wap-fixer",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-25T00:28:49Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T05:30:04Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCZrEA",
   "title": "Programs run from erased terms",
   "body": "Milestone S2: erase, the lowering of run terms (a self call in last place to a loop, loop state to locals, exits to jumps), emit; every test program prints the same both ways. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316288920\n\nbranch: theory-run-terms (2026-11-25)\n\nmeasured 2026-11-25: the elaborator accepts 0 of 290 test programs whole (255 of 4726 statements; top refusals: `use` an unknown form (199), the check harness's calls, int/nat, map, float, Node). Plan sent to wap-supervisor: erase → lower to typed kernel forms → today's emitter, a terms door beside verify, a ratchet of programs printing the same both ways.\n\nPlan approved (wap-supervisor): stages erase.wap/run_terms.wap/lower.wap → kernel forms → today's emitter; ratchet gate n of N programs (accepted whole) print the same both ways; prelude-prim slice pulled from S4; unfolding theorem kernel-checked; door wap terms; order a numbers+calls+door, b tail loops+exits, c unfolding theorems, d ratchet line. Gap carded: theory-reads-use.\n\nHANDOVER (wap-fixer, 2026-11-25). Plan approved by wap-supervisor, four steps (a) to (d), each its own handoff, all in wap/extensions/theory/ (nothing in core or kernel):\n(a) run_terms.wap: an enum Variable/Global/Apply/Lambda/Let/Literal/Construct/Choose/Prim. erase.wap: accepted declarations to run terms, dropping types, proofs, levels and Prop arguments; a recursor or course application on a known enum becomes a Choose. lower.wap: run terms to typed kernel forms (wap/kernel/forms.wap) with the facts the emitter reads (TYPE, BINDING, DEFINER, SIGNATURE…, see core/emit), written from the terms' types, not by today's typing. Then core/emit emitted(Block, file…) to WasmModule and encode, both unchanged (see compiler.wap:78-81). The prelude prim table (numbers' shortcuts to int prims, text literals, print) is the slice pulled forward from S4 (noted on theory-host-layouts). The door is wap/extensions/theory/terms.wap, built into the seed folder like verify.wasm, with a `wap terms <program.wap>` row in native/commands.wap; name that row in (a)'s handoff. Then test/wap/test_theory_run.wap, its header naming coc-plan §S2 and wiki/function.md. Each line is compiled both ways and must give equal stdout and exit status: double(3) prints 6; a match prints its arm.\n(b) a self call in last place becomes a While over its parameters as locals; E5's exits become Return and Break. Outcome lines: a tail count to 10^6 without stack overflow; an early return; a break.\n(c) recursion.wap keeps the run body as a term over the constant, with the unfolding theorem f = body proved case by case (recursor, refl per arm) and checked by the kernel. Erase takes a body only with that theorem. Today run_bodies (read.wap) holds only Div bodies, as Nodes.\n(d) ratchet_census.sh --theory gains 'n of N programs print the same both ways', N being the programs the theory accepts whole.\nFINDING: the elaborator accepts 0 of 290 test/test_*.wap programs whole (255 of 4726 statements). The top refusal is `use` (199); card theory-reads-use holds that and the check-harness gap. So the first domain is the theory tests' inline programs (81 of them, inline strings in test/wap/test_theory*.wap) plus the new run tests.\nSTART: a worktree from origin/main once theory-census (c0bcae75, with wap-integrator) has landed. Begin with (a), and read core/stage.wap and core/emit for the exact facts first. Risk: those facts must match what today's typing writes; probe one Define (print a Numeral) end to end before building the general lowering.\n\nReleased 2026-11-25 by wap-fixer: done: plan approved, measured; left: (a)-(d), handover note; branch: none yet\n\nDesign (wap-supervisor): S2 lowers run terms to typed wap in kernel forms and today's compiler binds/types/emits it (no hand copy of emitter facts). Bridge only: before S3 (which removes analyze/) the emitter's facts are written from the term's types, one function per fact family.\n\nS2 bridge (wap-supervisor 2026-11-25): lower writes the run terms as plain typed wap and today's compiler (analyze/) binds, types and emits it; the door prints that program (run/door.wap). Before S3 the emitter's facts get written from the terms' types, one function per fact family, the one place (no second copy of typing). Slice 1: top-level pure expressions accepted by the elaborator (their value shown, as a script's), erase/lower/hosts/door, test_theory_run. Branch theory-run-terms.\n\nfound 11-25: run/door.wap failed to compile with use \"../environment.wap\" before use \"../elaborate/file.wap\" (bogus 'arguments are not of the parameters' types' at theory/bindings.wap:37 Binds(binding) => binding_declared); with the uses reordered it compiles. Also: a call of a local function given a wrong argument type is reported as 'named_variable is defined in core/analyze/variables.wap, which this file does not use' instead of the mismatch. Both compiler diagnostics, not yet reduced.\n\nland: theory-run-terms 85448ffa — slice (a): run door (wap/extensions/theory/run), top-level values kept by the elaborator (Theory.values, option 1 per wap-supervisor); normal path green on the merge: hello + 20 theory areas 342 ✓ 0 ✗, growth (spec: wiki/function.md). Next: (c) run bodies of recursions with their unfolding theorem; (b) tail calls loop already in today's emitter (return_call) on the bridge.\n\nAudit 85448ffa (wap-supervisor): sound after fixes. door keeps elaborator prints out; lower uses written_name for hidden names; erase.wap:109 index by course's type; hosts rows reached by a test or removed, duplicate spellings merged; dedupe erase refusal 89/110, stale lower comment.\n\nland: theory-run-terms 064e6959 — slices (a)+(b)+(c) with the review fixes of 85448ffa: run door, recursion by its body as written (<f>.unfolds proved; Div as written), computations in order, int minus/comparisons in the prelude, negative literals keep their sign (fraction refused). hello + 20 theory areas green (349 ✓ then test_theory_run 15 ✓), growth clean. Left: (d) ratchet line, native `wap terms` row.\n\nAudit 064e6959: sound-after-fixes (recursion path sound: total only with <f>.unfolds proved, Div opaque). Fixes before landing: (1) hosts.wap nat/recursor rows get test lines or go; (2) declare.wap:154 run_body_kept catches only refusals, re-raises the rest; (3) erase.wap refuses an empty Choose (lower.wap:30 .last crash); (4) UNFOLDS, NEGATION to file tops; (5) computed for every statement is intended (reads-use step 2), keep it, confirm check/verify refusal tests green; (6) self-calls bind to d itself, not by name through declarations_named (overload could give a wrong run term). (wap-supervisor)\n\nland: theory-run-terms 560cf7e0 — audit of 064e6959 fixed: (1) every host case row is reached by a test (bool by truths/compare, int and nat by sign/early/larger: removing either set turned those red), so all stay; (2) run_body_kept keeps only refusals, re-raises the rest; (3) a recursor over no cases refused in erase; (4) UNFOLDS and NEGATION at the file tops; (5) computed for every statement kept, check/verify tests green; (6) a body read as written calls its own declaration (Elaborating.itself → declared_given(d.name)), never an overload by name; (+) tested.wap imports no prove/ file: Equation/equation_of/is_equality moved beside equality_checked in inductive.wap. Contains fc8fb9b0 (theory-arithmetic-linear) merged. Normal path: hello ✓, 22 theory areas + proof_page 353 ✓ 0 ✗, growth ✓. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/theory-run-terms/theory-run-terms-560cf7e0.patch (diff over fc8fb9b0)\n\nRe-audit 560cf7e0: sound (wap-supervisor). Host rows kept on the worker's row-removal evidence; tested.wap imports no prove/ file (Equation moved to inductive.wap), accepted. Forward on theory-wanted-reds: one helper for the REFUSED re-raise (read.wap:379, declare.wap:158, effects.wap:223).\n\nFloor 1426→1395 OK'd by wap-supervisor (b737d2fc): 48 lost were wrong values on main (fractions truncated, hex past 2^63, -1 - x), 18 gained. b9ecd0cb (function into a computation is a value) sound.\n\nland: theory-run-terms b737d2fc — merge with main 891a59f0; b9ecd0cb fixes the census crash 'no item at this place' (is_computation looked through binders: `: never`); b737d2fc floor 1426→1395 (45 fraction statements, 2 wrapped hex constants in lib/hash.wap, 1 `-1 - x`, 1 lib/time.wap, each one main accepted with a wrong value; 18 gained). Left: embedded() of 10–100 KB files crashes the elaborator (wap/compiler.wap WARM_STATE, LIBRARY).\n\nreview 81e3bd83: sound (wap-supervisor): checker copies its levels, 1 line; lands after theory-reads-use\n\nreview a9ab0da4: sound (wap-supervisor): checker's depth budget only adds a refusal, deterministic; floor 1464 OK\n\nFixed in [a7a895d3](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/a7a895d3d5343f0745ae79838e6746921fea65b0): merge theory-run-terms: the run door writes a program the theory accepts as plain typed wap from its erased terms, a function calling itself runs by its body, a negative literal keeps its sign, the checker gives up past a depth budget (S2 slices a-c; wap-supervisor sound, floor OK)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
