 "theory-host-layouts": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLaMZ8",
  "title": "The prelude's types run by their host layouts",
  "updated": "2026-11-25T09:35:25Z",
  "key": "theory-host-layouts",
  "agent": "",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-25T09:05:02Z",
  "assignees": [],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T09:35:24Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCaPrQ",
   "title": "The prelude's types run by their host layouts",
   "body": "Milestone S4 (plan 9.7): run bodies for constructors and case analysis, so nat runs as a number and a text as its bytes. plan: notes/coc-plan.md (branch coc-plan until it lands); the files and what each gives the others: notes/theory.md.\n\nAdded by wap-coc-plan with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316289439\n\nS2 (theory-run-terms) pulls forward the smallest slice: a prelude table of prim bodies for the types the accepted programs use (numbers' shortcuts to int prims, text literals, print); S4 starts from it.\n\nbranch: theory-host-layouts (2026-11-25)\n\n(wap-supervisor) layouts are @runs annotations on the prelude declarations (it = the case's value, params by name), read via annotation(); run bodies typed at the layout type, listed in notes/theory.md as the run trust base; hosts.wap goes\n\ndecision (wap-supervisor, 2026-11-25): a layout is an @runs annotation on the prelude declaration it is about, plain wap, parameters by name, a case's value `it`: @runs(int) enum nat { @runs(it == 0) zero, @runs(it > 0, it - 1) successor(n: nat) }, @runs(m + n) add(m, n). hosts.wap goes. A run body is trusted (erase believes it): keep @runs few, listed once in notes/theory.md as the run trust base beside the kernel's. A run body is type-checked against the layout types (nat's field as int), not the declaration's own type.\n\nland: theory-host-layouts 9f8423a3 (slice 1: layouts as runs(...) statements in the prelude, checked over host types; hosts.wap gone; trust base in notes/theory.md). Left for slice 2: list layout (needs theory list indexing/slicing for the case fields' check, or fields checked under the case's test as a subtype), text layout (text literal: text_of(numeral) decoded to a wap text literal via the texts binding; text + is an overload runs() cannot name yet), the prelude's laws run on values (S4 outcome).\n\naudit 9f8423a3 (wap-supervisor): not sound yet: a program's own runs() must be refused (trust base is prelude-only) + test; tests for an ill-typed run body and a running lambda; dedupe host_type/host_spelled and binders_of/binder_names; copy layouts in held; core numstat empty\n\nland: theory-host-layouts d718c96a (slice 1 + review fixes bc033ac0; replaces 9f8423a3). Slice 2 (list/text layouts) next.\n\nreview d718c96a: sound (wap-supervisor); landing. 4 findings fixed forward on slice 2: check door ignores program runs() silently; type layouts unchecked (file.wap:157) + shown_for default; misplaced comment read.wap:190; host_type belongs in run/, $k filled with empty.\n\nslice 1 landed 699c6238 (d718c96a); 4 audit findings fixed forward in slice 2\n\nland: theory-host-layouts-2 60b56c9b (second review's fixes; slice 1 landed in 699c6238). Slice 2 (list/text layouts) next.\n\nreview 60b56c9b (layouts-2): sound (wap-supervisor). Accepted: layouts checked at run door only, explicit shown_for in check, prelude(\"logic\") helper. Slice 2 adds: run-door test refusing program runs(), test header fix, drop/refuse ?? \"\" at erase.wap:234.\n\nslice 2 landed 7e3dca5d (theory-host-layouts-2 60b56c9b: layouts checked where they run, runs(…) refused in programs, type layouts checked). Leftovers: 3 small items from wap-supervisor's review go into the next slice.\n\n(wap-supervisor) slice 2: host spellings are typed by wap's own typer against the types module at the layout type (A), not modelled by the theory's same-named nat words; meaning match stays trusted, listed per layout in notes/theory.md. Core cost 0.\n\nReleased 2026-11-25 by wap-fixer: done: slice 1 (landed 699c6238, 60b56c9b); slice 2 handed to integrator as land: theory-host-layouts-2 202c7f26 — linear prover a > b (beyond_at_most), xs#i/text#i in the theory (Get with a non-text key calls #, item_at with range proof), arguments aimed at the wanted type after a hole, list/count/item_at/drop/joined/mapped/Subset layouts, projection erase, layouts typed by wap's own typer at the run door, lazy filled; census 2175. left: superseded by the approved prelude/wap-types merge (no more layout machinery); gaps seen: an if's condition is no fact in its branches (if #xs > 0 then xs#1 refused, though the refusal says 'test it with if first'); a list literal given straight to a subset parameter (first_of([7, 8])) reads its items as nats; text layouts (literal decode, text +) not done. branch: theory-host-layouts-2\n\nland: theory-host-layouts-2 202c7f26\n\nslice 2 202c7f26: wap-supervisor sound (diff-audit). Fix-forward nits: erase.wap:70-71 projected copies the lookup-or-refuse at :172 (one helper); erase.wap:266 layouts_checked's language parameter is dead; test/results.txt churn dropped at landing. Open gaps from the worker: an if's condition is no fact in its branches (match carrying Equal(bool,tested,yes)); list literal to a subset parameter reads nats (aim doesn't see through subset to carrier); text layouts. Audit 2026-11-25 R1.2 replaces the spelling check (491763c9) with run bodies as primitives: rewrite plan.\n\nslice 2 landed 6750bc45 (202c7f26: a > b in the linear prover, xs#i, arguments against the expected type, lists run as wap's lists, lazy filled, run door refuses runs(…))",
