  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T23:20:06Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCcLEw",
   "title": "format writes a result type as `as B` where…",
   "body": "Original title: wap format writes a result type as `as B` where the canonical spelling is `: B`\n\nUser decision 2026-11-24 (via wap-interviewer, card coc-plan): f(x: A): B is canonical, f(x: A) as B the alias. format should keep : B and turn as B into : B with a got-it note (canonical-output). Owner wap-reader (core/format.wap).\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316291220\n\nfound while formatting wap/extensions/theory: (1) `wap/compiler.wap format` aborts on wap/extensions/theory/show.wap and explicit.wap with 'this list has no item at this place'; (2) `if x is not ø {…}` is formatted `if x is (not ø) {…}`, which reads differently; (3) `{ f(x) }` loses its inner spaces.\n\nwiki/function.md:148 still says `wap fix` writes `as` for a result type, and wiki/as.md:16-21 shows `as int :=` as the example form: both follow the decision once format writes `: B` (wiki rewrite via the interviewer).\n\nbranch: format-colon-result (2026-11-25)\n\nwiki rewrites function.md:148 and as.md:15-16 to ': B' canonical, 'as B' alias: covered by the user's decision 2026-11-24 (wap-interviewer 2026-11-25), meaning unchanged\n\nseen: error texts still write a result type with as (core/bindings.wap RESULT_WORD = \"as\", used by calls.wap candidates_text: 'slice(t: text, r: Range) as text'); canonical-output wants ':'. Not changed on this branch.\n\nland: format-colon-result a9a7b671 (handed to wap-integrator; standing OK small fix, supervisor sound); wiki e0bfc39\n\nFixed in [7d05a190](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/7d05a1902a50102fc00794e874e37bd114aee0d4): merge format-colon-result: wap format writes a definition's result type after a colon, the canonical spelling (`f(x) as int` becomes `f(x): int`) (standing OK small fix, core/format.wap net −3, wap-supervisor sound)",
