  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiC23Ng",
   "title": "wap's formatter cannot run in a worktree",
   "body": "Original title: wap's formatter cannot run in a worktree, so branches land unformatted\n\nTwo ways in, both fail in /Volumes/Worktrees/<card>: (1) `warp --no-window wap/compiler.wap format <file>` stops with 'cannot read wap/warm.packed' (the file is ignored, so cowtree does not clone it); (2) the installed `wap format <file>` treats 'format' as a program word ('several functions have this name: format', the time library's format). theory-recursors 1a00016b landed unformatted because of this. Related: format-outside-tree.\n\nAdded by wap-emitter with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316317927\n\nbranch: format-in-worktree (2026-11-25)\n\nchecked on main 665da486: 'wap format <file>' works in a fresh cowtree (installed wap and the tree's), so the format-vs-time-library clash is gone. Still red: compiling with wap/compiler.wap from source in a fresh tree, 'cannot read wap/warm.packed' (embedded of an ignored built file). Asked the user via wap-interviewer: A, embedded of a missing file is ø, compiler.wap writes ?? \"\" (+1 core); B, leave it.\n\ndecided 2026-11-25 (wap-interviewer, rare dev path, 0 core): B, running wap/compiler.wap from source in a fresh tree stays unsupported; card closes as fixed (format works)\n\nuser decision B 2026-11-25 (via wap-interviewer): running wap/compiler.wap from source in a fresh tree stays unsupported, 0 core; wap format works in worktrees on main 665da486",
   "state": "CLOSED",
