 "theory-reads-use": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLoKaE",
  "title": "new stages cannot read use lines or check harness",
  "updated": "2026-11-25T08:12:35Z",
  "key": "theory-reads-use",
  "agent": "wap-theory-conditions-lifted",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-25T01:02:10Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T04:18:04Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiQv3AQ",
   "title": "new stages cannot read use lines or check harness",
   "body": "Original title: The new stages cannot read use lines or the check harness, so no test program is accepted whole\n\nFound by wap-fixer planning theory-run-terms: 0 of 290 test/test_*.wap accepted whole (255/4726 statements); top refusals: use \"check.wap\" (199), the check(...) calls, then int/nat mismatches, map, float, Node. Reading use (the program's modules elaborated in order) unlocks S2's ratchet domain and S1's census.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317204897\n\nbranch: theory-reads-use (2026-11-25)\n\nShape approved (wap-supervisor): modules via core modules_used, prelude→modules→program; expression statements (general rule, wiki/program.md) as own early handoff, used by theory-run-terms; census counts own statements, check.wap added, theory cached per module prefix.\n\nStep 2 builds on theory-run-terms be82a5c2 (Theory.values, computed/asked in declare.wap); one list of value terms.\n\nOwns the red census time line on main (aa8e9f46): theory census 1303 s vs typing 140 s, ratio 10 > 3 (count fine, 1522/11067). Cause: prelude re-checked per program; this card's once-per-census prelude and module-prefix cache fix it. Land with the ratio ≤ 3 measured on an unloaded run. (wap-supervisor)\n\nfound 11-25 (wap-fixer): `larger(a: int, b: int): int := if a > b then a else b` is refused by the elaborator: 'refused by not a function: _2 is a int, no function, and is given then' (also `if 2 > b then 1 else 0`). These read fine: `if b > 2 then 1 else 0`, `if (a > b) then a else b`, `if a > b { a } else { b }`. A comparison whose right side is a name, right before `then`, is read as a call of that name.\n\nAudit e8188e92: sound-after-fixes (wap-supervisor): source_key folder binding, lib link in ratchet_census.sh, census.making cleared on a refusal, cycle comment (core refuses cycles on read), one helper for the modules_used reader closure; census rerun.\n\nland: theory-reads-use 400cd868 (steps 1+3: modules read, census per-module theories + lib; census 1495, ratio ~1.7); step 2 (check/print effects) next on top of theory-run-terms\n\n400cd868 (steps 1+3): sound (wap-supervisor). Lib linked for real, 1495/11068, ratio 1.7; a cycle core cuts is guarded by census.making. Lands after theory-run-terms. Step 2 next.\n\nFixed in [0ef18a0f](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/0ef18a0fdfbc0f63d6f9cdda04be527d882fdca0): merge theory-reads-use: the theory's door elaborates a program's used modules first, each once, the census making each module's theory once (wap-supervisor sound)\n\nstep 1 landed 0ef18a0f. Step 2 (wap-supervisor): the theory reads the types module before every program, one cached module of modules_of (made once per census and copied per program); print, show, == and text come from its declarations, no special case\n\ndecision (wap-supervisor): the theory reads the types module before every program, as the compiler does: one more module in the modules_of cache, made once per census; print/show/==/text come from its own declarations, no special cases; words it can't elaborate are refused like any module's\n\ndecisions (wap-supervisor, step 2): A) the types module is a module like any: a program that names a types word reads it, cached; refused types statements taken back, a word that hits one refused as 'declared in <file>, which the theory refused: <reason>', never unknown name. B) a prim body is the host's: an opaque constant of its declared type, only at a data or computation type; a prim at a proposition is refused. Branch theory-reads-types.\n\nland: theory-reads-types 24b4cf31 (step 2: the types module read through the names a program uses, prims as constants, prelude reading wins on equal signatures, overloads by type place/whole call/specific; theory areas = main's reds minus 4, census 2327 accepted, ratio 2.8)\n\nland: theory-reads-types 1657a9e8 — supervisor's 7 audit fixes done + literal at its place's type (abs(0 - 3) → 3) + main's layouts merged (hosted spellings are Layouts now). Checks on the merged tip: theory areas 370✓/9✗, all 9 main's wanted reds; test_hello green; growth OK; census 2322 accepted (floor 2168), ratio 2.39. Open: print stays refused until the compiler accepts `write(…) := prim … ! IO` (red line in test/test_effects_wanted.wap). State: handed off, session retiring; after landing remove /Volumes/Worktrees/theory-reads-types.",
   "state": "CLOSED",
