   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiU1QLg",
   "title": "seed refresh refuses a sound seed when the…",
   "body": "Original title: The seed refresh refuses a sound seed when the machine is busy, because its timing gate swings with load\n\nscripts/refresh-seed.sh compares CPU time of the new compiler and the seed (150% gate). The same source measured 112% and 147% an hour apart (nightly 2x inflated): niced jobs land on efficiency cores. Fix: time A and C interleaved, best of 2. Found by wap-seed-refresh 2026-11-25.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317464632\n\nbranch: seed-refresh-refusal (2026-11-25)\n\nland: seed-refresh-refusal 6b0c3772 (express: hello ✓ growth ✓; --check under full load: 117% < 150%). Then the seed refresh on main.\n\nFixed in [f1eb883e](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f1eb883e69848164c3776b5723eda8400229c7a8): merge seed-refresh-refusal: refresh-seed times the seed and the last stage's compiler in turns, each by its best round",
