   "title": "emitter finds a primitive through seven tables…",
   "body": "Original title: The emitter finds a primitive through seven tables instead of one\n\naudit 2026-11-25 More general 1: core/emit/primitives.wap:61-85 (+ emitter.wap:169). One kernel/primitives.wap row per operation (name, wasm in/out, builder); primitive_code one lookup. ~-20 lines (pure shrink). Also the base of rewrite-plan step 'run bodies as primitives'. notes/audit/2026-11-25.md\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317648145\n\nbranch: primitive-lookup-tables (2026-11-25)\n\nbranch primitive-lookup-tables: step 1 @shown annotation for Prim(shown) committed (-32 nodes). Plan after advisor: kernel/primitives.wap holds the fixed-signature host ops (mnemonics, memory ops, WASI) in one map with wasm types; emitter's own ops (box, cast, typed helpers, helpers, item.*, text ops) keep the if chain; theory runs(...) prim bodies checked against rows. Size baseline 142947 = ceiling.\n\nbranch primitive-lookup-tables pushed: kernel/primitives.wap table + emitter lookup, theory number/bool layouts as prims checked against rows, native dedupe (primitive-operation-declaration). +85 nodes over ceiling 143077: waiting for supervisor's call. @shown annotation reverted (typing drops a call's facts). Careful path running.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (kernel+core) via wap-interviewer: land T1 one table of primitives (kernel +48 + moved opcodes, core -27 net; ~+21 vs plan -20, accepted)\n\nland: primitive-lookup-tables e5874302 (handed to wap-integrator; kernel +48, core -27 net, +147 nodes, ceiling 143253)\n\nFixed in [3f95fa00](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/3f95fa008f98f86a3777a0f5a371e131ec444277): merge primitive-lookup-tables: plan step T1, one kernel table of the host's operations, primitive_code one lookup (user OK 2026-11-25, wap-supervisor reviewed)",
