   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiYUMnA",
   "title": "leading annotation does not attach to operated…",
   "body": "Original title: A leading annotation like @runs does not attach to operated code or to an enum.\n\nUser OK 2026-11-25 via wap-interviewer: a leading @annotation belongs to the whole phrase it leads, about 5 core lines in wap/core/parse/cascade.wap (audit R1.9). Recorded in notes/coc-plan.md 13 on elaborator-replaces.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317694071\n\nbranch: annotation-attachment-fix (2026-11-25)\n\nland: annotation-attachment-fix f6c224d4 (careful path green: hello, growth, rules+protocols 48/48, test_self; census green but the size ceiling raised to the measured 143077 in its own commit, +105 nodes; main was 142972, already over 142947). Core: 5 net code lines in wap/core/parse/cascade.wap (phrase_annotated; a key's value read the same way). A rule asks for a phrase's annotation with its pattern in brackets: rule (@twice $a + $b) => …; unbracketed, the annotation stays on $a, as everywhere inside a phrase.\n\nreview (supervisor): sound. index_where is 1-based (0 = none), so led counts the leading annotations; the diff-audit's off-by-one claim does not hold. 5 net core lines, within the estimate; census +130 accepted.\n\nFixed in [f9ce07db](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f9ce07db90d2280ddb9c7d9a188cadf5c99f89e9): Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into HEAD",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
