  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiYUjIA",
   "title": "int wraps at 64 bits, but int is unbounded whole…",
   "body": "Original title: The number page says int wraps at 64 bits, but int is now the unbounded whole numbers.\n\nUser decision 2026-11-25 (coc-plan 13, branch elaborator-replaces 8604774a): int unbounded and exact, storage picked by context; nat = int where it >= 0; i32/i64 wrapping words; numerals int; #xs - 1 is -1; until storage by context lands, compiled int wraps silently. wiki/number.md is rewritten to say so; the old and new text go to wap-interviewer first.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317694418\n\nbranch: int-overflow-semantics (2026-11-25)\n\nWaiting for the user's OK via wap-interviewer (old/new text sent). wiki branch int-overflow-semantics a1f5ef7 (number.md, 2 passages); wap branch int-overflow-semantics c34c2120 (2 green page lines, 4 red wanted lines). Contradicting test left for the user: test_type_inference_wanted.wap:5 expects nat.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (wiki) via wap-interviewer: number.md rewrite approved as written (wiki a1f5ef7, tests c34c2120); test_type_inference_wanted.wap:5 'nat' → 'int' approved with it\n\nFixed in [f6fec5c1](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f6fec5c1daab320f61d117b3935101ff8624f529): merge int-overflow-semantics: int is the unbounded whole numbers, a numeral is an int, i64 wraps (user 2026-11-25, wiki/number.md)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
