  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiYyLCQ",
   "title": "Tests that start a process fail on Linux",
   "body": "Original title: Tests that start a process fail on Linux because lib/process.wap uses a macOS-only call.\n\naudit 2026-11-25-3: lib/process.wap:45 uses _NSGetEnviron (macOS only); every test driver fails in the cloud run, 63 of the 170 ✗ in test/results.txt.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317724893\n\nbranch: tests-start (2026-11-25)\n\nland: tests-start e77049b7 (express green + test_process 11/11 on the Mac). lib/process.wap calls process_environment (lib/native/system.h: returns environ; moved there from foreign.c, which wap's native host never included). Takes effect in the cloud only when its native wap is rebuilt from the tree (the cloud says 'no wasm2c: the installed wap runs the modules'). Left: compare test/reds.txt with the next Linux run; Linux-only reds then get one marked baseline.\n\nland: tests-start 617817c0: test/reds.txt joined (Mac f9ce07db + Linux 625564b8): 177 shared, 5 [Darwin], 13 [Linux]; run.sh reads shared + own system's, --known rewrites only this system's view.",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": {
    "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhvmgew",
