   "body": "Original title: One test command shows a regression apart from the tests already known red.\n\naudits 2026-11-25-2 (R3) and -3 (rewrite 1) both: wap test in the native driver runs every test in one process, a fresh compiler instance per test, against a baseline of expected reds; results passed/wanted/skipped(missing host feature)/failed. compile.sh, run.sh, scripted.wap (328 lines) become one ~150-line command; 143 driver checks become test-program checks. Low risk. Touches extensions/native (user OK needed for the extension part).\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317725249\n\nbranch: test-regression-known (2026-11-25)\n\nland: test-regression-known fd29a40e (express: hello + growth green). run.sh compares reds with test/reds.txt (182 reds, full run at f9ce07db on the Mac), names regressions and fixed checks, exit status by regressions only; --known records. Left on the card: the native 'wap test' runner (extensions/native, needs the user's OK).\n\nland: test-regression-known fd29a40e. The native 'wap test' runner part is dropped for now: run.sh is the one command; a native runner is an extension change and would need the user's OK, not worth it during track T.\n\nrun.sh baseline slice landed cb4f3e01 (fd29a40e); the one-command native test driver is still to come",
