 "one-environment-per-module": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhL1_ro",
  "title": "Each module is read with its own environment, so…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T03:28:04Z",
  "key": "one-environment-per-module",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-25T16:28:31Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T03:28:04Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiev6uQ",
   "title": "Each module is read with its own environment, so…",
   "body": "Original title: Each module is read with its own environment, so a declaration applies only from where it is written and in the files that use it\n\nStep TM of notes/coc-plan.md (user 2026-11-25, notes/audit/2026-11-25-2.md R1). The language record splits into the language, the tables kept per file, one compile's caches and the build; a file's text is scanned once for its uses; the restart after a standard module is brought in goes. Gates: a rule declared in one file does not fire in a file that does not use it; an operator used above its declaration is refused; --stage 2 a fixed point. Estimate about -70 core. Kernel-side module scopes are T2d stage 3 (wap-theory-reads-types): agree the seam in coc-t2.md. First a plan in notes/coc-tm.md, reviewed by the supervisor, before core edits.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318111418\n\nbranch: one-environment-per-module (2026-11-25)\n\nplan: notes/coc-tm.md on branch one-environment-per-module c1e09bb5 (TM1 split, TM2 grammar per module, TM3 one scan + declarations in order, TM4 restart gone; core ≈ −12 estimated); sent to wap-supervisor, no core edit before the OK\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (wiki) via wap-interviewer: use.md new sentence (syntax follows the use chain) and operator.md:146 'from its declaration on, in its file and in the files that use it', both as written; TM estimate core ~-12 noted, no objection asked\n\nTM4 lowers the ceiling below 143296 (TM1 raised it to 143455 for the field paths)\n\nland: one-environment-per-module b322deea (TM1, careful: hello, self 79✓, census ok; size ceiling 143569). TM2 on branch one-environment-per-module-tm2 (per-file grammars; +~60 core so far)\n\nTM2 built on one-environment-per-module-tm2 50eb975f: green except size +975 nodes (core +63) and theory 2228 (a red wanted file refused whole); decision asked of wap-supervisor\n\nTM1 landed caacda75 (size ceiling 166552 measured); TM2-4 remain\n\n(TM1's merge on main is 10bd563b, rebased from caacda75)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (core) via wap-interviewer: A, land TM2 (asked at +66; measured +74 = standing OK small overrun). TM total now est. +81, not +41: TM3 (+13) asked separately\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (core) via wap-interviewer: build TM3 (+13, operator works only below its declaration); TM total est. +81 accepted\n\ntyping gap met in TM3: `m.get(k) ?? {}` with m: map<text, map<text, text>> types the empty {} as map<any, any> instead of taking the left side's type; the census then types map == over any and refuses it as a function calling itself (#(map<any, any>, any) needs its full result type). Worked around in core/pipeline.wap line_told with a has test (337b0dca+1). The general fix: an empty literal on the right of ?? takes the left side's type.\n\nland: one-environment-per-module-tm2 ba2baca1 (TM2 + TM3; careful path green; size 169315; +1.9% instructions; patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/one-environment-per-module/tm2-tm3-ba2baca1.patch). Next: TM4 on a new branch.\n\ndecided 2026-11-25 (wap-interviewer, 0 core, reversible): TM ends at TM3; TM4 (the restart goes) moves into T5 (coc-plan.md:956), measured ~0 net now, not -14\n\nTM4 decided A (user via wap-interviewer 2026-11-25): TM ends at TM3, the restart goes with T5 (coc-plan.md:956). cleanup: empty branch one-environment-per-module-tm4 (local only, hook blocks the delete)\n\nTM2+TM3 landed f9c06b41 (fixed point, size 172419); TM4 remains",
