   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABigh8QA",
   "title": "The kernel types a term by one rule function per…",
   "body": "Original title: The kernel types a term by one rule function per typing rule, each giving a numbered judgement\n\nT2e of notes/coc-t2.md (\"Checked(term, type): the rule functions\"): Checked { term; type }, the checker's judgement table, one rule per row of 6.3; type_of becomes their walk, its memory keeping judgement numbers; an apply_rule per argument; compiler-growth.sh refuses a Checked( outside wap/kernel/typing.wap. Gate: the theory census CPU ratio stays under 3. Builds on kernel-ids.\n\nAdded by wap-theory-reads-types with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318235361\n\nbranch: kernel-rules (2026-11-25)\n\nbranch kernel-rules 7556ddfc, on kernel-ids 72a57632: theory 388 ✓, census 2364 of 11868, ratio 231/162 s (gate < 3 passes), size 166691 (+526), growth ✓. Hand-off once kernel-ids lands, rebased.\n\nland: kernel-rules d8de8e86 (patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/kernel-t2/kernel-rules.patch); then theory-census-retire\n\nland: kernel-rules c4aeb063 (replaces d8de8e86; patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/kernel-t2/kernel-rules.patch); then theory-census-retire\n\nFixed in [383f6a92](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/383f6a92f874ae3e420f1478db104a6d520e64d6): merge kernel-rules: T2e of the coc plan (card kernel-rules; the user's track-T decisions 2026-11-25; wap-supervisor: sound)",
