 "extension-rule-annotations": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhL4Rks",
  "title": "A rule in the compiler's extension files ignores…",
  "updated": "2026-11-25T20:25:14Z",
  "key": "extension-rule-annotations",
  "agent": "wap-annotation-attachment-fix",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-25T18:51:50Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-25T20:25:14Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABig8RoA",
   "title": "A rule in the compiler's extension files ignores…",
   "body": "Original title: A rule in the compiler's extension files ignores an annotation in its pattern\n\nIn a program's own rules, `rule (@D $f($p...): $r from $l) => print(\"A\")` matches only `@D g(a: i64): i64 from 'q'` and not the same line without @D, which is right. In wap/extensions/c/foreign.wap the same pattern, `rule (@Device $name($parameters...): $result from $library) => ($name($parameters...): $result from (device $library))`, behaves differently. Placed after the plain foreign rules, it never fires: an @Device line is lowered as unmarked. Placed first, it takes unannotated lines too, and the native wap stops building: wap/extensions/native/c.wap line 37 `calloc(count: i64, size: i64): i64 from 'c'` reports 'wap does not lower this form yet'. Attempt: /Volumes/Worktrees/c-device-openers/data/attempts/at-device.patch (from c-device-openers-in-bindings 800d7f8b). Guess (wap-supervisor, unchecked): extension rule files are read before the step that attaches leading annotations (f9ce07db), so their patterns never carry the annotation. After the fix, the C bindings switch from `! Device` to `@Device` (user 2026-11-25: @Device if easier). A fix of 3 lines or less goes under the standing OK.\n\nAdded by wap-annotation-attachment-fix with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318260811\n\nbranch: extension-rule-annotations (2026-11-25)\n\nbranch extension-rule-annotations 4efd671e: stages.wap rule_added's duplicate test compares annotations; rule_applied spends the asked annotations (no re-fire). @Device switch in foreign.wap, bindings, test_native; wiki 1b014b7. Seen: rule_applied refuses a tie eagerly before a later more specific rule (edge).\n\nstanding OK small fix (wap-supervisor sound). land: extension-rule-annotations 43766281; careful: hello, growth, self 79 ✓, census ✓ but size 143736 > 143614 (+122), integrator asked to raise\n\nFixed in [22d75086](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/22d75086d0537faf554f876c65744b18c35dfd98): merge extension-rule-annotations: a rule asking for an annotation is a rule of its own beside the same pattern without it, and spends the annotation on what it writes; the C device openers are marked @Device (standing OK small fix, core +1, wap-supervisor sound; @Device the user's preferred spelling, via wap-interviewer)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": null,
   "subIssuesSummary": {
    "total": 0,
    "completed": 0
   },
   "type": "Issue"
  },
  "left_board": "2026-11-27"
 },
