   "body": "Original title: Top-level statements of files that use each other should run in the order their values need\n\nBranch wap-globals-by-need, 1 commit, held for the user (2 days).\n\nbranch: wap-globals-by-need (parked, found without a card by the board keeper 2026-11-23; tip 35c85a6)\n\nAdded by wap-board with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314875685\n\nedge-case drop proposed to wap-interviewer (loud refusal stays, ~55 core lines saved); branch kept until the user answers\n\ndecided (edge case, 0 core, CLAUDE.md 'We do not care about edge cases'): main already refuses the read loudly at the line — of two files using each other, a top-level statement reading the other's constant gives 'this name is read before any value is given to it' when that file runs first, and runs ('ab') in the other use order (checked on 9eeb46ea + possessive-dynamic). The branch's reordering (+67/−25 in core/analyze) is not landed; branch wap-globals-by-need 35c85a65 kept for the user's cleanup list\n\nFixed in [250a8ad9](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/250a8ad930a5a73ade6cc7b94fca31fe7032d076): refactor: one library copy, built into the compiler; the native host finds it beside the compiler, no types-<hash>.wasm in output folders (user)",
