 "template-shape": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLE0g8",
  "title": "A sugar rule's output does not have the shape its…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T10:41:23Z",
  "key": "template-shape",
  "agent": "wap-annotation-attachment-fix",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T08:29:04Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T10:41:23Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhsK44g",
   "title": "A sugar rule's output does not have the shape its…",
   "body": "Original title: A sugar rule's output does not have the shape its text has in a program, so rules written for the text never fire on it\n\nDebt sugar/records.wap:15, rules/templates.wap:27 (notes/open_decisions.md debt 4). Shape (wap-reviewer): read and normalize each template once when its rule is declared (per build), filling holes gives the program text's shape; no per-firing re-read. Pay stages.wap:235 (a looping rewrite hangs) with it. Core -10 to +5. Lets a method's as and : forms become one rule.\n\nOK 2026-11-23 via wap-interviewer: user decided do it (core, this shape); queued after the work in flight, one at a time.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=314888719\n\nuser OK 2026-11-23 (core): read and normalize each template once when its rule is declared (per build), so its output has the shape its text parses to; the builder's own Define/Set construction goes; pay stages.wap:235 (endless rewrite hangs) in the same change. Estimate -10 to +5 core lines.\n\nbranch: template-shape (2026-11-24)\n\nPlan/state (branch template-shape, tip 75e9fc4a, pushed): root cause is not the templates. Templates already give the program's shape; the mismatch was in the matcher. patterns.wap normalized turns a pattern written in brackets, `rule q ($a + $b)`, into the bare call, but the program's `q (x + 1)` reaches the matcher as the grouped call ((Call ...)). Fix 2f5048ca in core/rules/matcher.wap (+2 code lines, +2 comment lines): a sequence matcher that is a form pattern (round, space-separated, literal head) takes a grouped call as the call; an argument group `f(x + 1)` stays a group (prelude.wap:248 proves the guard). This replaces 'normalize every template at declaration' (est. -10..+5); smaller, and it does not fold with enum-index option B (no template machinery touched). Payoff 75e9fc4a: the records.wap DEBT is paid; a method `... as T := body` rewrites to the `:` method, one rule. Tests: test_hello green; rules, typed_rules, records, class_page, pattern_matching_page 92 ✓; class_init and json_class red the same way as on main. Still open: the stages.wap:237 hang debt (a looping rewrite hangs instead of being refused); my plan is a cycle refusal inside `rewritten` (a node rewritten back to a shape it already had is refused, naming the rule), in a separate commit. Waiting: op-spelled-once must land first (core changes one at a time); then merge origin/main and hand off to warp-integrator.\n\nOK 2026-11-24 night via wap-interviewer: the fix moves from the template builder to the matcher (core/rules/matcher.wap, +2 code lines): a form pattern takes a grouped call as that call, and an argument group like f(x + 1) stays a group. Why: the templates were already right; the bug was the bracket mismatch. It stays inside the user's OK (-10..+5) and pays sugar/records.wap's DEBT. Undo: revert branch template-shape 75e9fc4a. Shown to the user at 10:00 as a note.\n\nUpdate: hang debt paid too, be6e5f2b (pushed, tip): a shape rewrite that keeps firing on its own output is refused after ROUNDS_LIMIT (100) instead of hanging; one refusal `refired` in stages.wap shared with the typed rules (typed.wap's copy removed), net 0 core lines. Probe `rule go $f => $f go` on `go go` hung >60 s before, now refused at once. The static termination check misses it because the head arrives through a hole. Checks at be6e5f2b: test_hello green; area tests 92 ✓ (class_init, json_class red as on main); test_self 78 ✓, 0 ✗. Card is done pending order: once op-spelled-once lands, merge origin/main and hand off to wap-integrator.\n\nParked: worktree removed; branch origin/template-shape tip be6e5f2b, clean. Next: once op-spelled-once lands, cowtree add the branch, merge origin/main, hand off to wap-integrator.\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-enum-index-constant-time: owner session wap-enum-index-constant-time retired (restarted into native-maps 09:11); state: see earlier notes/branch template-shape\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core) via wap-interviewer: keep the +2 matcher.wap fix; the normalize-at-declare refactor is dropped as unneeded.\n\nland: template-shape 867e36ee (merged with main 2026-11-26; careful checks green: areas 252 ✓, test_self 95 ✓)\n\nFixed in [9eeb46ea](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/9eeb46ea510872f8585dbc37788bbf6b818a93ff): merge template-shape: a call in round brackets fits a pattern of that call (core/rules/matcher.wap +2), so a method's as and : forms are one rule in sugar/records.wap; a shape rewrite that keeps firing on its own output is refused after ROUNDS_LIMIT instead of hanging, one refired shared with the typed rules (user OK 2026-11-23 and 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
