   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABhxqM0Q",
   "title": "wap has no word for the current working folder…",
   "body": "Original title: wap has no word for the current working folder, so remove_file's guard reads $PWD from when the run started\n\nlib/file.wap working_folder() is started_env(\"PWD\") ?? \".\"; remove_file's refusal of the working folder and folders above it uses it. warp used std_io(\"os\", \"cwd\"). A cwd word (WASI has none; natively getcwd from 'c') would make it exact. Interviewer asked for this card 2026-11-23.\n\nAdded by wap-wiki-lib with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315225783\n\nbranch: cwd-word (2026-11-27)\n\nFixed in [81459932](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/81459932b56b0e3f64f2165e713962283efcb71c): merge cwd-word: cwd is the working folder of now, by C's getcwd, in lib/file.wap, which remove_file's guard, absolute_path, os and shell's pwd use, no longer the $PWD the run started with (lib only; test_file +2; no compiler change)",
