 "sound-library-port": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLR3IA",
  "title": "Programs cannot use sound, music or audio yet",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T05:19:11Z",
  "key": "sound-library-port",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T04:54:29Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T05:19:11Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABh5w7xA",
   "title": "Programs cannot use sound, music or audio yet",
   "body": "Original title: Programs cannot use sound, music or audio yet because those libraries are still in warp\n\nPort lib/sound.warp (1645 lines), lib/music.warp and lib/audio.warp to plain wap under the port rule (copy warp, no slop, red rather than ugly). Compile-only checks: no sound played, nothing audible in any test. Compiler gaps go to wap-lead and stay red. First red: sound.warp:937 posix_spawnp environment: texts (use a handle as process.wap does).\n\nAdded by wap-host-port-window with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=315743360\n\nbranch: sound-library-port (2026-11-23)\n\nlib/sound.wap: notes, synth, effects, melodies, mini-notation ported (scratch-verified). Red on wap-binding's 'a non-callable value hides a function' (use units' min; sound's own filter setting hides .filter) and shared enum case (chord(C4, major)); test_sound.wap is red until that lands. data/scratch_sound.sh tests a renamed copy meanwhile.\n\ndone: sound.wap pure part (notes, chords, scales, synth, effects, melodies, mini-notation, WAV, MIDI files, spectrum) + test/test_sound.wap 14 ✓; playing half written. left: compiler crash 'this list has no item at this place' when sound's pure part (lines 1-270, any complete cut past ~250) is compiled with 'use c' (via host/native_host/platform.wap or SDL3); cut at 240 compiles. Bisect further (scratch: data/scratch_sound.sh, probe data/probe/bis.wap), minimal repro to wap-lead; then compile-only check data/probe/playing.wap (NEVER run it), check no stderr word exists before print_error in system.wap, delete lib/sound.warp, add music.wap/audio.wap (use sound), hello+sound tests, hand off. branch: sound-library-port tip 2ef0eaa9 (worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/units-chain-port)\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-host-port-window: done: sound.wap pure part (notes, chords, scales, synth, effects, melodies, mini-notation, WAV, MIDI files, spectrum) + test/test_sound.wap 14 ✓; playing half written. left: compiler crash 'this list has no item at this place' when sound's pure part (lines 1-270, any complete cut past ~250) is compiled with 'use c' (via host/native_host/platform.wap or SDL3); cut at 240 compiles. Bisect further (scratch: data/scratch_sound.sh, probe data/probe/bis.wap), minimal repro to wap-lead; then compile-only check data/probe/playing.wap (NEVER run it), check no stderr word exists before print_error in system.wap, delete lib/sound.warp, add music.wap/audio.wap (use sound), hello+sound tests, hand off. branch: sound-library-port tip 2ef0eaa9 (worktree /Volumes/Worktrees/units-chain-port)\n\nland: sound-library-port 7a43e73f\n\nFixed in [ebc8cbf2](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/ebc8cbf224e74a565ce69e607eb1d4fe5ea001fe): merge sound-library-port: warp's sound in lib/sound.wap (notes, chords, scales, synth, effects, melodies, mini-notation, WAV/MIDI, spectrum, playing); music and audio use it; their .warp files go",
