  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiCX0Nw",
   "title": "Naming an enum T clashes silently with the type…",
   "body": "Original title: Naming an enum T clashes silently with the type variable T and leads to confusing errors\n\nFound by wap-simplifier in K0. Refuse, never guess: the declaration should be refused, naming the clash.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316287059\n\nbranch: naming-enum (2026-11-26)\n\nReleased 2026-11-26 by wap-primitive-lookup-tables: done: nothing; left: all; branch: none (cpu-vs-instructions first, supervisor)\n\nbranch naming-enum 4d83ddb7: letters scoped by DECLARED_BY (is_letter, shaped, type_substituted), +1 net core, census +15 (179327); test/test_types_letter.wap; review asked of wap-supervisor\n\nland: naming-enum 20049fc5 (fix 4d83ddb7 + shrink 2f932420; express + types green)\n\nFixed in [404ceb91](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/404ceb91af04f45d148b48c0b7bf2d6d51ad5377): merge naming-enum: a letter the program declares as a type, enum T, is that type only in the program's own code, so the types module's generic words keep T generic; is_letter, has_letters and letters_in drop their records parameter (standing OK small fix, +1 core, then a pure shrink; wap-supervisor: sound at 4d83ddb7 and 2f932420); wap's size ceiling falls to the measured 179379 nodes (−47)",
