 "arrow-value-fixit": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLbJz4",
  "title": "function value written with -> is refused without…",
  "updated": "2026-11-27T02:26:55Z",
  "key": "arrow-value-fixit",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-27T01:44:46Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-27T02:26:55Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiDYr2Q",
   "title": "function value written with -> is refused without…",
   "body": "Original title: A function value written with -> is refused without saying that => writes function values\n\n(a, b) -> a + b as a value now gets 'nothing defines this name' (since function-value-wiki: -> writes function types only, wiki/closure.md). The refusal should carry a fix-it: '-> writes a function type; a function value is written with =>'. Asked by wap-reviewer on function-value-wiki a855aef7.\n\nAdded by wap-wiki-tidy with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316352318\n\nbranch: arrow-value-fixit (2026-11-26)\n\nprobed 2026-11-26 on main 3ed33f2a: a plain-wap rule cannot give the fix-it. rule ((...) -> $body) => refuse \"-> writes a function type; a function value is written with =>\" fires on written types too (double: (int) -> int = …, apply(f: (int) -> int, …)), and a rule's where-guard reads a fact on the node, while at the shape stage nothing marks a type position apart from a value. A typed rule comes too late: typing refuses a (nothing defines this name, core/analyze/modules.wap:69) before the -> call is typed. Missing mechanism: a fact for code written as a type (the reader knows: after a declaration's colon, a parameter's type), usable as a guard, where type; or the refusal at modules.wap:69 told that the name stands in a -> written as a value. Either is core.\n\nReleased 2026-11-26 by wap-annotation-attachment-fix: done: probed; left: needs a type-position fact or guard (core), see note; branch: none\n\nbranch arrow-value-fixit 3f559a25: form_bound refuses a -> call with the => fix-it (+1 core, core/analyze/scope.wap); test/wap/test_functions.wap line; census +14 (179489); review asked of wap-supervisor\n\nlater (wap-supervisor nit, not blocking): once T4a's written span lands, the fix-it can show the user's own code rewritten with => instead of the fixed example (a, b) => a + b\n\nland: arrow-value-fixit 54e07e86 (express + functions green; ceiling 179489)\n\nFixed in [09b9a57f](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/09b9a57f63f94d0d74b473c1f5305360b9c52f99): merge arrow-value-fixit: a function type written where a value stands, (a, b) -> a + b, is refused saying a function value is written with =>, not 'nothing defines this name' (+1 core in core/analyze/scope.wap; test_functions +1 check; census +14 measured; standing OK small fix; wap-supervisor: sound at 3f559a25)",
