 "class-named": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLb4Hw",
  "title": "class named like one in core gives confusing error",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T17:36:06Z",
  "key": "class-named",
  "agent": "wap-annotation-attachment-fix",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T11:49:37Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T17:36:06Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiEIKhA",
   "title": "class named like one in core gives confusing error",
   "body": "Original title: A class named like one in the compiler's own core gives a confusing error pointing into core instead of saying the two names clash\n\nRepro (wap-emitter): add `class Scope { variables: list<Term>; rest: Term? }` to wap/extensions/theory/elaborate/read.wap, compile elaborate/door.wap: 'wap/core/analyze/scope.wap line 41:52: the arguments are not of the parameters' types'. Expected: 'names.wap and read.wap both define Scope: rename one' (two extensions/theory files clashing already get that). Found while building theory-enums-match-recursion.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316399740\n\nbranch: class-named (2026-11-26)\n\nexplored 2026-11-26: the theory repro is gone (door.wap no longer pulls core). General repro: a program declaring class Scope and using two.wap, which declares its own class Scope and layered(s: Scope); layered(Scope([3])) is refused only by the emitter (core/emit/functions.wap:109, 'the arguments are not of the parameters' types'): typing takes both Scopes as one type by name. use.md: a program's own definition wins. Options sent to wap-supervisor: A refuse a program type named like a used module's (+~2 core, use.md line), B type identity per module (large), C emitter message names files. Recommend A.\n\nReleased 2026-11-26 by wap-primitive-lookup-tables: parked (wap-supervisor): option B arrives with T3b types-as-terms (82ac269b, records named by their declaration's place). After T3b lands, rerun /Volumes/Worktrees/loop-variable-reuses-name/data/probe/one.wap (uses two.wap): if typing refuses but the message doesn't name both declarations, that message is the fix (a few lines, no use.md change). Probe sent to wap-theory-reads-types.\n\nprobe files kept at ~/Library/Logs/warp/class-named/{one,two}.wap\n\nrerun on main (834b7b79 + claim fix): typing refuses now, 'no layered takes (Scope): layered(s: Scope) as int, line 2 of two.wap'; both sides still say Scope, the message naming each declaration's file and line is the fix left (the T3b follow-up)\n\nrerun 2026-11-26 on main 90782c24 (T3c1 in): unchanged, 'no layered takes (Scope): layered(s: Scope) as int, line 2 of two.wap'; the two Scopes are still both named Scope. Left: the refusal names each class by its declaration's file and line when two classes share a name.\n\ninterviewer 2026-11-26: emitter's Program renamed Emission (pure rename, 0 net, standing OK); types/system.wap Program stays\n\nland: class-named 98bb358f (standing OK small fix, +1 net core in type_notation.wap; pure rename Program → Emission in core/emit; wap-supervisor: sound; +0.06% instructions on the warm wap1→wap2 step)\n\nland: class-named 7a77ea9c (merged with main, T3c2 conflict resolved; test_hello, growth and the class areas 114 ✓ green; patches in /Volumes/Worktrees/class-named/data/patches)\n\nFixed in [b4d9aca6](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/b4d9aca60c6a458b8545a16c03f72c02e3927e5f): merge class-named: a message tells two records sharing a name apart by their declarations' places, `no layered takes (Scope one.wap 2:1)`; the emitter's state is the class Emission, so the compiler's own records share no name; whether a record shares its name is one lookup where records are declared; wap's size ceiling rises to the measured 178347 nodes (+101, the names counted where records are declared) (+2 net core, standing OK; wap-supervisor: sound)",
