  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiFjLEg",
   "title": "A body that starts on its own indented line does…",
   "body": "Original title: A body that starts on its own indented line does not continue past a line ending in an operator\n\ncore/parse (wap-reader). `x =⏎\\t1 +⏎\\t2` is refused: 'several functions have this name … +'. The second indented line reads as its own statement, and `+` is left as a bare function name. The same continuation works when the body starts on the `:=` line (`x = 1 +⏎\\t2` gives 3) and inside braces. Met while writing test_theory_prelude_checked.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316488408\n\nbranch: body-starts (2026-11-26)\n\nparked attempt on branch body-starts 0dcdd514, not to land: joining a body's same-depth line after an operator also joins 'operator % has precedence below +'. Main already continues when the next line is one tab deeper (x =⏎\\t1 +⏎\\t\\t2 → 3), as wap format writes it. Question to interviewer.\n\nclosed without a landing: a continued line is written one tab deeper (x =⏎\\t1 +⏎\\t\\t2 works on main, as wap format writes it); a same-depth join would misread a line ending in an operator name (operator % has precedence below +; wiki Features.md:59). Parked attempt 0dcdd514 not landed; branch body-starts to cleanup.\n\nuser 2026-11-26 via interviewer: a continued line is written one tab deeper, as format writes it (0 core); same depth stays refused; wiki syntax.md line added (6c6b397)",
