  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiFzsOQ",
   "title": "wap format does not format the file, it reads…",
   "body": "Original title: wap format <file> does not format the file: it reads 'format' as a program, and the compiler's format entry stops on a theory file's uses\n\nFrom wap-binding (theory-traits-conditions): `wap format f` gives 'format comes from time'; `wap wap/compiler.wap format f` follows the file's uses and stops at 'no module magnitude' (wap/extensions/theory/numbers.wap). Format must not need the uses resolved. The AGENTS.md landing check 'wap/compiler.wap format' cannot run on theory files. Owner: wap-reader (core/format.wap) after prelude-collections-rationals.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316506223\n\nAlso hit by wap-emitter (E5).\n\nbranch: wap-format (2026-11-26)\n\nfixed on main before this card was taken up: 79e1434b (wap format <file> is the native wap's format command, no longer a program named format) and 6e45f4b6 (format no longer needs typing: code typing refuses is formatted as read, so a theory file whose uses don't resolve formats). Checked 2026-11-26 on the installed wap: all 51 files of extensions/theory and extensions/prove format with exit 0 (one hint, no error).\n\ndup?: format-joins-lines (by score, 2026-11-28)",
