  "column_since": "2026-11-26T07:41:15Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiF0PKA",
   "title": "wap format joins a line continued after an…",
   "body": "Original title: wap format joins a line continued after an operator or an open call into one long line\n\nA body laid out over lines (`a +⏎\\tb`, a call whose arguments go on to the next line) comes out of `wap/compiler.wap format` as one line of 300+ characters, and a one-expression body on its own line gets wrapped in braces. Seen on test/wap/test_theory_prelude_checked.wap (branch prelude-collections-rationals). Owner wap-reader (core/format.wap); sibling of format-keeps-lines, which keeps bracket rows.\n\nAdded by wap-reader with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316506860\n\nbranch: format-joins-lines (2026-11-26)\n\nbranch format-joins-lines b5dd67b1: option A built (format.wap +9); only red test_reader.wap:75 (pins joining). Waiting for the user via interviewer.\n\nInterviewer: +9 core and a test_reader.wap:75 edit; queued for the user's morning popup, recommend A; not landed.\n\nuser 2026-11-26 via interviewer: A, keep a break written after an operator, one tab deeper (+9 core); test_reader.wap:75 expectation edit granted (own commit).\n\nland: format-joins-lines caf9cf30 (user decision 2026-11-26, A)\n\nFixed in [59d9dadc](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/59d9dadc3559c624147f8ba3e504dc67537b7c1c): merge format-joins-lines: wap format keeps a line break written after an operator, the next line one tab deeper (a +⏎\tb); test_reader's expectation follows (user 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer)\n\ndup?: wap-format (by score, 2026-11-28)",
