  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiG-a_w",
   "title": "test runner starts the whole suite when given an…",
   "body": "Original title: The test runner starts the whole suite when it is given an empty list of areas\n\nSeen by wap-binding 2026-11-24: a zsh glob matched nothing, run.sh got no areas and ran everything. test/wap/run.sh should refuse an explicit but empty area list loudly; the whole suite only when asked for with no arguments.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316581915\n\nbranch: run-empty-areas (2026-11-24)\n\nsupervisor: dropped. An empty area list is indistinguishable from the documented full run (run.sh --wait, wap test); one worker's glob slip doesn't justify changing the integrator's interface and AGENTS.md. Archive.\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by wap-fixer: dropped by supervisor: an empty area list looks like the documented full run; branch run-empty-areas has no commits (cleanup list)\n\nSibling seen 2026-11-26: one unknown area name among several (run.sh --wait self ratchet_census letters …, or … dispatch) prints 'no test of <name>' and runs none of the others.\n\nseen again 2026-11-26: run.sh --wait enum … generics … printed 'no test of generics' and ran none of the other areas\n\narchived (wap-supervisor 2026-11-26): already refused where detectable (zsh nomatch, bash literal pattern, \"\", unknown area); an empty $(…) is indistinguishable from the full run without an `all` word (declined 11-24)\n\nFixed in [0acaf08d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/0acaf08d0251aab899d12c8580134ff2c6550494): fix: run.sh keeps each test file's output apart (test_x.wap.txt, test_x.sh.txt) and an area runs all its programs and its script",
