  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiICqfQ",
   "title": "match arm bare case name catches every value",
   "body": "Original title: A match arm written as a bare case name catches every value instead of matching that case\n\nuser OK 2026-11-24 (core, size measured before landing) via wap-interviewer: in a match arm, a bare word naming a declared case or pattern (Break =>) matches that case, like Break(); only a word that names no case binds. Today it silently binds the subject and catches everything (reported by wap-emitter, theory-for-walk). Outcome test: match on a nullary case followed by another arm gives the later arm's value.\n\nAdded by wap-interviewer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316652996\n\nReleased 2026-11-24 by its agent: done: nothing; left: everything; branch: none\n\nbranch: match-bare-case (2026-11-26)\n\nland: match-bare-case 34d9d1bb — user OK 2026-11-24: a declared pattern's bare name in an arm matches its shape (core/analyze/scope.wap named_pattern, +5), holes named by their own names; census 179215 (+96); careful path green (test_matching_wanted red as on main). Seen: `pattern Pair = [_, _]` then `Pair()` in an arm is refused ('this pattern can never fit … (Call Symbol \"_\")'), already red in test_pattern_matching_wanted.wap:25-26.\n\nFixed in [9a9e047d](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/9a9e047d98b2a88ea2099ca414c75fa2b6684779): merge match-bare-case: in a match arm a bare word naming a declared case or pattern matches that case, like Break(); only a word that names no case binds the subject (wap/core/analyze/scope.wap; test_matching +1 check; user 2026-11-24 via wap-interviewer, on its card; census +96 covered; wap-supervisor: sound at 34d9d1bb)",
