 "format-spelling-drift": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLhvdg",
  "title": "wap format rewrites compiler files, landing check…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T19:30:20Z",
  "key": "format-spelling-drift",
  "agent": "wap-annotation-attachment-fix",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T18:40:30Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T19:30:20Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiJ_OsA",
   "title": "wap format rewrites compiler files, landing check…",
   "body": "Original title: wap format rewrites the compiler's own files into another spelling, so the landing check can't use it\n\nFound by wap-fixer with the seed after a6abf88d. wap format <tree file> rewrites: 'f(..): T :=' to 'f(..) as T :=', '{ a; b }' to '{a; b}', 'is not ø' to 'is (not ø)', '?? return x' to '?? (return x)'. Each one is either a wrong canonical word or a reading the compiler makes. 'is (not ø)' in particular may show that 'x is not ø' is read as x is (not ø): check what value it gives (a wrong-reading bug would be the worst kind). Canonical output follows the wiki's recommended spelling.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316784088\n\nSupervisor probe: 'x is not ø' gives yes for 3 and no for ø, so the value is right and only format's spelling is off.\n\nbranch: format-spelling-drift (2026-11-26)\n\nbranch format-spelling-drift 85e23143: format writes x is not ø without brackets and keeps (a * not b) + c (core/format.wap +11, 8 code lines; size +183 nodes); waiting for the user's core OK via wap-supervisor. The ?? (return x) item is no drift: test_operators.wap pins x = f(a) ?? (return ø), a phrase on the right printed in brackets as its reading. Brace spacing was fixed by 79b8c9e9.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 (interviewer popup): lands at +8 core in core/format.wap; census SIZE_NODES 178537 -> 178720 granted\n\nland: format-spelling-drift e22ca352 (normal path green: test_hello, compiler-growth, operators/reader/interpolation/native 219 ✓ 0 ✗, the census at 178720; patches in /Volumes/Worktrees/format-spelling-drift/data/patches). user OK 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer, option (a): +8 core code lines, SIZE_NODES 178537 -> 178720; wap-supervisor: sound.\n\nFixed in [57c5aeba](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/57c5aebabf620b33edce3fa9a68f64e8987f7939): merge format-spelling-drift: wap format writes a prefix operator as a right operand without brackets, so `x is not ø` round-trips, and code ending in a looser prefix keeps its brackets where the next operator is tighter, `(a * not b) + c`; wap's size ceiling rises to the measured 178720 (+8 core in core/format.wap; user OK 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer; wap-supervisor: sound)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
   "parent": {
    "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiEQMrg",
    "title": "formatter crashes on theory files and rewrites…"
