 "warp-temp-race": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLiCnI",
  "title": "under load warp can't read its temp file",
  "updated": "2026-11-27T00:32:57Z",
  "key": "warp-temp-race",
  "agent": "wap-native-no-layout-any",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T23:29:42Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-27T00:32:56Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiKTGsA",
   "title": "under load warp can't read its temp file",
   "body": "Original title: Under load warp sometimes can't read its own temp file, so a test fails once and passes on rerun\n\nSeen by wap-integrator landing 02bcb700: test_theory_elaborate failed once with warp 'cannot read /var/folders/…/T/warp-<n>', green on rerun. Probably a temp-file name race in warp between parallel runs (the name is likely not unique per process). warp's code, not wap's.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=316803698\n\nChecked 2026-11-26: warp's core/native/driver.warp compiled_path names its temp module warp-native-<pid>.wasm in $TMPDIR, unique per process, so the race the card guesses is not there in today's warp (~/dev/bin/warp = native-8a105fa36). The failing 'warp-<n>' name comes from elsewhere, maybe an older warp. Not reproducible; warp's code, not wap's: left for warp's owners.\n\nSeen again 2026-11-26 by wap-integrator: test/wap/test_theory_connectives.wap failed once with 'cannot read /var/folders/…/T/warp-446942843' while 43 areas ran at once (landing analyze-types-e2 471a8882); alone 15 ✓.\n\nbranch: warp-temp-race (2026-11-27)\n\nland: warp-temp-race 652fc53e. Cause: temp_named = warp-<random_below(1e9)> from the shared generator seeded by wall_clock_ms, then exists-then-write: runs started the same ms took one name, the first to finish (process.wap removed(child)) deleted the other's. Fix: mkstemps/mkdtemp make it at once. Probe: 64 parallel runs, old wap 1-5 names taken twice, new 0 in 5 rounds. Also image.wap: headless paintings go to a run's own temp_dir, not a shared wap-paint/. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/warp-temp-race/warp-temp-race.patch\n\nsuperseded by land: free-malloc 5d3fa17f (it holds this branch plus the lighter 48-run check)\n\nFixed in [d9cb1732](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/d9cb1732bdf0ba0438fad8b684a9580be21c7e1a): merge test-killed: run.sh ends every test's output with \"— ran to its end\" once judged, and an output without it is \"✗ <test> ran to its end\", so a test killed with its runner is red with its baseline reds kept; with free-malloc, lib/c.wap declares free, malloc, close, fopen, fclose, getenv, setenv, getcwd, strdup, strndup, calloc and field_i32 once for the libraries that use c, and warp-temp-race, a temporary file or folder made at once by mkstemps or mkdtemp, its name unique, so runs at the same moment never share one (library, test and scripts; no compiler change)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
