 "local-shadows-field-call": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLlyqA",
  "title": "local named like a function field breaks calling…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T20:44:26Z",
  "key": "local-shadows-field-call",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T19:21:27Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T20:44:26Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiOQMyg",
   "title": "local named like a function field breaks calling…",
   "body": "Original title: A local named like a function field breaks calling that field: make = m.make() says make is read before it has a value\n\nProbe: class Maker { name: text; make: () -> int }; f(m: Maker): int := { make = m.make(); make + 1 }; print f(Maker(\"a\", () => 3)) → \"line 3:11: this name is read before any value is given to it: make = m.make()\". Without the local of the same name it prints 3. The field call m.make() resolves to the local being defined (method-call lookup finds the binding first). Met in wap/extensions/prove/rewriting.wap (theory-arithmetic), worked around by naming the field `made`. Owner: wap-binding (core/analyze).\n\nAdded by wap-binding with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317049504\n\nbranch: local-shadows-field-call (2026-11-26)\n\nuser 2026-11-26 (interviewer popup): general rule: a name's first assignment reads its value before its own local exists (make = m.make(), twice = n.twice()); where the name is an outer variable (global) it stays refused with a fix-it; ~+5-6 core analyze/scope.wap; narrow field fix e82fc011 not landed\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26: census SIZE_NODES 178867 (+98)\n\nuser 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer: the general first-assignment rule, size +98 OK. land: local-shadows-field-call 4678f0b9; checks: hello, growth, 14 areas incl. self 290 ✓ 0 ✗, census green with ceiling 178867; speed unchanged\n\nFixed in [898d4062](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/898d40629ea05045dc6345dd68ae7f2cdfa8be45): merge local-shadows-field-call: a name's first assignment reads its value before its new local exists, so `make = m.make()` calls m's field and `twice = n.twice()` the function; the program's `count = count + 1` inside a function stays refused; wap's size ceiling follows to the measured 178994 nodes (+90) (+1 core code line in core/analyze names.wap and scope.wap; user OK 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer, census rise covered)",
