 "plus-assign-in-for": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhLmrw0",
  "title": "list += inside for loop in function fails with…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T15:15:15Z",
  "key": "plus-assign-in-for",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T14:28:28Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T15:15:15Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiPKfCg",
   "title": "list += inside for loop in function fails with…",
   "body": "Original title: A list += inside a for loop in a function body fails with an assignment error that names no line\n\nFrom wap-binding. Repro: /Volumes/Worktrees/theory-arithmetic-linear/data/probe/plus-assign-in-for.wap\ng(xs: list<int>): list<int> := { unknowns: list<int> = []; for u in xs { unknowns += [u] }; unknowns }\n→ 'no place to assign: a name, a variable, a part or an item: ø', no line. Works: top level; int += in a function's for; ys = ys + [x]; list += outside a loop.\nRelated footgun: 'unknown' is an alias of ø (types/operators.wap:167), so a parameter or lambda variable named unknown silently becomes ø (seen: 'no added takes (Sums, Term, ø)'). A parameter named by an alias of ø could be refused with why.\n\nAdded by wap-fixer with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317107981\n\nalso: a local named `unknown` (an ø alias) gives 'no place to assign: a name, a variable, a part or an item: ø' with no file or line at all (met in wap/extensions/theory/options.wap, theory-census): the refusal should name the place and the alias\n\nbranch: plus-assign-in-for (2026-11-26)\n\nland: plus-assign-in-for ab0b0e4d (merged with origin/main 886ad89a; hello, growth, census green; areas for_page, assignment_page, loops, self 136 ✓). Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/handoff/plus-assign-in-for.patch\n\nFixed in [cad87b5e](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/cad87b5e59f2b7560f37fa40a956670b1af9c97a): merge plus-assign-in-for: an assignment to ø or a word for it (`unknown = 0`) is refused where it is written, with its line and code; wap's size ceiling follows by 4 nodes (0 net core in core/rules/lowering.wap, standing OK; wap-supervisor: sound at 5c1a983f)",
