   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiP-hbA",
   "title": "wap format writes a function's result type as…",
   "body": "Original title: wap format writes a function's result type as 'f() as T :=' where the colon is canonical\n\nSeen by wap-fixer on theory-census: `wap format` rewrites `f(): T :=` as `f() as T :=` and drops brace spacing across wap/extensions/theory. wiki/conversion.md:152 makes `:` canonical (`wap fix` writes it). The tree uses both (63 files with `as`, 77 with `:`). Format must write the canonical form.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317157474\n\nfixed on main by 7d05a190 (merge format-colon-result: wap format writes a definition's result type after a colon, f(x) as int becomes f(x): int; test_native 'wap format writes a result type after a colon' pins it). Checked 2026-11-26: format of wap/core/paths.wap writes beside(…): text :=.",
   "state": "CLOSED",
