  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiX3tfw",
   "title": "native binary takes a non-number memory or time…",
   "body": "Original title: The native binary takes a non-number memory or time limit as zero\n\naudit 2026-11-25 tangential (b): extensions/native/driver.wap:94 atol turns a non-number --memory-gb/--seconds into 0. Fix exists on branch bools-as-numbers-dropped (cap_given, +5 net in an extension): needs the user's OK (extension change over 3 lines); split out of that landing.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=317665588\n\nuser OK 2026-11-25 (extension) via wap-interviewer, standing: small change: driver.wap refuses a --memory-gb/--seconds value that isn't a whole number (cap_given, +5, no form), branch native-cap-option-numbers cd1c8fce\n\ncap_given (driver.wap: --memory-gb/--seconds refuse a non-number) OK'd by wap-interviewer 2026-11-25 under the small-change rule; lands with bools-as-numbers-dropped\n\ncorrection: the earlier 'standing: small change' note was the interviewer's own call, not covered by a standing OK. Now: user OK 2026-11-25 (extension) via wap-interviewer: popup 'Land it' for driver.wap cap_given +5 (commit 61ff02aa on bools-as-numbers-dropped)",
