 "relative-compiler-library-path": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhL9CnA",
  "title": "A program compiled by a compiler given by a…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T08:20:50Z",
  "key": "relative-compiler-library-path",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T03:51:20Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T08:20:49Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABimVvbg",
   "title": "A program compiled by a compiler given by a…",
   "body": "Original title: A program compiled by a compiler given by a relative path does not run: it names its library by that relative path\n\nRepro in /Volumes/Worktrees/derived-words-library: wap data/wap-tests/wap1-<hash>/wap1.wasm data/profile/hello.wap $PWD/data/profile/hello.wasm, then wap data/profile/hello.wasm → 'wap: no module data/wap-tests/wap1-<hash>/types-….wasm at data/profile/data/wap-tests/…, as data/profile/hello.wasm names it'. The written module imports its types library by the compiler's relative path, which the runner reads relative to the module's folder. An absolute compiler path works. Expected: the import names the library by an absolute path (or one relative to the module).\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318573168\n\nbranch: relative-compiler-library-path (2026-11-26)\n\nWIP, not for landing: branch tip dc0d8156 makes program.folder absolute (types only). That breaks the relocatable seed tools (test_native, standalone). The general fix is to name each import by its path from the output module's folder; it needs core, and the supervisor is choosing among about +9 core lines, about +2 core lines, or parking.\n\nOption (a) built at c3d42937, not landed, waiting for the user's yes via wap-interviewer.\n- Rule: an import path from the root stays as it is; a relative one is written as the path from the output module's folder.\n- Core: +13 net code lines.\n- Tests: modules/cli/os/files and test_self green; test_native shows only main's 4 console failures.\n- After the next seed refresh, path_from and rooted move to types/host.wap.\n\nInterviewer: (a) measured at +13 net core code (+6 comments), tip c3d42937, about +3 after the seed refresh; queued for the user's morning popup, not landed.\n\nuser 2026-11-26 via interviewer: not (a). A compiled compiler uses the compiled modules beside it, in its own folder, found through the program's folder (the running program's own path, not an environment variable). Rebuild the fix that way, measure, back to the interviewer if it exceeds +3 core.\n\nRebuilt per the user's 2026-11-26 rule, 0 core: branch relative-compiler-library-path-2, tip 8affafcc (the old branch keeps the rejected option a). types: program.folder read from the root. native linker: a module missing where its import names it is found by its file name beside the importer. New test_native line. native 67 ✓, modules/cli/os/files 110 ✓, self 95 ✓. land: relative-compiler-library-path-2 8affafcc. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/handoff/relative-compiler-library-path.patch\n\nFixed in [f214d429](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/f214d429afc90fee3d33f8cf279eabf71c6a3d1a): merge relative-compiler-library-path-2: a compiler named by a relative path finds its library: program.folder is read from the root, and the native linker finds a missing module beside its importer by its file name (0 core; user 2026-11-26)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": [
     {
      "login": "pannous"
     }
    ]
   },
