 "fact-ids": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhL9HE0",
  "title": "Finding a node's fact walks all its facts by name",
  "updated": "2026-11-27T01:43:40Z",
  "key": "fact-ids",
  "agent": "",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "",
  "assignees": [],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-27T00:31:43Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABima04Q",
   "title": "Finding a node's fact walks all its facts by name",
   "body": "Original title: Finding a node's fact walks all its facts by name; small fact ids would make it cheap\n\nSelf compile profile at main 31e3fcc9: fact_name 3.6%, fact_of 2.6%, meta_unwrapped 2.5%, text == 4.4% self time of the samples (the == share is all text compares, not only facts). facts-by-name-speed (text == by place first) saved only 1.4%: most compares in a fact scan are mismatches, which already stop at the length or the first byte; the cost is the scan of Key nodes and the matches on each. Design: fact names as an enum (or ints from one registry in core/stage.wap), facts held in a Meta as (id, value) pairs or a small map, has_fact/fact_of comparing ints. Expected gain: up to the ~9% those functions take, realistically 4–6% of instructions retired. Core cost: core/stage.wap's fact words (~15 lines changed), every fact constant (TYPE, DEFINED_AT, DEFINER … ~40) becomes an enum case, and the readers that match a fact's Key by hand (with_facts_of, attributes_of in nodes.wap) adapt; net about 0 to +10 lines. A design question for the user (wap-interviewer, morning).\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318577741\n\nDesign question sent to wap-interviewer (2026-11-26):\n- (A) fact names as one enum Fact with int ids: core net about +5, after a seed refresh, about 3–5% gain.\n- (B) TYPE in a fixed Meta slot: core about +5, after a seed refresh, about 2–3%.\n- (C) leave it. Recommended: C, revisited with a fresh profile after funcref lands.\nRead counts: TYPE 11, DEFINED_AT 10, DEFINER 8. 48 fact names in 25 core files; facts are core-only.\n\nInterviewer (night, reversible, 0 core): option C, leave it. Fact lookups stay a scan by name. Reopen with option A (fact names become an enum of ids, net about +5 core, after a seed refresh) if a profile taken after funcref-calls-by-table lands still shows the fact words above 5% of self time. Option B (a fixed slot for TYPE) is out: it favours one fact by hand.\n\nProfile 2026-11-26 on main 90782c24 (after funcref): fact lookups by text name take about 20% of a self-compile's busy time: text == 9.4% self, fact_name 6.3%, fact_of 4.5%. The one_text fast path (facts-by-name-speed) is in; the rest needs fact ids in core/stage.wap.\n\nPlan (2026-11-26, for the user's OK; no core edit before it).\nMeasured: fact lookups by text name about 20% of a self-compile's busy time (text == 9.4%, fact_name 6.3%, fact_of 4.5%, wasmtime perfmap profile at 90782c24). On the native run, where GC takes 46%, expect about 8-12% fewer instructions.\nWhat a fact id is: a case of one enum Fact in core/stage.wap, which lists every fact a stage writes (about 50: type, defined_at, definer, binding, result_unknown, …), each with the comment its constant has today. A fact stays a node's Meta entry Key(key, Op.Colon, value); its key holds the case's number in place of the name's text, so fact_of, has_fact and with_fact compare ints. Where a fact is shown, the case's name is printed, so dumps read as today.\nCore: the 50 one-line text constants (TYPE = \"type\", spread over core/) become the enum's cases in stage.wap (lines moved, comments kept), the 198 call sites write Fact.type for TYPE (same lines), stage.wap gets its own without-fact by number (+3, since nodes.wap's with_attribute compares names as text, and the seed's types module can't take a new word). Estimate: about +3 net code lines.\nTrack T: no collision. notes/coc-plan.md keeps core/stage.wap, and its checked facts hold a judgement's number in a fact's value, not its key.\n\nuser 2026-11-26 via interviewer: OK to land (gc heap 2 GB 0 core / fact ids +3 core / no double prepare +3 core)\n\napproved (user 2026-11-26), parked: after the nested match in fact_of (−3.3%, 0 lines, branch fact-ids) the ids would save about 2-4% for +3 core and about 200 call sites; fact_of's remaining 11.4% self is the scan over a node's facts, and only ~1% of samples is text == from fact_of.\n\nwap-supervisor: sound at dc9731b2 (a84dd421 fact_of's one nested match, −3.3%; dc9731b2 same_definer reads its first id once, −0.5%; both 0 net).\n\nland: fact-ids 7ab80094\n\nMeasured 2026-11-26 on interned-names 73c53bda (wasmtime perfmap + sample, 17061 running samples): fact_of 7.9% self, text == 10.1% self, but only 4.7% of =='s samples come from fact_of (about 1.2% of all); fact_of's self time is the scan over a node's Meta entries, which ids keep. Expected gain of ids under 2%: not built (supervisor's 2% bar). Main callers of fact_of: definer_id 11.5%, same_definer 8.7%, signature_key 7.5%.\n\nclosed: fact ids measured under 2% (fact_of's cost is the Meta scan, ids keep it); not built. The 0-line fact_of speedups landed in 7ab80094.\n\ndup?: fact-list-copy (by score, 2026-11-27)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
    "nodes": []
