   "title": "The typing stage holds types as kernel terms, one…",
   "body": "Original title: The typing stage holds types as kernel terms, one representation instead of written notation\n\nT3b of notes/coc-t3.md (user 2026-11-25 via wap-interviewer: one representation, about +300 lines). Branch types-as-terms in /Volumes/Worktrees/coc-t3b.\n\nAdded by wap-theory-reads-types with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318694406\n\nbranch: types-as-terms (2026-11-26)\n\nland: types-as-terms 82ac269b. Careful path: test_hello, compiler-growth, all 22 theory files (388 ✓), test_self (95 ✓), the regressed areas (records types variants functions_calls lists events tasks regex packed: only wanted files and test_tasks' known red fail), census 2832/2832 typed. Speed self-compile +2.7% (302370 → 310433 M), warm hello +1.6%. Size ceiling 174382 (supervisor: within +300 lines). Patch: ~/Library/Logs/warp/coc-t3/types-as-terms-82ac269b.patch\n\nland: types-as-terms 58584921 (replaces 82ac269b, after wap-supervisor review points 1-4). Checked: test_hello, compiler-growth, 22 theory files + 32 areas + test_self (1036 ✓; only *_wanted and test_tasks' known red fail), census 2831/2831. Speed +3.8% self, +2.3% warm hello. Size ceiling 174358. Patch: ~/Library/Logs/warp/coc-t3/types-as-terms-58584921.patch\n\nwap-supervisor: sound (58584921). Handed to wap-integrator. Follow-up after landing: a refusal naming two records of one name gives each declaration's file and line (own branch).\n\nFixed in [834b7b79](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/834b7b795abd654ffbb4271ece4095dae266d628): merge types-as-terms: T3b of the coc plan, every type a kernel term (a word applied to its parts), one representation; written types read into terms at one door and spelled back for messages and keys; facts name a type by its place in the compile's table, so 31 comparisons by computing became ==; one rule for a record's identity (user 2026-11-25 via wap-interviewer; wap-supervisor: sound at 58584921)",
