 "letters-as-holes": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhL-6F8",
  "title": "Type letters and unknown item types become holes…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T15:00:10Z",
  "key": "letters-as-holes",
  "agent": "wap-theory-reads-types",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T08:00:41Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T15:00:10Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABioV0UQ",
   "title": "Type letters and unknown item types become holes…",
   "body": "Original title: Type letters and unknown item types become holes of the unifier, and letters.wap goes\n\nT3c of notes/coc-t3.md (user 2026-11-25 via wap-interviewer). Branch letters-as-holes off types-as-terms 82ac269b, /Volumes/Worktrees/coc-t3c; rebased once T3b lands.\n\nAdded by wap-theory-reads-types with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318695519\n\ndup?: theory-unifier (by score, 2026-11-26)\n\nbranch: letters-as-holes (2026-11-26)\n\nExplored, no edits yet (branch at 82ac269b). Blockers for unifier holes: (1) unify.wap answered() checks each answer's type with kernel type_of, which refuses a constant the environment does not declare (environment.wap:203), so a hole cannot take int or list<int> until the type words are kernel declarations (T3b's plan row listed 'the type words declared in wap/types'; T3b deferred it). (2) -> and fn take any number of parts: no fixed kernel type. (3) unify.wap alike_made compares constants by name, not id (line 107): two records named Program would unify. (4) letters.wap's bound_as is more than equality: boxing into any/number, char read as text, shapes narrowing, wrapping into T?; those stay as conversions around unify. Callers outside letters.wap: unified 11, type_keyed 8, has_unknowns 7, unknown_type 6, has_letters 5, settled_type 5.\n\nReleased 2026-11-26 by wap-worker: agent gone (wap-worker); branch: letters-as-holes (pushed, not merged)\n\nSupervisor ruling (2026-11-26), for T3c onward: don't port read.wap's overload weights into analyze, that is nearest (read.wap:584-600), TRIAL_LIMIT and the numeral special cases at read.wap:458-485. The rule is numerals at the expected type, then the most specific overload by conversion order (plan §4).\n\nReleased 2026-11-26 by wap-worker: agent gone (wap-worker); branch: letters-as-holes (pushed, not merged)\n\nland: coc-t3c 1dc4004a — T3c1 (type words declared in the kernel environment, function types as Pi, lambda words, alike_made by id). Careful path: suite 2856 ✓ (reds = main's test_graphics/test_optimize + guarded flake under load), test_self ✓, census 2838/2838, size ceiling 174841 (+303); speed +0.9% self, −1.7% hello vs 58584921; core +26 net. T3c2 next on its own branch.\n\nT3c2 plan (explored read-only on coc-t3c 1dc4004a):\n1. Holes. TypingState gets one Elaboration over TYPES.environment, made per compile. α: unknown_type(s) becomes hole(el, α, Type), a kernel Free. settled_type and facts_settled become filled(el, t); has_unknowns becomes t.holds_free (O(1), was a walk). all_settled answers every unanswered hole with any. Letters T, U: at each call (letters_bound) the definition's letter words are replaced by fresh holes, and each argument is unified with the kernel unifier unified(el, wanted, given). The Binding lists, type_keyed, type_substituted and bound_as go; a call's answers are read back by filled. _ in a written type: the same hole as a letter that is named nowhere else.\n2. What stays as analyze code: the fits unification doesn't give, tried when unify refuses an argument, in this order: wraps (a T? given a value), read_type and reads_as (a char as text, a range as list<int>, an atom as Node), boxed fits, a shape for its narrowed type, a function value against a function type (function_value_bound, written_parameters, value_function_typed, still through the instance machinery), and the deferred and distinct-instances bookkeeping (deferred_typed, distinct_instances, same_instance) over filled types. letters.wap's 235 lines become about 90, moved into calls.wap and function_values.wap; the file goes. fits.wap's bare_fit and joined_settling's settling go to kernel equality (−45). No ported weights: overloads by conversion order only.\n3. Core cost: about −235 letters, −45 fits, +90 moved, +25 for instantiation and the conversion fallback ≈ −165 net, within the plan's −169 −45 +60 band.\n4. Speed risk, high (T3c1 used 0.9% of the 5%, so about 4.1% is left):\n- holes.wap's taken_back copies Found (answers, problems, scope) on every trial, and overload trials and argument fits trial constantly. With one hole per letter per call, the answers map grows, so the copy cost grows quadratically.\n- answered() type-checks every answer with kernel type_of.\nMitigations, measured after step 1:\n- (a) taken_back keeps an undo trail instead of a copy, about +20 in core/analyze/holes.wap; it speeds theory too;\n- (b) a letter's hole is made only when the parameter holds a letter, and no hole is made for an argument without unknowns;\n- (c) answered() skips the type check for an answer made of declared type words of the right arity;\n- (d) letters of a finished call are answered and never revisited, so they stay out of copies.\nIf still over 4%: stop and report with the profile.\n5. Outcome test, backed by wiki/list.md (t = [] then t += \"a\" gives [\"a\"]): an α settled through a letter, in test/test_lists.wap: first_of(xs: list<T>): T := xs#1; t = []; t += \"a\"; check(\"an empty list started with [] takes a text, and a generic reads its item as one\", first_of(t) + \"b\", \"ab\"). The census and identity(3) stay green.\nOrder: holes for α first (smallest diff, measures the copy cost), then letters, then letters.wap's removal; each its own commit, careful path at the end.\n\nbranch: coc-t3c2 (off coc-t3c 1dc4004a), /Volumes/Worktrees/coc-t3c2\n\nstep 1 landed on coc-t3c2 2ecf4aea (α as kernel holes): self-compile +1.6% against T3c1, +2.6% for T3c in all; about 2.4% left (wap-supervisor). Step 2 design:\n(a) letters_bound instantiates the definition's letters as fresh holes once per call: the written parameter types are substituted letter to hole. Each argument then binds through the same conversion-aware unified, where a letter is now simply an unknown, so the bound_as path covers both, is_letter is read only at instantiation, and has_letters becomes has_unknowns on the instantiated types.\n(b) An overload trial's bindings stay a local Binding list, keyed by the hole's name, and only the chosen call settles them through settled_by and the kernel's unified. Trials then need no taken_back, and the undo trail is needed only if measurement says so.\n(c) The written result type is substituted with the call's holes and then filled.\nStep 3: letters.wap's remains move to calls.wap and function_values.wap, and the file goes.\n\nlanded: coc-t3c T3c1 as 90782c24 (land note done; T3c2 next)\n\nland: coc-t3c2-land 3776d31f — steps 1+2 (wap-supervisor: sound at 80ab52e1; careful path green; the census's copied state fixed; SIZE_NODES 176050). Step 3 continues on coc-t3c2 (17860c16: the binder meets holes only). Side finding: a refused call prints a hole's spelling, 'no size_of takes (α1)'; it should name an item type not settled yet.\n\nland: coc-t3c2 ff72fa5a — step 3 (binder meets holes only; no answer holds a letter hole; SIZE_NODES 176202). T3c3 on coc-t3c3 a40e6cdd: answers keyed by hole id, spelling cache gone, full suite green, self-compile 308194 M (+3.4% vs T3b).\n\nland: coc-t3c3 e18f1d2c — T3c3 (answers by hole id, spelling cache gone; -0.9% instructions; SIZE_NODES 176441). T3d continues on coc-t3d.\n\nFixed in [2207cd57](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/2207cd5741541f3a41d2175ce65be46e218b9057): merge coc-t3c3: a call's answers for holes are keyed by the hole's id, a letter's name only in the types the definition writes; hole_text and its cache go; wap's size ceiling follows to the measured 176441 nodes (Called and Answer), the self-compile retires 1% fewer instructions (track T, user 2026-11-25; wap-supervisor: sound at e18f1d2c)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
