 "console-misreads-lines": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhL_nD0",
  "title": "The console misreads lines on main",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T04:59:15Z",
  "key": "console-misreads-lines",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T04:47:06Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T04:59:15Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABipDKCg",
   "title": "The console misreads lines on main",
   "body": "Original title: The console misreads lines on main: test_native fails 4 console tests\n\nOn main (seen at 423576f4), test/wap/test_native.sh fails 4 tests: 'wap repl is the console' (gives 22, expected 42); 'the console keeps a definition and runs each line once' (this bracket is never closed: ((x: int) as int := x * 2); 'the console runs a line that only prints once, after a value'; 'the console keeps a value for the lines after it' (nothing defines =, neither as a function nor as a field of int: (Get 5 \"=\")). Find the breaking commit by bisecting, then fix its cause.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318741565\n\nbranch: console-misreads-lines (2026-11-26)\n\nland: console-misreads-lines 1bad5e6f\n\nSince 6568b5d7, \"\" + t is t itself, so a text a host fills in place (a reused read buffer) is aliased by it. A reader into a reused buffer must copy (byte_text, or a fresh text_made per read).\n\nFixed in [aa694445](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/aa694445427e574cef8c03177c1d6351eac6bfb2): merge console-misreads-lines: the native console reads each byte into a fresh text (editing.wap's byte), since \"\" + cell gives back cell itself after 6568b5d7; test_native's console checks green again (extensions −1, fixing a red main)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
