   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABipUQhQ",
   "title": "The native wap says a missing imported module…",
   "body": "Original title: The native wap says a missing imported module once per import, a dozen times for one file\n\nwap/extensions/native/run.wap imports_linked tries instance_defined for every import of a .wasm module the linker does not hold; for a missing file module_path (linking.wap) says 'wap: no module … as … names it' each time (about 12 lines for hello's library). One line per missing module.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318759770\n\nbranch: native-missing-module-once (2026-11-26)\n\nland: native-missing-module-once 23b67230\n\nFixed in [54b42643](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/54b42643b97a4c13ecf4621421a41b536441ca26): merge native-missing-module-once: the native wap reports a missing imported module once, not once per import (0 core; wap-supervisor: sound)",
