  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABipaR9w",
   "title": "use music and use audio do not bring sound's…",
   "body": "Original title: use music and use audio do not bring sound's words, as the wiki's sound page promises\n\nwiki/sound.md: \"use music and use audio are other names of use sound\". lib/music.wap is `use sound`, but a use brings on only operators, rules and aliases, so `use music; midi(A4)` only works because naming a standard word brings sound in, with the hint 'midi comes from sound: write use sound'. Supervisor's recommendation: a module made only of uses forwards what they give (a bundle). Uses: music, audio, extensions/rules.wap, a future use graphics.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318766148\n\nbranch: use-bundles (2026-11-26)\n\nprototype at 07364d37 (branch use-bundles): given_by in core/pipeline.wap modules_of_uses, +4 code lines. Question sent to wap-interviewer: (A) bundles, (B) drop the alias from the wiki, (C) leave it.\n\n07364d37: areas modules, sound and use green; only the wanted files are red (test_sound_wanted, test_use_wanted), both red on main too. Queued for the user's morning decision via wap-interviewer, recommendation A.\n\nuser 2026-11-26 via interviewer: (C) leave it. use music works through the standard-module fallback; no bundle mechanism, branch use-bundles not landed.\n\nClosed as obsolete: user 2026-11-26: (C) leave it; branch use-bundles 07364d37 kept on origin as the record",
   "state": "CLOSED",
