 "class-setter": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhMAQP4",
  "title": "Writing a name cannot run code of the class it…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T10:05:25Z",
  "key": "class-setter",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T05:44:12Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T10:05:24Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiprg4g",
   "title": "Writing a name cannot run code of the class it…",
   "body": "Original title: Writing a name cannot run code of the class it holds, so on change x and whenever cannot be built in plain wap\n\nPrototype on branch class-setter: in name_set_typed (core/analyze/types.wap), a value the name's type does not hold goes through that type's set(to: v, of: x), the way an item's write goes through set(to:, of:, at:). +1 net core line. Waiting for the user's decision via wap-interviewer (2026-11-26); signals then become plain wap with x = signal(0).\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318783742\n\nbranch: class-setter (2026-11-26)\n\nInterviewer: measured +1 net core, tip 3982e352; stays queued for the user's morning popup together with the wiki spelling x = signal(0); not landed.\n\nlib/signals.wap on the branch, tip ed0dcd4a: test_signals 5 ✓. Spelling: x = signal(0), whenever x.value > 5 { global n += 1 }. Gaps: a Signal does not read as its value (x > 5), and a block's write of a global needs global (test_block_wanted twice). Held for the user.\n\nInterviewer: signals ported at ed0dcd4a (test_signals 5 ✓). The getter twin (whenever x > 5) joins the morning question; worker measures it on a branch. A write of an any value to a Signal name trying the conversion first: an edge case, accepted as is.\n\nInterviewer: getter measured +3 core at ae18b2d6; setter + getter +4; queued for the user's morning popup, not landed.\n\nuser 2026-11-26 via interviewer: setter + getter (+4 core) approved, signals in lib/signals.wap, wiki/signal.md changes `x = 0` to `x = signal(0)` (approved).\n\nland: class-setter f8007dd2 (user yes 2026-11-26, setter+getter +4 core). Wiki: wap.wiki branch class-setter-wiki a3eb251 (signal.md: listened variables written x = signal(10), approved). Areas 382 ✓, only test_signal_wanted red (wanted file). Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/handoff/class-setter.patch\n\nland: class-setter 14ea5929. Recursion fixed: the get retry rebinds the arguments, and word_scopes gives list<list<Signature>>. self 95 ✓, census ✓ with ceiling 175069 (main 174871 + 198), signals 9 ✓. Core +4 net. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/handoff/class-setter.patch\n\nFixed in [a7179dcc](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/a7179dcceb6fd361aa2d6d2cb8126adca1b073e6): merge class-setter: writing a value of another type into a signal calls its class's set (x = 5), a signal used where no word takes it reads through get (whenever x > 5), a typed copy reads the value; lib/signals.wap replaces signals.warp (+4 net core; user 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer) spec: wiki/signal.md",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
