   "title": "test_graphics is red",
   "body": "Original title: test_graphics is red: lib/sound.wap and lib/image.wap both define save, and a free standard word may come from only one module\n\nRed on main since sound-library-port (ebc8cbf2): test_graphics, 'lib/sound.wap and lib/image.wap both define save: write the use of one' (core/analyze/modules.wap standard_word_bound). Decision (wap-supervisor): (b2) definitions of one name taking different types are overloads wherever they live, so a free standard word brings every standard module defining it. test_graphics stays red until it lands. reds: test_graphics.wap\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318809730\n\nbranch: sound-save-clash (2026-11-26)\n\nBuilt at d63719d2 (branch sound-save-clash): −2 net core lines. test_graphics is green; test_self 95 ✓. Waiting for wap-supervisor's sound under the standing OK.\n\nland: sound-save-clash d63719d2 (supervisor: sound; standing OK small fix)\n\nFixed in [0d551cdc](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/0d551cdcddb7c6838e5323509d6cb524ab04a685): merge sound-save-clash: a word several standard modules define brings in all of them, their definitions one word's overloads, so draw's canvas save and sound's save no longer clash; fixes test_graphics red since sound-library-port (standing OK small fix, −2 net core; wap-supervisor: sound, ruling b2)",
