   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiq_BFg",
   "title": "The stage-2 fixed point and the speed gates are…",
   "body": "Original title: The stage-2 fixed point and the speed gates are checked by no script, and _wanted files that fail to compile hide 496 checks\n\n(audit 2026-11-26) item 7.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318872274\n\nbranch: stage-fixed (2026-11-26)\n\nland: stage-fixed aecbbea3. test_self: fixed point wap2==wap1 + instructions ceiling 172517638896 (+1%). run.sh: _wanted programs compile without each refused statement (red by check name); reds.txt re-recorded for all 99 _wanted files: 357 refused, 2 wrong, 5 green, 4 blocked whole (meta, strict, pattern_matching, type). Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/stage-fixed/stage-fixed.patch\n\nFixed in [a7dc36dc](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/a7dc36dc50a09c9b5b1996c856352fdd5eced271): merge stage-fixed: test_self's stage 2 checks that wap2 is wap1's bytes and that wap1 compiling wap's compiler retires at most 1% more instructions than SELF_COMPILE_INSTRUCTIONS, a ratchet like the census ceiling; run.sh compiles a _wanted program that does not compile without each statement wap refuses, so each refusal is its own red line and the rest runs; test/reds.txt re-recorded for the _wanted files (wap-supervisor: approved at aecbbea3; audit item 7)\n\ntest_self's instructions-retired count moves on one commit between runs: 000eadba read 164365816233 and 164166720945, e0dea1d8 163573119884 and 163763728672 (up to ~0.5%; machine load 7-14). The 1% ratchet then flaps on noise; it may want a noise band or a median of runs. Ratchet raised to 164166720945 in a33ea0da (integrator)",
