   "title": "The native commands keep a command's words as one…",
   "body": "Original title: The native commands keep a command's words as one spaced text, though native code now holds lists of texts\n\nwap/extensions/native/commands.wap:11 and programs.wap:16 carry a DEBT: 'a native build makes a list of texts a GC type (wasm2c refuses it)'. Native code now uses list<text> locals (run.wap imports_linked unlinked, console.wap history, commands.wap:67 lines), so the reason may be stale (audit 2026-11-26 item 9). Check whether a class field list<text> builds natively; if yes, pay off: Usage.words: list<text> and usage.words.contains(word).\n\nAdded by wap-integrator with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=318873887\n\ndup?: native-function-values (by score, 2026-11-26)\n\nbranch: native-commands (2026-11-26)\n\nland: native-commands 69442544: both DEBTs paid off, the reason stale. Usage.words (commands.wap) and hashed_files (programs.wap) are list<text>; the native wap builds and test_native gives 67 ✓, 0 ✗ with each step. 0 core, extensions/native 17+/21−; test_hello and compiler-growth green on the merge; patches in /Volumes/Worktrees/native-commands/data/patches.\n\nFixed in [a3aa35b0](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/a3aa35b00cc20da5d14b7b7f394382e46b8c106c): merge native-commands: the native wap's command words and hashed files are lists of texts, read by contains and is empty, now that a native build takes a list of texts (0 core, extensions/native)",
