   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiuGXpQ",
   "title": "The native wap starts with a 128 MB GC heap, so a…",
   "body": "Original title: The native wap starts with a 128 MB GC heap, so a compile of wap spends almost half its time collecting\n\nProfile 2026-11-26: GC is 46% of the native wap's busy time on a self-compile, plus 5.5% memmove. Measured with GC_HEAP_BYTES (wap/extensions/native/run.wap) on the same wap1: 128 MB 285 G instructions, 1 GB 252 G, 2 GB 211-237 G, 4 GB 204-208 G. A compile's RSS: 1.1 GB, 1.3-1.8 GB, 2.1 GB, 3.4 GB. A small program's RSS is unchanged (44 MB). Branch native-gc-heap sets 2 GB (no core): self 95 ✓, native 66 ✓ 1 ✗ — 'keeps the compiler's machine code beside it' finds 2 cwasm because the seed tools are built by the installed wap (128 MB settings hash) and the tree's native writes its own; gone after a seed refresh.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319077805\n\ndup?: self-compile-allocation (by score, 2026-11-26)\n\nNot for landing on my own: the interviewer's night decision on self-compile-allocation was 'A, allocate less (not B, the 1 GB start heap)'. New numbers sent to wap-interviewer 2026-11-26; branch native-gc-heap 017bf4c9 kept unpushed until a yes.\n\nuser yes 2026-11-26 via interviewer (replaces the night's 'A, not B'). land: native-gc-heap 3339fd5b (merged with main, test_hello ✓, self 95 ✓). One native red: 'the native wap keeps the compiler's machine code beside it' (2 cwasm: the seed tools are compiled by the installed wap with the old GC_HEAP_BYTES, so the engine-settings hash differs); cleared by the next scripts/refresh-seed.sh, whose seed carries 2 GB.\n\nFixed in [7c852aa6](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/7c852aa6f27744700dc0e1fd85cb8ca64d117573): merge native-gc-heap: the native wap's GC heap is 2 GB instead of 128 MB, so the self-compile retires 17-26% fewer instructions; a compile holds 2.1 GB instead of 1.1 GB, small programs are unchanged (0 core; user 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer)\n\ndup?: cpu-vs-instructions (by score, 2026-11-26)",
