 "long-path-cost": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhMFFeo",
  "title": "A compile of wap whose files are named by long…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T22:41:54Z",
  "key": "long-path-cost",
  "agent": "wap-native-no-layout-any",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T20:41:38Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T22:41:54Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiuczaA",
   "title": "A compile of wap whose files are named by long…",
   "body": "Original title: A compile of wap whose files are named by long absolute paths takes 4% more than with short relative ones\n\nMeasured 2026-11-26: wap1 --sources compiler.wap run from the compiler's folder: 6528a968's compiler (program.folder relative, files named core/…) 345 G instructions; f214d429's (program.folder read from the root, files named /Volumes/Worktrees/…/core/…) 359 G (+4%, the integrator's +3.3%). 6528a968's compiler on f214d429's sources: 344-345 G, so the sources cost nothing; the file names' length does. File names are compared and hashed as text throughout (DEFINED_AT facts, module keys, standard_sources). A file id (or one interned text per file, so text == answers at once) would make the cost independent of the path.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319100394\n\nTried the no-core route 2026-11-26 (branch long-path-cost 6d24280d, not pushed): program.folder relative again plus linked_name naming the held library from the root (with use types/host.wap). The --sources compile got 2.2% cheaper (354.8 -> 346.9 G), but the written import stayed relative (wap-seed/types-<hash>.wasm), so test_native's 'compiler named by a relative path' line went red: inside the compile absolute_path seems to give ø although the host names fd 3 by its absolute path (wasmtime trace). Not chased further; the general fix stays file ids (or one interned text per file).\n\nbranch: long-path-cost (2026-11-26)\n\nbranch long-path-cost d33bca0a (measurement only): definer ids \"<path>#n\" are in every place_key; with the path cut short the --sources self compile retires 4.3% fewer instructions (237.5 G -> 227.2 G). A file's place in its wap folder is not unique (native build reads seed's and tree's types/text_bytes.wap), so the fix is a per-compile file number (map in core/stage.wap) that the warm state packs and restores: ~+3 core, ~+3 extensions/warm. Asked the user via wap-interviewer (2026-11-26).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 (interviewer popup): option A, file numbers in definer ids; number = place in errors.wap sources_read (one table, errors still name the path); ~+3 core stage.wap, +3 extensions/warm.wap\n\nland: long-path-cost d996f52f — user OK 2026-11-26 (option A via wap-interviewer): definer ids name a file by its place in errors.wap sources_read; self compile --sources -5.3% (235.7 G -> 223.2 G). +5 core code lines (merge message says +3, wrong), warm +3, census 179120 (+111). hello, 8 areas 328 ✓, self 96 ✓, census, growth green\n\nInterviewer 2026-11-26: +5 core (est. ~+3) +3 extensions/warm.wap, census +111, −5.3% instructions: user OK option A, standing: small overrun (the 2 extra lines are the sources_read reuse the user asked for).\n\nFixed in [ade14e3b](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/ade14e3b150d4951859f8eb5d541c33860b12c55): merge long-path-cost: a definer id is <file number>#n in place of <path>#n, a file's number its place in sources_read, which the warm state packs and restores; the --sources self-compile retires about 5% fewer instructions; wap's size ceiling follows by 111 nodes (user 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer, option A: +5 core, of about +3 asked, for the reuse of sources_read; wap-supervisor: sound at d996f52f)",
