  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABivlDnQ",
   "title": "Five small refusals and fixes the interviewer…",
   "body": "Original title: Five small refusals and fixes the interviewer decided are not built yet\n\nwap-interviewer 2026-11-26, each ≤3 core under the standing OK, each needs wap-supervisor's sound and one outcome line:\n1. C import clash: refuse it (refuse-never-guess).\n2. A block argument to a defaulted parameter: passed, not run (bug fix).\n3. A standard-module word across feeds/random: drop the refusal at standard bind (±3).\n4. Indexing an any parameter: a clear refusal instead of the internal error.\n5. try of ø: refuse it.\nNot to build: template typing waits for kernel types (T4); lib/list.wap positions from 1 stay.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319171949\n\nbranch: interviewer-small-fixes (2026-11-26)\n\nSupervisor review 2026-11-26: items 2-5 sound (standing OK). Item 1, C import clash 76fc7b26 at +4 core: sound, foreign_shape to be bound once; it waits on the user's OK via wap-interviewer. If no, it lands without that commit.\n\nbranch interviewer-small-fixes tip b8737f05 (merged with origin/main 37d5bd3f; hello, growth and census green, size 176315). Items 2, 3, 4 and 5 are sound (supervisor). Item 1 (76fc7b26 + dd267430, +4 core) waits on the user's answer via wap-interviewer; if no, the landing is redone without those two commits. Patch: ~/Library/Logs/warp/handoff/interviewer-small-fixes.patch\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 (interviewer popup): C import clash refusal 76fc7b26 at +4 core lands\n\nland: interviewer-small-fixes d6573f3f (merged with origin/main; hello, growth, census green, size 176593; 13 areas 321 ✓, only test_errors_wanted red by design). Item 1 user 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer. Patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/handoff/interviewer-small-fixes.patch\n\nFixed in [5b0393bf](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/5b0393bf9fcc3209344ce1332198d61c3eeec6b3): merge interviewer-small-fixes: a block is a function value before a defaulted parameter; a try whose body gives nothing beside a catch that gives a value is refused where no type is wanted; a C function declared again with other types is refused, naming the other declaration; outcome lines for the cross-module standard word and x[\"url\"]; wap's size ceiling follows to 176593 (+5 core: +4 user 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer, +1 standing OK; wap-supervisor: sound)",
