 "types-relative-path": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhMHIVk",
  "title": "The compiler refuses its own types module when it…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T18:21:31Z",
  "key": "types-relative-path",
  "agent": "wap-annotation-attachment-fix",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T13:22:38Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T18:21:30Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABiwijCg",
   "title": "The compiler refuses its own types module when it…",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler refuses its own types module when it is given again by a relative path, so the seed cannot be refreshed\n\nA compiler that holds the library (the seed, wap1 and later) refuses types/types.wap given by a relative path: 'types/text_bytes.wap: byte_count is a function every program has' (core/analyze/calls.wap:405), but takes the same file by its absolute path: one file, two names. Seed wap-seed-2026-11-26-5871bde4 broke test_hello this way, so the lock was reverted (37d5bd3f) and no seed refresh can happen until this lands; test_native's cwasm-count line stays red until then. TODO.md line 2. General fix: a source is known by its resolved path wherever the library's own files are recognized. Path: careful (seed).\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319234393\n\nbranch: types-relative-path (2026-11-26)\n\ntest_native 'the native wap keeps the compiler's machine code beside it' goes red under load: during an area run a second wap-<hash>.cwasm (another engine-settings hash, same seed wap.wasm) is written into the stage's bin/wap-seed (seen in interviewer-small-fixes data/wap-tests/wap1-7440064ed3e70489, 14:05 and 14:22). A separate cause from the seed revert.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 (interviewer popup): wap-annotation-attachment-fix may git revert 2cb321f2 and continue (the earlier No was the supervisor's mistake)\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 (interviewer popup): branch types-library-files fdc011e4, library_place, lands at +8 core in core/pipeline.wap\n\nland: types-library-files 0dce20e0 (careful: test_hello, test_self, the census, refresh-seed --check all green; patches in /Volumes/Worktrees/types-relative-path/data/patches). module_key is the cache key and library_place is a module's identity: a library file is known by its path inside its wap folder (typed_modules, wasm is_library), so the types module given by any path is the library. +8 core code lines plus one comment line; user OK 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer; size ceiling +94 nodes. Then the seed refresh.\n\nland: types-library-files b7e454ab (merged with main at b4d9aca6; green: test_hello, native 67/0, test_self, the census, refresh-seed --check, and the types module compiled relative, absolute and held). Only the types module given as the program is known by its place (own, preparing inside itself, wasm is_library); held and program_modules compare raw spelling, so a program naming host.wap by path keeps it. Debt: held means the modules whose words the library shows to programs; by raw spelling it is right by accident, since a program bringing in one of those files by another path gets it twice. The general rule is held = shown modules by place, private files such as host.wap left out.\n\nFixed in [9cc3a30a](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/9cc3a30a8d59f6ad66eb0c9076b7dd6947c29a28): merge types-library-files: a library file is known by its path inside its wap folder (library_place), so a compiler holding the library takes its own types module, given by a relative path as compile.sh gives it, as the library and not as a second module; a program naming a types file by path, as the native wap names host.wap, keeps it as its own module; wap's size ceiling follows to the measured 178473 nodes (+9 core lines, +6 code, in core/pipeline.wap; user 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer; wap-supervisor: sound at b7e454ab)",
