 "interned-names": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhMK-ZE",
  "title": "The compiler spends a quarter of its time…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T19:27:51Z",
  "key": "interned-names",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T17:09:20Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T19:27:50Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABi0bMig",
   "title": "The compiler spends a quarter of its time…",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler spends a quarter of its time comparing and hashing names as texts\n\nProfile of the self-compile at main a2107d22 (perfmap + /usr/bin/sample, running self time; notes/speed.md): ==(a: text, b: text) 14%, hashed(t: text, size: int) 10% (plus most of % 3.4%), fact_of 7%, meta_unwrapped 4%; the garbage collector 26% is the only bigger share. Names (scopes, name tables, facts, signatures by name) are compared byte by byte and hashed anew at every lookup. Direction: a name read once into a number (interned when the reader meets it), compared and hashed by that number, as fact-ids began for facts (fact-ids, facts-by-name-speed dc97d6d9 did the text == identity fast path). Touches core: the plan with its core lines goes to wap-supervisor first, then the user.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319486353\n\ndup?: facts-by-name-speed (by score, 2026-11-26)\n\nbranch: interned-names (2026-11-26)\n\nstep 1 c77aebbe handed off (map hash low bits, −2.6%, 0 core). Profile after it: text == 15%, hashed 4.9%, fact_of 7.7%, GC 29.5%. Step 2 plan sent to wap-supervisor: place keys as numbers (an intern table in core/stage.wap, place_key → int, TypingState.defines and the Placed lists int-keyed); about +10 net core, 78 uses in 19 files change type; prototype to measure first. Tried and dropped: text == from the end (−0.35%).\n\nstep 2a 9fa8c4cd (branch interned-names): the emitter's functions and globals as map<text, Placed>, −4.9% (249.1 → 236.9 G), +4 net core (3 code + 1 comment), areas 297 ✓. Steps 1 and 2a together: 254.7 → 236.9 G (−7.0%). Profile after them: GC 26.7%, text == 10.1% (from 15%), fact_of 7.9%, hashed 4.5%. Numeric place keys (PlaceKey) estimated at 2-4% for ~25 core lines, warm state included (DEFINER ids are 'file#count' texts packed in it): recommended not to build (wap-supervisor asked).\n\nPlaceKey dropped (wap-supervisor agreed). Step 1: land interned-names-1 c77aebbe (queued). Step 2a 9fa8c4cd: sound; it waits for the user's OK via wap-interviewer (+3 code lines in core/emit, size ceiling +35). Next lever from the profile after both: the garbage collector 27% of running time, fact_of 8% (facts read by name).\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer: option (a). 9fa8c4cd lands at +4 core in core/emit (3 code, 1 comment). The census SIZE_NODES ceiling in test/wap/ratchet_census.sh rises 178246 → 178281 (+35). Self-compile 254.7 → 236.9 G (−7.0%) with step 1. PlaceKey dropped (2-4% left for about 25 core lines). Next lever: GC 27%, fact_of 8%. wap-supervisor: sound.\n\nland: interned-names 06af327c — step 1 (map hash low bits) + 2a (emitter maps, +3 core), user-OK'd; census size 178449; −7.0% self-compile; patch ~/Library/Logs/warp/handoff/interned-names.patch\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 (interviewer popup, correction): census SIZE_NODES +64 in all, 178385 -> 178449 (map hash +35, emitter maps +29); core +4 unchanged\n\nuser 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer: the census ceiling rises +64 in all (178385 → 178449 on main cd6f1b92): step 1 +35, emitter maps +29. Corrects the earlier +35 grant. Core +4 in core/emit, unchanged.\n\nlanded 4efda754 (steps 1 + 2a, −6.4%); worktree removed. Left on the card: the real interned names.",
