  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABi1dxPQ",
   "title": "The compiler allocates the same values again on…",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler allocates the same values again on every call, so a quarter of a self-compile is garbage collection\n\nAllocation profile of the self compile (interned-names 73c53bda, wasmtime copying GC, /usr/bin/sample + perfmap; the wasm caller of each gc_alloc_raw sample, 5189 samples; GC is 26.7% of running samples). Top allocators:\n1. 0 core: types/texts.wap LEAD_BITS := [128, 32, 16, 8] builds its list at every call (4.8% of allocations, plus 0.8% self time), read per character at texts.wap:92/177. Every list constant NAME := [...] does the same; computed once it would be free for all of them (that general form is core).\n2. core/emit/values.wap enum_base(m) (5.0%): builds open_type([], struct_type([TAG_FIELD])) at every call, then added_type finds it again by comparing (added_type is also 9.3% of the text == calls). Keep the index once per module.\n3. core/stage.wap annotation(n, word) (9.4%): annotations_of builds [] or [said] and find a closure at every call, mostly for nodes without annotations; an early ø for a node without the ANNOTATIONS fact allocates nothing.\nAlso high: flat_map 8.1%, get(map<text, Node>) 6.3%, bytes_between 6.1%, int_in 5.8% (an int? result), text + 5.4%, record_declared 5.2%, direct_parts 5.1%, signature_key 4.4%, place_key 4.2%. Script: ~/Library/Logs/warp/profile/callers.py <sample> <perf map> gc_alloc_raw.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319548729\n\nbranch: allocation-hotspots (2026-11-26)\n\nMeasured 2026-11-26 on main 9cc3a30a, self-compile, instructions retired, two runs each (base 262.1/260.2/259.7/259.7 G):\n- annotation() early ø (+1 line): −0.02% (on cd6f1b92), not kept. The gc_alloc_raw caller counts do not predict gains.\n- LEAD_BITS inlined in decoded (throwaway): about −0.6%. The general form (a pure zero-parameter := whose body reads only constants is computed once, wiki/charged.md 'Needless charging') is not built. Writing types/ constants with = instead does not build. Core estimate: a lazily filled global per such getter in the emitter, plus the purity check, about +10 lines. Gain under 1% on today's source.\n- enum_base kept per module (+3 lines, throwaway): −0.78%, under the 1% bar.\n- Bigger lever: added_type (core/emit/wasm.wap) scans every type with list == at each call: 5.8% of samples inclusive. A map from type to index would save most of that, estimated 3-5%, about +4 core lines (a WasmModule field plus the lookup), but it must keep the scan's first-match-outside-a-distinct-group rule. Patches in data/ of the worktree.\n\nbranch allocation-hotspots e9285d44: added_type by a map from type to index, −2.3% self-compile, +3 core code lines, census size +49 (178473 → 178522 on 9cc3a30a), 16 areas 380 ✓ 0 ✗. wap-supervisor: sound; waiting for the user's answer via the supervisor. Dropped: annotation() (−0.02%), enum_base (−0.78%); constant folding stays the wiki's to-do.\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 (interviewer popup): wasm type map e9285d44 lands, +3 core emit/wasm.wap, +1 types/maps.wap, census SIZE_NODES +49 granted\n\nuser OK 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer (option a: +3 core, +1 types/maps.wap, size +49). land: allocation-hotspots f1d2104b; careful path green: hello, growth, 17 areas incl. native and self 447 ✓ 0 ✗, census with ceiling 178586\n\nFixed in [3d419813](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/3d419813fc9185be890353abfddf98501e89f334): merge allocation-hotspots: added_type finds a type by a map from type to index instead of a scan of every type; the self-compile retires about 2% fewer instructions; wap's size ceiling follows by 49 nodes (+3 core in core/emit/wasm.wap, +1 in types/maps.wap, census +49: user OK 2026-11-26 via wap-interviewer; wap-supervisor: sound at f1d2104b)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
