  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T23:01:21Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABi2hRvA",
   "title": "The fix-it for a shared case name suggests…",
   "body": "Original title: The fix-it for a shared case name suggests Shape.Circle(3), which the compiler refuses\n\nWith enum Shape { Circle(r: int), Square(side: int) } used beside an enum Figure { Circle(name: text), Dot }, a bare Circle(3) is refused: 'Circle is a case of each of Shape, Figure: write Shape.Circle or Figure.Circle'. But the spelling it suggests is refused too, even with one enum alone (main 3e3564df): print radius(Shape.Circle(3)) gives 'Circle takes a value for each of its fields: r', and Shape.Circle(r: 3) the same. The named form Circle(r: 3) gives 'the typing stage reads only kernel forms'. Only the bare positional Circle(3) works, so the fix-it leads to a refused form (found on case-name, wap-annotation-attachment-fix).\n\nAdded by wap-annotation-attachment-fix with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319615204\n\ndup?: case-name (by score, 2026-11-26)\n\nbranch: fix-shared-case (2026-11-26)\n\nland: fix-shared-case eab7ae00 (standing OK small fix; wap-supervisor sound at 7b66abb1); checks green, census 179177 = main + 58\n\nFixed in [19f51be9](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/19f51be92d8e454ffac570cb048a62466399fa33): merge fix-shared-case: `Shape.Circle(3)` is that case given its fields, as the shared-case fix-it suggests, and a case's fields or a module word's parameters may be given by name, `Circle(r: 3)`; wap's size ceiling rises by its measured 58 nodes (+2 core in core/analyze, standing OK small fix; wap-supervisor: sound at 7b66abb1)",
