  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABi4by-w",
   "title": "The type page's wanted tests no longer compile at…",
   "body": "Original title: The type page's wanted tests no longer compile at all, so their red lines are counted as fixed\n\ntest/test_type_wanted.wap fails to compile on main: 'Record: no definition takes these values' types' (already at b91b5a92, reported by wap-theory-reads-types via wap-integrator). run.sh then lists 8 of its baseline reds as 'fixed, green now'. Two parts: (1) find the landing that broke it (candidates: e1 551ffd93, library-import-names b91b5a92, native-no-layout-any b42962c8) and fix the compiler, never the test; (2) run.sh: a _wanted file that does not compile is a regression of all its lines, reported loudly, never counted as fixed (test/wap/run.sh baseline compare). wap-supervisor 2026-11-26.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319736475\n\nbranch: type-wanted-broken (2026-11-26)\n\nland: type-wanted-broken b6b95b58. No landing broke test/test_type_wanted.wap: it has refused whole since 2026-11-23 (the wanted generic class Pair<A, B> since 11-24), in the baseline as compiled and ran. The bug: run.sh keyed reds by basename, 14 shared between test/ and test/wap/. Fixed by test_key (script reds wap/<name>), the baseline migrated, and a test that did not compile keeps its baseline reds red. Verified on the 28 shared-name tests: no regression, nothing read as fixed.\n\nFixed in [7ea9eaf1](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/7ea9eaf161c983ace3df51762b399d264dbe25c0): merge type-wanted-broken: run.sh keys a script's reds as wap/<file name>, so a program and a script of one file name keep their reds apart, and a test that does not compile and run through keeps its baseline reds red instead of reading as fixed (test/wap/run.sh, test/reds.txt; no compiler change)",
