  "column_since": "2026-11-27T02:09:22Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABi4fxxQ",
   "title": "Inside a function, global n = n + 1 is refused…",
   "body": "Original title: Inside a function, global n = n + 1 is refused, though the refusal of n += 1 suggests that spelling\n\nn = 1; bump() := { global n = n + 1 } is refused: 'the program changes n after this function is defined: write global n in the function'. The fix-it for n += 1 names 'global n = …'; wiki/charged.md lets global stand on either side. Fix: core/analyze/variables.wap globals_named counts a Set that declares global (global n = …) as declaring n for the block, 0 net lines. Repros: g.wap, g2.wap, g3.wap from wap-supervisor.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319740443\n\nbranch: global-assign (2026-11-26)\n\nland: global-assign 36acc7f8 (handed to wap-integrator; standing OK small fix, sound at 6ef2ea03; ceiling 179250)\n\nFixed in [95cd7400](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/95cd74000f8927cb942b2633b492575c768ca921): merge global-assign: global x = … in a function declares the program's x for the whole function, its own value too, so bump() := { global n = n + 1 } changes the program's n, as the refusal of n += 1 suggests (0 net core lines in core/analyze/variables.wap; standing OK small fix; census +49 measured; wap-supervisor: sound at 6ef2ea03)",
