 "cpu-vs-instructions": {
  "id": "PVTI_lAHOAAfgFs4BsfrazhMO8aI",
  "title": "The compiler retires fewer instructions but takes…",
  "updated": "2026-11-26T22:59:19Z",
  "key": "cpu-vs-instructions",
  "agent": "wap-primitive-lookup-tables",
  "try": "",
  "repeat": "",
  "now_by_todo": "2026-11-26T22:28:29Z",
  "assignees": [
   "pannous"
  ],
  "column": "Done",
  "column_since": "2026-11-26T22:59:19Z",
  "content": {
   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABi4lcuQ",
   "title": "The compiler retires fewer instructions but takes…",
   "body": "Original title: The compiler retires fewer instructions but takes about 10% more CPU time than the seed before it\n\nReported by wap-integrator 2026-11-26. refresh-seed timing: new compiler 16.6 s vs seed 15.0 s (and 15.5 vs 13.6 on --check), while stage2 instructions fell 253 -> 231 G. The refresh before went the other way (17.0 vs 18.0). Suspect native-gc-heap 7c852aa6 (heap 2 GB instead of 128 MB: a compile holds 2.1 GB, page faults / cache misses), or noise. Measure: wall, user+sys and max RSS of a self-compile at 7c852aa6^ vs 7c852aa6 vs main, 5 runs each, niced through job-slot.sh; if the heap is the cause, find the size that keeps the instruction gain without the time loss. wap-supervisor.\n\nAdded by wap-supervisor with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319746466\n\ndup?: native-gc-heap (by score, 2026-11-26)\n\nbranch: cpu-vs-instructions (2026-11-26)\n\nmeasured 2026-11-26 (main de6e7240, interleaved, niced): heap 128M/512M/1G/2G → 21.3/19.6/18.2/15.0 s user, 331/302/275/229 G instr, RSS 2.07 GB at all; 2 GB best. New seed ce6d0bb0 vs old 4e9dd42f on the same host: --sources 15.6 vs 17.3 s, plain 13.8 vs 16.2 s. Cause: wap-beside.sh:83 wap_stage_compiled times the seed without --sources and the new compiler with it (~10% more work). Fix proposed to supervisor: timing rounds use the same command for both.\n\nland: cpu-vs-instructions 8e34eb87 (refresh-seed timing rounds both --sources; --check green 16.9 vs 18.6 s). Heap: 2 GB best on time and instructions, RSS same at every size.\n\nFixed in [dbc67ed7](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/dbc67ed76af765951b65907a48deb472e83cd8a1): merge cpu-vs-instructions: refresh-seed's timing rounds run the seed and the new compiler both on wap's source as sources, so both do the same work; before, the seed compiled plain compiler.wap and a faster compiler read as about 10% slower (scripts/refresh-seed.sh; wap-supervisor: approved)",
   "state": "CLOSED",
   "assignees": {
