   "title": "C's free, malloc and close are declared in four…",
   "body": "Original title: C's free, malloc and close are declared in four library files instead of one\n\nAdded by wap-native-no-layout-any with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319807954\n\nland: free-malloc 5d3fa17f (contains warp-temp-race). Left: lib/host/native_host/gpu.wap keeps fopen/fclose/set_field_bytes; its set_field_bytes(data: list<int32>) differs from c.wap's (data: bytes), so a program using both gpu and c is refused 'declares c.set_field_bytes with other types'; one of them needs the other's type.\n\nFixed in [d9cb1732](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/d9cb1732bdf0ba0438fad8b684a9580be21c7e1a): merge test-killed: run.sh ends every test's output with \"— ran to its end\" once judged, and an output without it is \"✗ <test> ran to its end\", so a test killed with its runner is red with its baseline reds kept; with free-malloc, lib/c.wap declares free, malloc, close, fopen, fclose, getenv, setenv, getcwd, strdup, strndup, calloc and field_i32 once for the libraries that use c, and warp-temp-race, a temporary file or folder made at once by mkstemps or mkdtemp, its name unique, so runs at the same moment never share one (library, test and scripts; no compiler change)",
