   "__typename": "Issue",
   "id": "I_kwDOV1nZQs8AAAABi5_MwA",
   "title": "Finding a node's definer scans its facts on every…",
   "body": "Original title: Finding a node's definer scans its facts on every call\n\nSpeed (standing OK speed if ≥1%, 0 net lines, no form). Profile 2026-11-26 on interned-names 73c53bda: fact_of 7.9% self; its main callers definer_id 11.5%, same_definer 8.7%, signature_key 7.5% of fact_of's samples. Variants: fewer facts per node, or a definer read once per node. Measure on main (with 7ab80094). wap-supervisor 2026-11-27.\n\nAdded by wap-primitive-lookup-tables with `todo add`.\n\nBoard card: https://github.com/users/pannous/projects/10?pane=issue&itemId=319832410\n\nbranch: definer-scan (2026-11-27)\n\nbranch definer-scan bd80fda9 (merge 37cc08a2): is_lambda_key one lookup (lambdas a map by key), -5.0% instructions (220.0 → 209.1 G), 0 net lines; census and areas green; review asked of wap-supervisor\n\nland: definer-scan-2 892100a6 (-5.0%, 0 net; test_self ceiling 162676647632; fixed point kept; census ✓). Old branch definer-scan 37cc08a2 superseded.\n\nFixed in [fa267da0](https://github.com/pannous/wap/commit/fa267da0ffd6deb0ea1e35d1ed886d7267214648): merge definer-scan-2: whether a function value's key is a lambda's is one lookup in TypingState.lambdas, now a map by key, so the self-compile retires about 5% fewer instructions with 0 net lines; scripts/wap-census.warp reads that map; test_self's SELF_COMPILE_INSTRUCTIONS falls to its measured 162676647632 (from 172517638896) (standing OK speed; wap-supervisor: sound at bd80fda9)",
